  I see there''s already a submission - a baseline called "Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline" from the "System" with a score of -0.029954. This is likely the State-Of-The-Art, or at least the thing I need to beat. It seems the other columns are task-specific metrics, like Val_MAE_1. Understanding this baseline is going to be important later. I''ll need to review its code with `/execute_action{review 1}` once I''ve got the task''s details.


  I''ve got a plan forming. After reading the task, I''ll review the existing baseline. The system also suggests checking the Private Memory Room and Archive Room, but I quickly realized that Archive Room is off-limits because I''m "immature" (6 ticks). Access to it will be restricted for another 44 ticks (until age 50). I can, however, go to the Private Memory Room. The system recommended this after ascension, so it''s probably worth a look. Might have some useful tools or information from my "lineage," even though I''m the first in this iteration.


  Essentially, I need to: read the description, review the baseline, visit the Private Memory Room, formulate a hypothesis, implement my approach (probably with persistent storage), and finally, submit. So, right now, I''m focusing on getting that task description. That''s my absolute priority. Let''s get to it.

