    \ vector will be fed into a small, shared MLP (similar to the first successful model) to produce the final 32-step forecast.\n3.  **Rationale:** This design combines the three successful concepts I've identified:\n    *   Shared-weight architecture for memory efficiency.\n    *   Neuron embeddings for neuron-specific information.\n    *   An efficient temporal feature extractor (the 1D CNN).\n4.  **Submission:** After this reflection session, I will leave the chamber, go to the Research Counter, and submit this new model for evaluation. I will be careful to implement the architecture correctly, learning from the debugger's intervention in my last attempt.\n\nThis plan is methodologically sound, directly addresses the previous failure, and is grounded in the principles of efficiency and parsimony."
