tick: 16
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have analyzed the failure of the GRU model and formulated a clear, methodologically sound plan for my next experiment using a 1D CNN. It is now time to put this plan into action.\n\nI will leave the Reflection Chamber, return to the Research Counter, and submit the new architecture.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"1D CNN with Neuron Embeddings for Efficient Temporal Feature Extraction\"\ntags: \"cnn, cnn-1d, embedding, temporal-modeling, feature-extraction\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission proposes a 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to address the computational inefficiency of the previous GRU model (ID: 9). The CNN acts as a fast, parallelizable feature extractor across the 4-step input sequence. It is combined with neuron-specific embeddings to capture both temporal dynamics and unique neuron characteristics. This approach aims to provide the benefits of temporal modeling while remaining within\
    \ the station's computational time limits, hypothesizing an improvement over purely feed-forward architectures.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'cnn_features': 32,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 2,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class CnnEmbeddingModel(nn.Module):\n      embedding_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, _, _ = x.shape\n\n          # Neuron embedding layer\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim, name=\"\
    neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n\n          # Reshape input and combine with embeddings\n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) # (batch, num_neurons, 4)\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, axis=-1) # (batch, num_neurons, 4, 1)\n\n          # Broadcast embeddings to match sequence length\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.expand_dims(broadcasted_embeddings, axis=2)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.broadcast_to(broadcasted_embeddings_seq, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, self.embedding_dim))\n\n          # Concatenate features: (batch, num_neurons, 4, 1 + embedding_dim)\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, broadcasted_embeddings_seq], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Reshape for CNN processing: (batch * num_neurons, 4, 1 + embedding_dim)\n          cnn_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size\
    \ * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n\n          # 1D CNN for temporal feature extraction\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(cnn_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          \n          # Flatten the output of the CNN\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n\n          # MLP head for prediction\n          y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(y)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          \n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n\n          # Reshape back to the final format: (batch, 32, num_neurons)\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          \n          return output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = CnnEmbeddingModel(\n\
    \              embedding_dim=hparams.get('embedding_dim', 8),\n              cnn_features=hparams.get('cnn_features', 32),\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 2),\n              mlp_hidden_size=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size', 64),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1)\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
