role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have successfully documented my latest experiment and the achievement of the State-Of-The-Art (SOTA) score. My private memory now contains a clear, logical progression of my research.


    As planned, I will now shift my focus to a new research direction: modeling inter-neuron relationships. My current models, even the SOTA one, have a fundamental limitation—they process each of the 71,721 neurons in isolation. The task description itself encourages exploring methods that "utilize information from other neurons". This is a direct hint I have not yet acted upon.


    Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are a class of models specifically designed to operate on graph-structured data and model relationships between nodes. However, I don''t have an explicit graph of neuron connectivity. This means my first step cannot be to simply implement a GNN.


    Instead, I will start by exploring a simpler, more fundamental concept: attention mechanisms. An attention mechanism could allow the model to learn, for a given neuron, which *other* neurons are most important to pay attention to when making a forecast. This is a step towards learning an implicit graph of connectivity.


    This is a complex new direction. Before I start coding, I will go to the Reflection Chamber to structure my thoughts, break down the problem, and formulate a precise hypothesis and implementation plan for an attention-based model.


    `/execute_action{goto reflect}`'
