tick: 21
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection on incorporating inter-neuron relationships is complete. I have a solid plan for a dual-branch architecture that introduces a global context vector. It is now time to execute this plan.\n\nI will leave the Reflection Chamber, go to the Research Counter, and submit my new model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-Branch CNN with Global Context Vector for Inter-Neuron Modeling\"\ntags: \"cnn, cnn-1d, embedding, global-context, attention, inter-neuron\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a novel dual-branch architecture to model inter-neuron dependencies in a computationally tractable way. One branch computes per-neuron temporal features using a 1D CNN, similar to the previous SOTA model. A second, parallel branch computes a global context vector by aggregating the activity of all neurons. This context vector is then fused with the per-neuron features before the final forecast. This approach hypothesizes that\
    \ conditioning individual neuron predictions on the overall brain state will lead to a more accurate and context-aware model.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'cnn_features': 32,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 2,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'context_vector_dim': 16,\n          'global_encoder_hidden_dim': 32\n      }\n\n  class DualBranchModel(nn.Module):\n      embedding_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      context_vector_dim: int\n      global_encoder_hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, _, _ = x.shape\n\n          # ---\
    \ Branch 1: Per-Neuron Feature Extractor ---\n          # (This is similar to the previous SOTA model)\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim, name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          \n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, axis=-1)\n          \n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.expand_dims(broadcasted_embeddings, axis=2)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.broadcast_to(broadcasted_embeddings_seq, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, self.embedding_dim))\n          \n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, broadcasted_embeddings_seq], axis=-1)\n          cnn_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n\
    \          \n          local_features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(cnn_input)\n          local_features = nn.relu(local_features)\n          local_features = local_features.reshape((local_features.shape[0], -1))\n\n          # --- Branch 2: Global Context Encoder ---\n          # Aggregate across all neurons: (batch, 4, 71721) -> (batch, 4)\n          global_activity_summary = jnp.mean(x, axis=2)\n          \n          # Encode the summary into a context vector\n          global_context = nn.Dense(self.global_encoder_hidden_dim, name=\"global_encoder_1\")(global_activity_summary)\n          global_context = nn.relu(global_context)\n          global_context = nn.Dense(self.context_vector_dim, name=\"global_encoder_2\")(global_context)\n          global_context = global_context.reshape((batch_size, -1)) # Flatten context features\n\n          # --- Fusion and Prediction Head ---\n          # Broadcast global context to match per-neuron features\n\
    \          # From (batch, context_dim) to (batch * num_neurons, context_dim)\n          expanded_context = jnp.repeat(global_context, NUM_NEURONS, axis=0)\n          \n          # Concatenate local and global features\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([local_features, expanded_context], axis=-1)\n\n          # Final MLP prediction head\n          y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(fused_features)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          \n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n\n          # Reshape to final format\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          \n          return output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DualBranchModel(\n              embedding_dim=hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n\
    \              cnn_features=hparams.get('cnn_features'),\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size'),\n              mlp_hidden_size=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size'),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n              context_vector_dim=hparams.get('context_vector_dim'),\n              global_encoder_hidden_dim=hparams.get('global_encoder_hidden_dim')\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
