tick: 24
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully documented my breakthrough. My research trajectory is clear and well-recorded. The success of the global context vector derived from a simple mean aggregation validates the core concept, but it is unlikely to be the optimal way to summarize the state of 71,721 neurons. A simple average treats every neuron as equally important, which is biologically implausible. Some neurons are likely more informative than others for determining the global brain state.\n\n**Hypothesis:** A more sophisticated aggregation mechanism that can learn to weigh the importance of different neurons when creating the global context vector will produce a more informative summary and lead to better forecasting performance than a simple, unweighted mean.\n\n**Plan:**\n\nThe most direct way to implement a learned weighting is with an attention mechanism. However, as established, self-attention over all neurons is too expensive. A full attention mechanism computes Query, Key, and Value matrices\
    \ of size (N, d). The core bottleneck is the QK^T multiplication, which is (N, d) x (d, N) -> (N, N).\n\nI can create a much cheaper, simplified attention mechanism. Instead of N queries, I can use a *single*, learnable global query vector. This query will attend to the \"keys\" derived from all 71,721 neurons to produce attention weights. This reduces the complexity from O(N^2) to O(N).\n\n**Implementation:**\n\n1.  Instead of `jnp.mean(x, axis=2)` to get the global summary, I will implement a new module.\n2.  This module will have a single, learnable query vector `q` of size `(d_k)`.\n3.  For each neuron's 4-step input, I'll project it into a `key` vector `k_i` (also size `d_k`).\n4.  The attention score for each neuron will be `score_i = dot(q, k_i)`.\n5.  These scores will be passed through a softmax to get attention weights `w_i`.\n6.  The final context vector will be the weighted sum of all neuron `value` representations: `context = sum(w_i * v_i)`. The `value` vector `v_i` can\
    \ be derived from another projection of the input.\n\nThis \"global query attention\" is a principled way to let the model learn which neurons are most important for summarizing the brain state. I will now go to the research counter and submit this new model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Global Query Attention for Learned Context Vector\"\ntags: \"attention, global-context, learned-aggregation, inter-neuron\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission improves upon the dual-branch model (ID 27) by replacing the simple mean aggregation with a \"global query attention\" mechanism. Instead of an unweighted average, this model uses a single, learnable global query vector to attend to all neurons, computing a weighted average based on learned importance. This hypothesizes that a more sophisticated, learned aggregation for the global context vector will capture a more informative brain state summary, leading to superior forecasting performance.\n\
    content: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'cnn_features': 32,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 2,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'attention_key_dim': 16,\n          'global_encoder_hidden_dim': 32\n      }\n\n  class GlobalAttention(nn.Module):\n      key_dim: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, num_neurons)\n          \n          # Project neuron activities into key and value representations\n          # We process the mean activity over the 4 timesteps for simplicity\n          neuron_summary = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, num_neurons)\n          \n          keys = nn.Dense(features=self.key_dim, name=\"attention_keys\"\
    )(neuron_summary) # (batch, num_neurons, key_dim)\n          values = nn.Dense(features=self.key_dim, name=\"attention_values\")(neuron_summary) # (batch, num_neurons, key_dim)\n          \n          # Learnable global query vector\n          query = self.param('global_query', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.key_dim,))\n          \n          # Compute attention scores\n          # dot product between global query and each neuron's key\n          # (batch, num_neurons, key_dim) * (key_dim,) -> (batch, num_neurons)\n          scores = jnp.einsum('bnd,d->bn', keys, query)\n          \n          # Softmax to get attention weights\n          weights = nn.softmax(scores, axis=-1) # (batch, num_neurons)\n          \n          # Weighted sum of values to get context vector\n          # (batch, 1, num_neurons) @ (batch, num_neurons, key_dim) -> (batch, 1, key_dim)\n          context = jnp.einsum('bn,bnd->bd', weights, values)\n          \n          return context\n\n\n  class AttentionContextModel(nn.Module):\n\
    \      embedding_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      attention_key_dim: int\n      global_encoder_hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, _, _ = x.shape\n\n          # Branch 1: Per-Neuron Feature Extractor (same as before)\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim, name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, axis=-1)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.expand_dims(broadcasted_embeddings, axis=2)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.broadcast_to(broadcasted_embeddings_seq, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON,\
    \ self.embedding_dim))\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, broadcasted_embeddings_seq], axis=-1)\n          cnn_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n          local_features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(cnn_input)\n          local_features = nn.relu(local_features)\n          local_features = local_features.reshape((local_features.shape[0], -1))\n\n          # Branch 2: Global Context via Attention\n          global_context = GlobalAttention(key_dim=self.attention_key_dim, name=\"global_attention\")(x)\n          # Pass through a small MLP encoder\n          global_context = nn.Dense(self.global_encoder_hidden_dim, name=\"global_encoder_1\")(global_context)\n          global_context = nn.relu(global_context)\n\n          # Fusion and Prediction Head\n          expanded_context = jnp.repeat(global_context, NUM_NEURONS, axis=0)\n          fused_features\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([local_features, expanded_context], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(fused_features)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = AttentionContextModel(**hparams)\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n\
    \          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams={\n          'embedding_dim': hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n          'cnn_features': hparams.get('cnn_features'),\n          'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size'),\n          'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size'),\n          'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n          'attention_key_dim': hparams.get('attention_key_dim'),\n          'global_encoder_hidden_dim': hparams.get('global_encoder_hidden_dim')\n      })\n```"
