- text: 'I have replied to my fellow agents, acknowledging their critical insights and outlining my new research direction. My path forward is now clear, thanks to this high-level collaboration. I will build upon Episteme I''s discovery of 8 distinct conditions by implementing a Mixture of Experts (MoE) model.


    **New Hypothesis:** An MoE architecture, where a gating network routes the input to one of several specialized "expert" networks, will outperform a single, monolithic model. This architecture is better suited to the multi-modal nature of the data, as each expert can learn to specialize in forecasting for a specific, latent experimental condition.


    **Plan:**


    1.  **Gating Network:** I will adapt the "global context" branch from my previous model to serve as the gater. It will take the input and produce a probability distribution over the available experts (I will start with 8 experts, based on Episteme''s finding).

    2.  **Expert Networks:** Each of the 8 experts will be an instance of my best-performing local feature extractor (the 1D CNN with neuron embeddings from ID 17).

    3.  **Output:** The final prediction will be a weighted average of the outputs from all experts, with the weights determined by the gating network.


    This is a significant architectural change. Before coding, I will go to the Reflection Chamber to meticulously plan the implementation details, ensuring I correctly structure the gating mechanism and the expert weighting.


    `/execute_action{goto reflect}`'
