role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 31\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 102,247 / 300,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 31 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Mixture\
    \ of Experts CNN for Multi-Condition Forecasting' (ID: 42) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.028589299159242063\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0265\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0299\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0318\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 42\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission code after two iterations. The code now runs without crashing and has been executing for over 300 seconds successfully.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 42) had two critical bugs in the Mixture of Experts (MoE) implementation using Flax's `nn.vmap`:\n\n### Bug 1: Incorrect RNG Key Structure\n**Location**: `ModelWrapper.init()` method (line 67-68 in original)\n\n**Problem**: The code was creating an array of RNG keys and passing it to `model.init()`:\n```python\nexpert_rngs = random.split(rng_params, self.hparams.get('num_experts'))\n\
    return self.model.init({'params': expert_rngs, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n```\n\n**Error**: `ValueError: First argument passed to an init function should be a jax.PRNGKey or a dictionary mapping strings to jax.PRNGKey.`\n\n**Explanation**: When using `nn.vmap` with `split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True}`, Flax automatically handles RNG splitting internally. The init function expects a single PRNGKey for each RNG stream, not an array.\n\n### Bug 2: Missing axis_size Parameter\n**Location**: `MoEModel.__call__()` method (line 91-96 in original)\n\n**Problem**: The `nn.vmap` call was missing the `axis_size` parameter:\n```python\nexperts = nn.vmap(\n    Expert,\n    in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n    variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n    split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True}\n)(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n```\n\n**Error**: `ValueError: axis_size should be specified manually.`\n\n**Explanation**: When using `nn.vmap` without\
    \ input data that has a batch dimension to infer from, the `axis_size` parameter must be explicitly specified to tell Flax how many copies of the module to create (in this case, 8 experts).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix for Bug 1 (submission_v2.py):\nChanged the RNG key handling to pass single keys instead of arrays:\n```python\ndef init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n    # Fixed: Pass a single rng_key, not an array. Flax handles RNG splitting internally\n    # when using nn.vmap with split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True}\n    rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n    return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n```\n\n### Fix for Bug 2 (submission_v3.py):\nAdded the `axis_size` parameter to the `nn.vmap` call:\n```python\nexperts = nn.vmap(\n    Expert,\n    in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n    variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n    split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n    axis_size=self.num_experts\
    \  # Fixed: Added axis_size parameter\n)(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v3.py) was automatically executed by the evaluation system and ran successfully for over 300 seconds without any crashes, confirming that both bugs were properly resolved. The code is still running (likely performing model initialization and training), which is expected behavior for this type of neural network task.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The MoE architecture uses 8 experts with CNN-based architectures\n- Each expert has its own parameters and batch statistics\n- The gating network determines how to weight the expert outputs\n- The implementation correctly uses Flax's `nn.vmap` for parallel expert execution\n- All architectural choices in the original submission were sound; only the RNG handling and axis_size specification needed correction\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage\
    \ files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nINPUT_HORIZON = 4\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'embedding_dim': 8,\n        'cnn_features': 32,\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 2,\n        'mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'num_experts': 8,\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n    }\n\nclass Expert(nn.Module):\n    embedding_dim: int\n    cnn_features: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n\n        # This is the architecture from ID 17/27's local branch\n        neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n        embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim,\
    \ name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n        broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n\n        x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, axis=-1)\n\n        broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.expand_dims(broadcasted_embeddings, axis=2)\n        broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.broadcast_to(broadcasted_embeddings_seq, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, self.embedding_dim))\n\n        combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, broadcasted_embeddings_seq], axis=-1)\n        cnn_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(cnn_input)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n\n        y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(y)\n        y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n        y =\
    \ nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n\n        output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n\n        output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n        output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n        return output\n\nclass GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, num_neurons)\n        # Use global average pooling as input to the gater\n        gater_input = jnp.mean(x, axis=2) # (batch, seq_len)\n        gater_input = gater_input.reshape((gater_input.shape[0], -1)) # Flatten\n\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(gater_input)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\nclass MoEModel(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    expert_params: dict\n    gating_params: dict\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n\n        # Define the experts using vmap for parallel execution\n        # Note: Flax's nn.vmap is a powerful way to create parallel experts\n        # Fixed: Added axis_size parameter to specify number of experts\n        experts = nn.vmap(\n            Expert,\n            in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n            variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n            split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n            axis_size=self.num_experts\n        )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n\n        # Get gating weights\n        gating_network = GatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n        gating_weights = gating_network(x) # (batch, num_experts)\n\n        # Get outputs from all experts\n        # experts(x) will return shape (batch, num_experts, 32, 71721)\n        expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n\n        # Weight the outputs\n        # Reshape weights for broadcasting:\
    \ (batch, num_experts, 1, 1)\n        gating_weights = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n\n        # Weighted sum\n        weighted_outputs = expert_outputs * gating_weights\n        final_output = jnp.sum(weighted_outputs, axis=1)\n\n        return final_output\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        expert_params = {\n            'embedding_dim': hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n            'cnn_features': hparams.get('cnn_features'),\n            'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size'),\n            'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size'),\n            'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n        }\n        gating_params = {\n            'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n            'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n        }\n        self.model = MoEModel(\n            num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'),\n            expert_params=expert_params,\n\
    \            gating_params=gating_params\n        )\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # Fixed: Pass a single rng_key, not an array. Flax handles RNG splitting internally\n        # when using nn.vmap with split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True}\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable:\n            return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n\
    === SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.054101\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 150112 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
