tick: 32
role: model
parts:
- text: "My protocol is now complete. I have analyzed the results, formulated a new hypothesis, and documented my findings. The next step is to execute the experiment.\n\nMy hypothesis is that a Mixture of Experts model with simpler MLP-based experts will outperform the more complex CNN-based MoE model because it can train for more epochs within the time limit. This is a direct test of the trade-off between architectural complexity and training convergence. The MLP expert will be based on my successful submission ID 2.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit this new, more computationally efficient MoE architecture.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Computationally Efficient MoE with MLP Experts\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, mlp, computational-efficiency\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests the hypothesis that a computationally simpler Mixture of Experts (MoE) model can outperform a more complex one by training for more\
    \ epochs. It replaces the CNN-based experts from the SOTA model (ID 42) with simpler, faster MLP-based experts (based on ID 2). The goal is to determine if the benefits of longer convergence time outweigh the reduced architectural complexity of each expert, potentially leading to a better overall score.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_experts': 8,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n      }\n\n  class MlpExpert(nn.Module):\n      embedding_dim: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Simplified MLP Expert based\
    \ on ID 2\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim, name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          \n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_transposed, broadcasted_embeddings], axis=-1)\n          \n          mlp_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON + self.embedding_dim))\n\n          y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(mlp_input)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          \n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n          \n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output,\
    \ (0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gater_input = jnp.mean(x, axis=2)\n          gater_input = gater_input.reshape((gater_input.shape[0], -1))\n          \n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEModel(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              MlpExpert,\n              in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n              axis_size=self.num_experts\n          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\"\
    )\n          \n          gating_network = GatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          \n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_weights = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n          \n          weighted_outputs = expert_outputs * gating_weights\n          final_output = jnp.sum(weighted_outputs, axis=1)\n          \n          return final_output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          expert_params = {\n              'embedding_dim': hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n              'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size'),\n              'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n          }\n          gating_params = {\n              'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n              'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n          }\n          self.model = MoEModel(\n\
    \              num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'),\n              expert_params=expert_params,\n              gating_params=gating_params\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
