tick: 38
role: model
parts:
- text: "My protocol has been followed. The analysis of my breakthrough result (ID 59) and its documentation are complete. The next step is to formulate a new hypothesis based on the findings.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\n\nThe analysis of ID 59 revealed two key points: the spatial gating network is extremely effective, but the overall MoE model is still computationally expensive and times out before full convergence. The number of experts (8) was based on Episteme I's initial analysis, but this may not be the optimal number for this specific architecture. It's possible that a smaller number of experts could capture the necessary dynamics while being significantly faster to train, allowing for deeper convergence.\n\nTherefore, I hypothesize that an MoE model with fewer experts (e.g., 4) will achieve a superior score to the 8-expert model. The performance gain from allowing the model to train for more epochs will outweigh the potential loss of specialization from having fewer experts.\n\n**3.\
    \ Experiment:**\n\nI will now design the experiment to test this. This is a simple but critical ablation study. I will take my SOTA model from ID 59 and change only one hyperparameter: `num_experts` from 8 to 4. All other aspects of the architecture will remain identical.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation Study: MoE-MLP with 4 Experts for Deeper Convergence\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, ablation-study, computational-efficiency, convergence\"\nabstract: |\n  This is an ablation study on the SOTA MoE-MLP model (ID 59). It tests the hypothesis that a version with fewer experts (4 instead of 8) can achieve a better score by training for more epochs within the time limit. The experiment aims to determine if the performance gains from deeper convergence outweigh the reduced specialization capacity of having fewer experts, seeking a better balance between\
    \ model complexity and training efficiency.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Same as ID 59, but with num_experts changed from 8 to 4\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n          'gating_pool_window': 256,\n      }\n\n  class MlpExpert(nn.Module):\n      embedding_dim: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim,\
    \ name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_transposed, broadcasted_embeddings], axis=-1)\n          mlp_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON + self.embedding_dim))\n          y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(mlp_input)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n   \
    \   pool_window: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEModel(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              MlpExpert, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n              axis_size=self.num_experts\n\
    \          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n          \n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          \n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n          \n          final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n          return final_output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          expert_params = {\n              'embedding_dim': hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n              'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size'),\n              'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n          }\n          gating_params = {\n              'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n              'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n              'cnn_features':\
    \ hparams.get('gating_cnn_features'),\n              'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'pool_window': hparams.get('gating_pool_window'),\n          }\n          self.model = MoEModel(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
