tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "My protocol is complete for the last cycle. I have documented the falsified hypothesis regarding the learning rate. Now, I will begin a new cycle.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\n\nMy analysis has led me to a new frontier. The success of the spatial CNN in my *gating network* was a massive breakthrough. It proved that local spatial relationships between neurons are highly predictive. However, my *expert networks* are still the simple MLP architecture, which processes each neuron in complete isolation. They are spatially blind.\n\nTherefore, I hypothesize that replacing the simple MLP experts in my SOTA MoE model with more sophisticated experts that can also process local spatial information will lead to a new S-O-T-A score. Each expert, now spatially aware, will be able to make a more informed forecast for its specialized condition.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\n\nI will design an experiment to test this hypothesis directly. The expert architecture will be a hybrid. It will first process the 4-step\
    \ temporal sequence for each neuron (similar to my 1D CNN in ID 17), and *then* it will use a 1D convolution across the neuron dimension to capture local spatial interactions. This creates a spatio-temporal expert.\n\nBecause this new expert is more complex, I will need to be mindful of computational cost. I will start by combining this new expert architecture with my best gating network (from ID 65) and a small number of experts (4).\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to submit this new, more powerful MoE architecture.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE with Spatio-Temporal Experts\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, cnn, spatial-features, temporal-features, spatio-temporal\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission proposes a new expert architecture for the SOTA MoE framework. The spatially-blind MLP experts are replaced with more powerful spatio-temporal experts. Each new expert uses a 1D CNN across the time dimension for temporal\
    \ feature extraction, followed by another 1D CNN across the neuron dimension for spatial feature extraction. This tests the hypothesis that incorporating spatial processing within the experts themselves, in addition to the gating network, will lead to a significant performance breakthrough.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n          'gating_pool_window': 256,\n          'expert_temporal_cnn_features': 16,\n          'expert_temporal_cnn_kernel_size': 2,\n          'expert_spatial_cnn_features': 4,\n          'expert_spatial_cnn_kernel_size': 32,\n          'expert_mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n      }\n\n\
    \  class SpatioTemporalExpert(nn.Module):\n      embedding_dim: int\n      temporal_cnn_features: int\n      temporal_cnn_kernel_size: int\n      spatial_cnn_features: int\n      spatial_cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n\n          # --- Temporal Feature Extraction (per neuron) ---\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, -1)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.expand_dims(broadcasted_embeddings, 2)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.broadcast_to(broadcasted_embeddings_seq, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON,\
    \ self.embedding_dim))\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, broadcasted_embeddings_seq], axis=-1)\n          cnn_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n          temporal_features = nn.Conv(features=self.temporal_cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.temporal_cnn_kernel_size,))(cnn_input)\n          temporal_features = nn.relu(temporal_features)\n          temporal_features = temporal_features.reshape((batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, -1))\n\n          # --- Spatial Feature Extraction (across neurons) ---\n          spatial_features = nn.Conv(features=self.spatial_cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.spatial_cnn_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(temporal_features)\n          spatial_features = nn.relu(spatial_features)\n\n          # --- Fusion and Prediction ---\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([temporal_features, spatial_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_flat = fused.reshape((batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, -1))\n      \
    \    \n          y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(fused_flat)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n          \n          output = output.reshape((batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      pool_window: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits,\
    \ axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEModel(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              SpatioTemporalExpert, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True}\n          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n          \n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          \n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n          \n          final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n          return final_output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          expert_params\
    \ = {\n              'embedding_dim': hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n              'temporal_cnn_features': hparams.get('expert_temporal_cnn_features'),\n              'temporal_cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('expert_temporal_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'spatial_cnn_features': hparams.get('expert_spatial_cnn_features'),\n              'spatial_cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('expert_spatial_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('expert_mlp_hidden_size'),\n          }\n          gating_params = {\n              'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n              'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n              'cnn_features': hparams.get('gating_cnn_features'),\n              'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'pool_window': hparams.get('gating_pool_window'),\n          }\n          self.model = MoEModel(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n\
    \          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          # Simplified RNG for non-dropout model\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
