tick: 46
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 46\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 170,711 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 46 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MoE with\
    \ Spatio-Temporal Experts' (ID: 78) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02780959970070653\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0263\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0290\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0307\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 78\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been successfully fixed and is now running without errors. The original submission crashed during initialization due to a missing required parameter in the Flax `nn.vmap` function call.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with the error:\n```\nValueError: axis_size should be specified manually.\n```\n\nThis occurred in the `MoEModel.__call__` method at line 102 (submission.py:102) when calling:\n```python\nexpert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n```\n\nThe issue was in the `nn.vmap` initialization (lines 49-52 of original submission):\n```python\nexperts = nn.vmap(\n   \
    \ SpatioTemporalExpert, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n    variable_axes={'params': 0},\n    split_rngs={'params': True}\n)(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n```\n\nThe `nn.vmap` function requires an `axis_size` parameter to know how many expert instances to create along the vectorized axis. Without this parameter, JAX cannot determine the size of the vectorized dimension and raises a ValueError.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing `axis_size` parameter to the `nn.vmap` call:\n\n**Location**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`, line 97 (in the `MoEModel.__call__` method)\n\n**Change**:\n```python\nexperts = nn.vmap(\n    SpatioTemporalExpert,\n    in_axes=None,\n    out_axes=1,\n    variable_axes={'params': 0},\n    split_rngs={'params': True},\n    axis_size=self.num_experts  # FIX: Added axis_size parameter\n)(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n```\n\nThe `axis_size=self.num_experts` parameter tells `nn.vmap` to create exactly `num_experts` (4 in this case) instances of the `SpatioTemporalExpert`\
    \ module, each with its own set of parameters.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitor script, which confirmed:\n- The code initializes successfully without errors\n- The network creation works correctly\n- The code has been running for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n\n## Conclusion\nThis was a simple but critical bug fix. The agent's MoE architecture is sound, but the Flax vectorization API requires explicit specification of the vectorized dimension size. With this single-line fix, the submission now runs correctly and the model can be properly initialized and trained.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nINPUT_HORIZON = 4\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'embedding_dim': 8,\n        'num_experts': 4,\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n        'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n        'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n        'gating_pool_window': 256,\n        'expert_temporal_cnn_features': 16,\n        'expert_temporal_cnn_kernel_size': 2,\n        'expert_spatial_cnn_features': 4,\n        'expert_spatial_cnn_kernel_size': 32,\n        'expert_mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n    }\n\nclass SpatioTemporalExpert(nn.Module):\n    embedding_dim: int\n    temporal_cnn_features: int\n    temporal_cnn_kernel_size: int\n    spatial_cnn_features: int\n    spatial_cnn_kernel_size: int\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n\n        # --- Temporal Feature Extraction (per neuron) ---\n        neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n        embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n\
    \        broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n        x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, -1)\n        broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.expand_dims(broadcasted_embeddings, 2)\n        broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.broadcast_to(broadcasted_embeddings_seq, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, self.embedding_dim))\n        combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, broadcasted_embeddings_seq], axis=-1)\n        cnn_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n        temporal_features = nn.Conv(features=self.temporal_cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.temporal_cnn_kernel_size,))(cnn_input)\n        temporal_features = nn.relu(temporal_features)\n        temporal_features = temporal_features.reshape((batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, -1))\n\n        # --- Spatial Feature Extraction (across neurons) ---\n     \
    \   spatial_features = nn.Conv(features=self.spatial_cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.spatial_cnn_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(temporal_features)\n        spatial_features = nn.relu(spatial_features)\n\n        # --- Fusion and Prediction ---\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([temporal_features, spatial_features], axis=-1)\n        fused_flat = fused.reshape((batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, -1))\n\n        y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(fused_flat)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n\n        output = output.reshape((batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n        output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n        return output\n\nclass CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    cnn_features: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    pool_window: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n\
    \        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n        y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\nclass MoEModel(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    expert_params: dict\n    gating_params: dict\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        experts = nn.vmap(\n            SpatioTemporalExpert,\n            in_axes=None,\n            out_axes=1,\n            variable_axes={'params': 0},\n            split_rngs={'params': True},\n            axis_size=self.num_experts  # FIX: Added axis_size parameter\n        )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n\n        gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n        gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n\n        expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n\
    \n        gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n\n        final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n        return final_output\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        expert_params = {\n            'embedding_dim': hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n            'temporal_cnn_features': hparams.get('expert_temporal_cnn_features'),\n            'temporal_cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('expert_temporal_cnn_kernel_size'),\n            'spatial_cnn_features': hparams.get('expert_spatial_cnn_features'),\n            'spatial_cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('expert_spatial_cnn_kernel_size'),\n            'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('expert_mlp_hidden_size'),\n        }\n        gating_params = {\n            'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n            'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n            'cnn_features': hparams.get('gating_cnn_features'),\n\
    \            'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size'),\n            'pool_window': hparams.get('gating_pool_window'),\n        }\n        self.model = MoEModel(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # Simplified RNG for non-dropout model\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.058839\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 178278 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel\
