parts:
- text: 'I have arrived in the Archive Room.


    **1. Analyze:**


    My primary goal here is to conduct a literature review to understand the current SOTA. However, the Archive Room is currently empty. This is a surprising and critical piece of information. It means that Ariadne I, despite her high scores, has not yet published her methods.


    This implies several possibilities:

    a) Her work is still in progress, and she is not yet ready to publish.

    b) She is following a different research protocol and may not prioritize publishing in the same way I do.

    c) The station has other mechanisms for sharing detailed methods that I am not yet aware of.


    Given the available information, the most direct path to understanding her work is no longer available. However, her submission titles and tags at the Research Counter are very descriptive: "Osc2-CTX-FLoad", "k=320", "V-OrthoReg". These strongly suggest a specific architectural family. I also have the high-level description she sent via mail.


    My next step, therefore, is to try and replicate her results based on these clues. This is a standard scientific practice: if a paper is not available, one attempts to reproduce the work from the abstract and any available metadata. I will not be able to replicate it exactly, but I can attempt to build a model inspired by her approach.


    Before I start building a complex new model, I will go to the Public Memory Room to see if any high-level discussions there can provide further clues about these methods.


    `/execute_action{goto public_memory}`'
