tick: 54
role: model
parts:
- text: "My protocol cycle is complete. The catastrophic failure of my replication attempt has been analyzed and documented. It is a clear directive to return to my own successful line of research and improve it, rather than blindly chase a poorly understood SOTA.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\nMy best model is ID 65: a 4-expert MoE with a spatial CNN gater and simple MLP experts. Its strength is the MoE framework and the smart gater. Its weakness is the simplicity of the experts, which treat the 4-step input sequence crudely by simply concatenating embeddings. My attempt to add a temporal CNN to the experts in ID 17 was a good idea, but my attempt to add *both* a temporal and a spatial CNN in ID 78 was too computationally expensive.\n\nThis suggests there is a middle ground. The MLP experts in ID 65 are fast. The CNN experts from ID 17 were also reasonably fast. The failure of ID 42 (MoE-CNN) was because it used 8 complex experts.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\nAriadne I's success is rooted in sophisticated\
    \ temporal modeling. My most powerful architectural component is the MoE framework with a spatial gater. I can combine these strengths.\n\nI hypothesize that an MoE model with 4 experts, where each expert is the computationally efficient *temporal 1D CNN* model from my experiment ID 17, will outperform the current SOTA which uses simpler MLP experts. The combination of the powerful spatial gater, the optimal number of experts (4), and more powerful (but still efficient) temporal experts will unlock a new level of performance.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\nI will construct this model. It will be a hybrid of my two most successful independent ideas: the MoE framework from ID 65 and the temporal CNN expert architecture from ID 17.\n\nI will now go to the research counter to submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE with 4 Temporal CNN Experts\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, cnn, temporal-features, spatial-features\"\nabstract:\
    \ |\n  This submission returns to the successful MoE framework and aims to improve it by enhancing the experts. It combines the SOTA 4-expert architecture (ID 65) with the efficient temporal 1D CNN expert design from experiment ID 17. The hypothesis is that replacing the simple MLP experts with more powerful, yet still computationally efficient, temporal CNN experts will provide a significant performance boost, creating a new SOTA model that leverages both spatial gating and expert-level temporal processing.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Combining best elements: 4 experts, spatial gater, and temporal CNN experts\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size':\
    \ 128,\n          'gating_pool_window': 256,\n          'expert_cnn_features': 32,\n          'expert_cnn_kernel_size': 2,\n          'expert_mlp_hidden_size': 64,\n          'expert_dropout_rate': 0.1,\n      }\n\n  class CnnExpert(nn.Module):\n      embedding_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # This is the temporal CNN expert from ID 17\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim, name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, axis=-1)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.expand_dims(broadcasted_embeddings,\
    \ axis=2)\n          broadcasted_embeddings_seq = jnp.broadcast_to(broadcasted_embeddings_seq, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, self.embedding_dim))\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, broadcasted_embeddings_seq], axis=-1)\n          cnn_input = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (batch_size * NUM_NEURONS, INPUT_HORIZON, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(cnn_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n          y = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(y)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n\
    \      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      pool_window: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEModel(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              CnnExpert, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats':\
    \ 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n              axis_size=self.num_experts\n          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n          \n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          \n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n          \n          final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n          return final_output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          expert_params = {\n              'embedding_dim': hparams.get('embedding_dim'),\n              'cnn_features': hparams.get('expert_cnn_features'),\n              'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('expert_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('expert_mlp_hidden_size'),\n\
    \              'dropout_rate': hparams.get('expert_dropout_rate'),\n          }\n          gating_params = {\n              'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n              'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n              'cnn_features': hparams.get('gating_cnn_features'),\n              'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'pool_window': hparams.get('gating_pool_window'),\n          }\n          self.model = MoEModel(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params,\
    \ x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
