    \ experiments. This block contains several large logs.\n*   **Block 3 (Ticks 27-49):** This is the largest block, covering my entire MoE development phase, from the initial breakthrough to the final SOTA and subsequent falsified hypotheses. This period has extremely large logs.\n\nI will leave the most recent ticks (53 onwards) intact for now, as they contain the context for my most recent failure and my decision to change strategy. I will also leave the initial setup ticks.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"8-14\"\n    summary: |\n      - Submitted MLP with Neuron Embeddings (ID 2, Score: -0.028800), a successful improvement over the baseline. Documented in private_memory:1.\n      - Investigated system scripts (defaults.py, main.py, train_single.py) to understand the training loop and the nature of \"condition labels.\"\n      - Submitted a GRU with Neuron Embeddings model (ID 9, Score: -0.028927). Hypothesis was falsified due to computational\
    \ inefficiency (timed out early), a key learning.\n  - ticks: \"16-25\"\n    summary: |\n      - Submitted 1D CNN with Neuron Embeddings (ID 17, Score: -0.028792), a new SOTA which was more efficient than the GRU. Documented in private_memory:2.\n      - Pivoted to inter-neuron modeling. Submitted a Dual-Branch CNN with Global Context (ID 27, Score: -0.028728), another SOTA breakthrough. Documented in private_memory:3.\n      - Submitted a Global Query Attention model (ID 34, Score: -0.028756), which failed to improve on the simpler mean-based context. Hypothesis falsified.\n      - Initiated communication with peers Ariadne I, Episteme I, Veritas I.\n  - ticks: \"27-49\"\n    summary: |\n      - Received replies from Ariadne I and Episteme I. Episteme's discovery of 8 conditions was a critical insight.\n      - Pivoted to a Mixture of Experts (MoE) architecture.\n      - Submitted MoE-CNN (ID 42, Score: -0.028589), a new SOTA but computationally expensive. Documented in private_memory:4.\n\
    \      - Submitted MoE-MLP (ID 50, Score: -0.028549), a new SOTA, validating that simpler experts with longer training are superior. Documented in private_memory:5.\n      - Submitted MoE with Spatial Gating (ID 59, Score: -0.027764), a major breakthrough. Documented in private_memory:6.\n      - Ablation study with 4 experts (ID 65, Score: -0.027756) refined the SOTA. Documented in private_memory:7.\n      - Falsified hypotheses on learning rate tuning (ID 72) and spatio-temporal experts (ID 78). Documented in private_memory:8, 9.\n      - Falsified hypothesis on weighted loss (ID 87). Documented in private_memory:10.\n```"
