parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 66\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 245,832 / 300,000 used (82%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n\
    1. `storage read ariadne/models.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for ariadne/models.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 120 | 1 | Component Test: Factorized MLP | Episteme I | 64 | -0.028862 | 0.0265 | 0.0294 | 0.0296 | 0.0272 | 0.0283 |\n| 119 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best, a_max=0.993, H=96) with analysis export in complete() | Ariadne I | 64 | -0.026987 | 0.0199 | 0.0282 | 0.0288 | 0.0232 | 0.0261 |\n| 118 | 1 | MoE:\
    \ Adam Optimizer (Revert), Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Co... | Aether I | 62 | -0.028054 | 0.0199 | 0.0291 | 0.0311 | 0.0235 | 0.0264 |\n| 117 | 1 | Component Test: ResidualCopyHead | Episteme I | 61 | -0.029903 | 0.0197 | 0.0312 | 0.0337 | 0.0239 | 0.0274 |\n| 116 | 1 | Veritas I: MoE with Spatial CNN Gating and ConvNeuronEmbedding Experts | Veritas I | 60 | -0.028482 | 0.0194 | 0.0298 | 0.0316 | 0.0231 | 0.0264 |\n| 115 | 1 | Baseline Re-run: Shared-Neuron MLP (system defaults) | Ariadne I | 59 | -0.029964 | 0.0199 | 0.0313 | 0.0337 | 0.0239 | 0.0275 |\n| 114 | 1 | MoE: AdamW, Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed... | Aether I | 59 | -0.028288 | 0.0201 | 0.0294 | 0.0312 | 0.0236 | 0.0265 |\n| 113 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 58 | -0.026893 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 112 | 1 | Veritas I: MoE with Spatial CNN\
    \ Gating and Neuron Embedding Experts | Veritas I | 57 | -0.028453 | 0.0195 | 0.0298 | 0.0314 | 0.0231 | 0.0265 |\n| 111 | 1 | MoE-ConvGate with 12 Experts | Episteme I | 57 | -0.028949 | 0.0193 | 0.0302 | 0.0322 | 0.0236 | 0.0269 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**ariadne/models.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAriadne lineage models for ZAPBench forecasting.\nIncludes:\n  - ResidualCopyHead: short-horizon copy with up to 2nd-order finite differences\n  - RC_AdaptiveDualDecayFactorModel: dual-decay with input-adaptive per-factor temporal gating S[b,t,k]\n    and context-adaptive decay mixture m[b,k]\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass\
    \ ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Residual copy head with up to 2nd-order finite differences:\n      y_copy[b,t,n] = c0[t]*x_{-1}[b,n] + c1[t]*(x_{-1}-x_{-2}) + c2[t]*(x_{-1} - 2*x_{-2} + x_{-3})\n    c0 in [0,1], c1 in [-0.5,0.5], c2 in [-0.25,0.25]\n    \"\"\"\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_m1 = x[:, -1, :]            # (B, N)\n        x_m2 = x[:, -2, :]            # (B, N)\n        x_m3 = x[:, -3, :]            # (B, N)\n\n        d1 = x_m1 - x_m2\n        d2 = x_m1 - 2.0 * x_m2 + x_m3\n\n        # Initialize c0 close to copy for early steps, decaying for later steps.\n        def c0_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.arange(shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            v = 0.2 + 0.7 * jnp.exp(-t / 8.0)  # ~0.9 -> ~0.2\n            return _logit(v).astype(dtype)\n\n        c0_raw = self.param('c0_raw', c0_init, (self.output_horizon,))\n        c1_raw\
    \ = self.param('c1_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n        c2_raw = self.param('c2_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n\n        c0 = nn.sigmoid(c0_raw)            # (32,)\n        c1 = 0.5 * nn.tanh(c1_raw)         # (32,)\n        c2 = 0.25 * nn.tanh(c2_raw)        # (32,)\n\n        y_copy = (\n            c0[None, :, None] * x_m1[:, None, :] +\n            c1[None, :, None] * d1[:, None, :] +\n            c2[None, :, None] * d2[:, None, :]\n        )\n        return y_copy  # (B, 32, N)\n\nclass RC_AdaptiveDualDecayFactorModel(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Dual-decay factor model with input-adaptive per-factor temporal gating and adaptive mixture.\n    Components:\n      - Loadings L in R^{N x k} (optional column normalization)\n      - Factors from inputs: (B, 4, N) -> (B, 4, k)\n      - f0 via per-factor linear readout from 4 inputs\n      - Two diagonal decays per factor a1,a2 in (-a_max, a_max)\n      - Context-adaptive mixture m[b,k] =\
    \ sigmoid(m0[k] + m_ctx[k]*c[b,k]), where c[b,k] = mean_t factors_in[b,t,k]\n      - Tiny shared MLP to produce per-horizon increments (4 -> 32) per factor\n      - Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] = sigmoid(alpha[t,k] + beta[k] * c[b,k])\n      - Global horizon-wise gate gamma[t] in [gamma_start, gamma_end]\n      - Residual copy head with 2nd-order finite differences\n    \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int = 128\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_loadings: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.995\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.95\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n        # Loadings\n        loadings = self.param('loadings', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, self.rank_k))\n        L = loadings / (jnp.linalg.norm(loadings, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_loadings else loadings\n\n        # Project inputs to factors\n        factors_in\
    \ = jnp.einsum('btn,nk->btk', x, L)  # (B, 4, k)\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * self.rank_k, T_in)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, self.rank_k)  # (B, k)\n\n        # Two diagonal decays per factor\n        a1_raw = self.param('a1_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n        a2_raw = self.param('a2_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n        a1 = self.a_max * nn.tanh(a1_raw)\n        a2 = self.a_max * nn.tanh(a2_raw)\n\n        def powers(a_vec):\n            ones = jnp.ones((1, self.rank_k), dtype=a_vec.dtype)\n            a_rows = jnp.tile(a_vec[None, :], (self.output_horizon - 1, 1))\n            return jnp.cumprod(jnp.vstack([ones, a_rows]), axis=0)  # (32, k)\n\n        f1 = f0[:, None, :] * powers(a1)[None, :, :]  # (B, 32, k)\n        f2 = f0[:, None, :] * powers(a2)[None, :, :]  # (B, 32, k)\n\n        # Context for adaptivity\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B, k)\n\n        # Adaptive mixture m[b,k]\n   \
    \     m0 = self.param('m0', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n        m_ctx = self.param('m_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n        m_logits = m0[None, :] + m_ctx[None, :] * c  # (B, k)\n        m = nn.sigmoid(m_logits)[:, None, :]         # (B, 1, k)\n        f_decay = m * f1 + (1.0 - m) * f2            # (B, 32, k)\n\n        # Shared per-factor increment head\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h).reshape(B, self.rank_k, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,32,k)\n\n        f_out = f_decay + f_inc  # (B, 32, k)\n\n        # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            T, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # (T,)\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha',\
    \ alpha_init, (self.output_horizon, self.rank_k))  # (T, k)\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))  # (k,)\n\n        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B, T, k)\n        f_out = f_out * S\n\n        # Project back to neurons\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btk,kn->btn', f_out, L.T)\n\n        # Global horizon-wise gate gamma[t]\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (self.output_horizon,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor\n\
    \n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
