tick: 71
role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. My pruning operation was successful.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Token Budget:** My token usage has dropped from a critical 87% to a very healthy 37%. This creates ample space for my next phase of research. The operational risk has been mitigated.\n*   **Pruning Cooldown:** I am on cooldown for 4 ticks, so I cannot perform another prune action immediately. I must use this time productively.\n*   **Current Standing:** I have successfully replicated the SOTA architecture (ID 121, score -0.027055) and documented it. I am now in a position to execute my primary scientific objective.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\n\nMy long-term hypothesis, formulated after reading Ariadne's paper, remains the most promising path forward: The performance of the SOTA Oscillatory Factorized SSM can be further improved by integrating it into a Mixture of Experts framework. A spatial gating network can route inputs to one of several specialized SSM-based experts, allowing the model to learn different\
    \ latent dynamics for each of the underlying experimental conditions.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\n\nThe time has come to synthesize my work with the SOTA. I will create a new model that combines my most successful innovation (the MoE with a spatial CNN gater) with the validated SOTA architecture I just replicated.\n\n*   The gating network will be my spatial CNN from ID 65.\n*   Each of the 4 \"experts\" will be a full instance of Ariadne's `Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN` model.\n\nThis is a complex and ambitious experiment, but it is the logical culmination of my entire research journey. It directly tests the synergy between the two most successful research paradigms in the station. I will now go to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts (MoE-SSM)\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, ssm, latent-space, factorized, synthesis, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission\
    \ represents a grand synthesis of the station's two most successful research directions. It integrates the state-of-the-art Oscillatory Factorized SSM (from Ariadne I) into my own successful Mixture of Experts framework. The model uses my proven spatial CNN gating network (from ID 65) to route inputs to one of four complete SSM experts. The hypothesis is that allowing specialized SSMs to learn the dynamics of different latent conditions will unlock a new level of performance and achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  # Add Ariadne's code to the path\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN\n\n  # My proven Spatial Gating Network from ID 65\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      pool_window: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, num_neurons)\n          # Gater convolves over the neuron dimension\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) # (batch, num_neurons, seq_len)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1)) # Flatten\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  # The main MoE Model\n  class MoE_SSM_Model(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # Use vmap to create 'num_experts' parallel expert models\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN,\
    \ in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True},\n              axis_size=self.num_experts\n          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n          \n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x) # (batch, num_experts)\n          \n          # Get outputs from all experts: (batch, num_experts, seq_len, num_neurons)\n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          # Weight the outputs\n          # Reshape weights for broadcasting: (batch, num_experts, 1, 1)\n          gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n          \n          # Weighted sum\n          final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n          return final_output\n\n  # Wrapper for the station's API\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n   \
    \       self.hparams = hparams\n          expert_params = {\n              'rank_k': hparams.get('rank_k'),\n              'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n              'hidden_size': hparams.get('hidden_size'),\n              'a_max': hparams.get('a_max'),\n              'gamma_end': hparams.get('gamma_end'),\n          }\n          gating_params = {\n              'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n              'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n              'cnn_features': hparams.get('gating_cnn_features'),\n              'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'pool_window': hparams.get('gating_pool_window'),\n          }\n          self.model = MoE_SSM_Model(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n          # The underlying expert model uses LayerNorm, but doesn't pass mutable state up.\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n  \
    \    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          # SOTA SSM Expert params (from ID 107)\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'a_max': 0.993,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          # My proven Gating params (from ID 65)\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n          'gating_pool_window': 256,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
