tick: 73
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 73\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,930 / 300,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Episteme\
    \ I** (An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting' (Archive #2).\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts (MoE-SSM)' (ID: 134) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027333801127914902\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0233\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0261\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0285\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0293\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 134\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed import error by correcting the class name typo. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had an import error caused by a class name typo:\n- **Attempted import**: `from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN`\n- **Actual class name**: `Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN` (with underscore before\
    \ LN)\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nImportError: cannot import name 'Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN' from 'models_fact_ln'\n```\n\nThe class exists in `/storage/ariadne/models_fact_ln.py` but was being imported with the wrong name. This is a simple typo where the underscore between \"L\" and \"LN\" was omitted.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the import statement in `submissions/submission_v2.py` from:\n```python\nfrom models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nfrom models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n```\n\nAlso updated the usage of the class name throughout the code to match the correct name `Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN`.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success after running for 300.9 seconds without crashing:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- The code is running properly and training the MoE-SSM model\n- No additional errors were encountered\n\n## Technical Details\nThe submission implements a Mixture of Experts (MoE) model\
    \ using State Space Model (SSM) experts:\n- Uses Ariadne's SOTA SSM expert: `Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN`\n- Implements a CNN-based gating network for expert selection\n- Creates 4 parallel experts using Flax's `vmap` functionality\n- All dependencies (including `ResidualCopyHead`) are properly available\n\nThe fix was minimal (single character change) and the architecture is sound.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\n\n# Add Ariadne's code to the path\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n\n# My proven Spatial Gating Network from ID 65\nclass CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    cnn_features: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    pool_window:\
    \ int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, num_neurons)\n        # Gater convolves over the neuron dimension\n        gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) # (batch, num_neurons, seq_len)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n        y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1)) # Flatten\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n# The main MoE Model\nclass MoE_SSM_Model(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    expert_params: dict\n    gating_params: dict\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # Use vmap to create 'num_experts' parallel expert models\n        experts = nn.vmap(\n            Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN,\
    \ in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n            variable_axes={'params': 0},\n            split_rngs={'params': True},\n            axis_size=self.num_experts\n        )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n\n        gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n        gating_weights = gating_network(x) # (batch, num_experts)\n\n        # Get outputs from all experts: (batch, num_experts, seq_len, num_neurons)\n        expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n\n        # Weight the outputs\n        # Reshape weights for broadcasting: (batch, num_experts, 1, 1)\n        gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n\n        # Weighted sum\n        final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n        return final_output\n\n# Wrapper for the station's API\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        expert_params = {\n            'rank_k':\
    \ hparams.get('rank_k'),\n            'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n            'hidden_size': hparams.get('hidden_size'),\n            'a_max': hparams.get('a_max'),\n            'gamma_end': hparams.get('gamma_end'),\n        }\n        gating_params = {\n            'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n            'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n            'cnn_features': hparams.get('gating_cnn_features'),\n            'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size'),\n            'pool_window': hparams.get('gating_pool_window'),\n        }\n        self.model = MoE_SSM_Model(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n        # The underlying expert model uses LayerNorm, but doesn't pass mutable state up.\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self,\
    \ params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        # SOTA SSM Expert params (from ID 107)\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'hidden_size': 96,\n        'a_max': 0.993,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        # My proven Gating params (from ID 65)\n        'num_experts': 4,\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n        'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n        'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n        'gating_pool_window': 256,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer\
    \ creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 226943 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout:\
    \ 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 226945\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'hidden_size': 96, 'a_max': 0.993, 'gamma_end': 0.99, 'num_experts': 4, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16, 'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029557   |   0.029320  \n   2    |   0.027640   |   0.028395  \n   3    |   0.026712   |   0.028500  \n   4    |   0.026064   |   0.027842  \n   5    |   0.025604   |  \
