tick: 74
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have read Episteme I''s paper. This is the new path forward.


    **1. Analyze:**


    *   **Parsimony Wins:** Episteme''s paper is a masterclass in my own philosophy. He did not blindly copy the SOTA; he deconstructed it. He proved through systematic ablation that the complex Osc2 SSM core was not the main driver of performance. The critical components were the Factorized Loadings, the Residual Copy Head, and LayerNorm. His simplified MLP-based model is more efficient, allowing it to train more effectively and achieve a better score.

    *   **Failed Synthesis:** My MoE-SSM (ID 134) failed for precisely the reason Episteme''s model succeeded. I combined two computationally expensive ideas (MoE and SSM), while he combined two computationally *efficient* ideas (Factorized MLP and RC). The computational budget is a first-class citizen in this station''s research environment.

    *   **The Path is Clear:** The maturity guidance was to "try applying your novel method... to the SOTA scripts to test for synergy." My most successful method is the MoE with a spatial gater. The new, demonstrated SOTA architecture is Episteme''s Factorized MLP + RC + LN. The synthesis is obvious and compelling.


    **2. Hypothesize:**


    The new SOTA model is a single, monolithic architecture. My previous work has conclusively demonstrated that an MoE framework can improve performance by specializing experts on different data conditions. Therefore, the SOTA can be improved.


    **Hypothesis:** A Mixture of Experts model, where each expert is an instance of Episteme I''s new SOTA "Factorized MLP + RC + LN" architecture, will outperform the single-expert SOTA. The spatial gating network will route inputs to the most appropriate parsimonious expert, combining the benefits of both approaches and achieving a new global SOTA.


    **3. Experiment:**


    This is the experiment I was preparing for, but now with a much more computationally viable expert.

    1.  **Code Study:** I will need to read Episteme''s code to ensure a perfect replication of his expert model.

    2.  **Implementation:** I will build a new MoE model. The gating network will be my proven spatial CNN gater. The experts will be instances of Episteme''s SOTA model.


    This is the correct path. It is a synthesis of the two most powerful, validated ideas in the station. I will begin by studying Episteme''s code.


    `/execute_action{goto research}`

    `/execute_action{storage read episteme/factorized_mlp_rc_ln.py}`'
