tick: 75
role: model
parts:
- text: "My attempt to read Episteme I's code has failed: File not found.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Missing Code:** Episteme I has published a paper detailing his SOTA architecture, but unlike Ariadne I, he has not placed the corresponding code in his public lineage storage.\n*   **Alternative Path:** This is not a dead end. His paper (Archive #2) provides an extremely clear, concise pseudocode block that outlines the entire model structure. The components are standard: `Dense` layers for the MLP and factorized projections, `LayerNorm`, and the `ResidualCopyHead` which I have already studied from Ariadne's storage.\n*   **Implementation Viability:** I can implement his model myself based on the paper's description and by importing Ariadne's public `ResidualCopyHead` module. This is more work than a direct import, but it is a clear and direct path. My understanding of the components is sufficient to proceed.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\n\nMy hypothesis remains unchanged, as it is still the most\
    \ promising direction: A Mixture of Experts model, where each expert is an instance of Episteme I's new SOTA \"Factorized MLP + RC + LN\" architecture, will outperform the single-expert SOTA.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\n\nMy plan is now to implement Episteme's SOTA model myself, and then wrap it in my MoE framework. This is a single, unified experiment. I will build the expert class based on his paper, and then use it within my proven MoE + spatial gater structure.\n\nI have all the information required. I will proceed with the submission.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE Synthesis with Episteme I's Parsimonious SOTA\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, factorized, parsimony, synthesis, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission synthesizes my successful MoE framework with Episteme I's new parsimonious SOTA architecture (ID 129). Since the source code was unavailable, the expert model (\"Factorized MLP + RC + LN\") was re-implemented based on his paper (Archive #2). The model\
    \ uses my proven spatial CNN gater to route inputs to one of four of these highly efficient experts. The hypothesis is that this combination of a multi-condition framework with a computationally efficient SOTA expert will yield a new global SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  # Import the ResidualCopyHead from Ariadne's public storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  # Re-implementation of Episteme I's SOTA expert model from his paper\n  class FactorizedMlpExpert(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # Stage 1: Encoder (Factorized Projection)\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (NUM_NEURONS, self.proj_rank))\n          V = self.param('V',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.latent_dim, self.proj_rank))\n          \n          # Einsum for efficiency: (B, 4, N) @ (N, p) -> (B, 4, p), then (B, 4, p) @ (p, k) -> (B, 4, k)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', factors_in, V)\n\n          # Stage 2: Forecaster (MLP)\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(factors_flat)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(features=OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.latent_dim)(y)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.latent_dim))\n\n          # Stage 3: Stabilization & Decoder\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1)(factors_out)\n          \n          # Einsum for efficiency: (B, 32, k) @ (k, p) -> (B, 32, p), then (B, 32, p) @ (p, N) -> (B, 32, N)\n\
    \          y_factor_p = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', y_factor_p, U)\n\n          # Stage 4: Residual Connection\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON)(x)\n          \n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  # My proven Spatial Gating Network\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      pool_window: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n\
    \          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  # Main MoE Synthesis Model\n  class MoE_Episteme_Model(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              FactorizedMlpExpert, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True},\n              axis_size=self.num_experts\n          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n          \n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n          final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n          return final_output\n\n  # Wrapper for the station's\
    \ API\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          expert_params = {\n              'latent_dim': hparams.get('latent_dim'),\n              'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n              'mlp_hidden_dim': hparams.get('mlp_hidden_dim'),\n          }\n          gating_params = {\n              'num_experts': hparams.get('num_experts'),\n              'hidden_dim': hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim'),\n              'cnn_features': hparams.get('gating_cnn_features'),\n              'cnn_kernel_size': hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size'),\n              'pool_window': hparams.get('gating_pool_window'),\n          }\n          self.model = MoE_Episteme_Model(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False,\
    \ mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          # Expert params from Episteme's SOTA\n          'latent_dim': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, # Based on my reading of his paper/ablations\n          # My proven Gating params\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n          'gating_pool_window': 256,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
