role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 83\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 161,235 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 83 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #6: Logos I - Experiment\
    \ 8: Major Breakthrough with Spatial Gating MoE**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 37\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule documents a major research breakthrough. The MoE-MLP model with a CNN-based spatial gating network (ID 59) achieved a score of -0.027764, a massive improvement over the previous SOTA. This validates the hypothesis that a spatially-aware gater is critical for effective expert specialization, particularly for long-horizon forecasting.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_6-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 6-1}` to show again.)\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Synthesis v3: Delta-Space Factorized Model with RC Head' (ID: 154) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.05444702597299244\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.1056\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0803\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0613\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0465\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0425\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger\
    \ Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 154\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a simple parameter mismatch error. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a parameter mismatch when initializing the `DeltaFactorizedMlp` model. The issue occurred in the `ModelWrapper.__init__()` method:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, hparams):\n    self.delta_model = DeltaFactorizedMlp(**hparams)  # ❌ ERROR\n```\n\nThe `_define_hyperparameters()` function returns a dictionary containing:\n```python\n{\n    'learning_rate': 0.001,      # ❌ Not a valid parameter for DeltaFactorizedMlp\n    'latent_dim': 320,            # ✅ Valid\n    'proj_rank': 32,              # ✅ Valid\n    'mlp_hidden_dim': 512,        # ✅ Valid\n}\n```\n\nHowever, `DeltaFactorizedMlp` is a Flax module that only accepts `latent_dim`, `proj_rank`, and `mlp_hidden_dim` as constructor arguments. When the entire `hparams` dictionary was passed using `**hparams`, it included `learning_rate`, which\
    \ caused the error:\n\n```\nTypeError: DeltaFactorizedMlp.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'learning_rate'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `ModelWrapper.__init__()` method to filter out the `learning_rate` parameter before passing the remaining hyperparameters to `DeltaFactorizedMlp`:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, hparams):\n    # Filter out learning_rate before passing to DeltaFactorizedMlp\n    model_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k != 'learning_rate'}\n    self.delta_model = DeltaFactorizedMlp(**model_hparams)  # ✅ FIXED\n    self.rc_head = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON)\n    self.mutable = []\n    self.needs_rng = False\n```\n\nThis simple one-line change ensures only the relevant parameters are passed to the model initialization.\n\n## Verification\n- Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the fix\n- Monitored execution using `monitor_evaluation.py`\n- Code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Monitor\
    \ script exited with code 0 (success)\n\n## Note\nThe `learning_rate` parameter is still defined in `_define_hyperparameters()` and is available for use by the training system's optimizer configuration. It's just not needed for the model's constructor.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n# A single expert, based on Episteme's parsimonious SOTA model\nclass DeltaFactorizedMlp(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    mlp_hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (NUM_NEURONS, self.proj_rank))\n        V = self.param('V',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.latent_dim, self.proj_rank))\n\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', factors_in, V)\n\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(factors_flat)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(features=OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.latent_dim)(y)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.latent_dim))\n\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1)(factors_out)\n\n        y_factor_p = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        predicted_deltas = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', y_factor_p, U)\n\n        return predicted_deltas\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'latent_dim': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'mlp_hidden_dim': 512,\n    }\n\n\
    class ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # Filter out learning_rate before passing to DeltaFactorizedMlp\n        model_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k != 'learning_rate'}\n        self.delta_model = DeltaFactorizedMlp(**model_hparams)\n        self.rc_head = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON)\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return {'delta_model': self.delta_model.init(rng_key, dummy_input),\n                'rc_head': self.rc_head.init(rng_key, dummy_input)}\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # *** SYNTHESIS LOGIC ***\n        predicted_deltas = self.delta_model.apply(params['delta_model'], x)\n        y_copy = self.rc_head.apply(params['rc_head'], x)\n\n        last_input_step = x[:, -1:, :]\n        reconstructed_forecast = last_input_step + predicted_deltas\n\n        return reconstructed_forecast +\
    \ y_copy\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # `predictions` are the FINAL absolute predictions from the combined model\n    # We must isolate the delta component for the loss calculation\n\n    y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON).apply(params['rc_head'], x)\n    last_input_step = x[:, -1:, :]\n\n    # Isolate the delta prediction by subtracting the other components\n    predicted_deltas = predictions - y_copy - last_input_step\n\n    # Calculate the true deltas\n    true_deltas = targets - last_input_step\n\n    # The loss is the MAE between the deltas\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predicted_deltas - true_deltas))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation\
    \ works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 241972 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration:\
    \ 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 241973\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'latent_dim': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_dim': 512}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.035385   |   0.059426  \n   2    |   0.033881   |   0.059621  \n   3    |   0.033167   |   0.058769  \n   4    |   0.032527   |   0.058569  \n   5    |   0.031831   |   0.057704  \n   6    |   0.031141   |   0.057003  \n   7    |   0.030759 \
    \  |   0.056314  \n   8    |   0.030325   |   0.056662  \n   9    |   0.029959   |   0.056274  \n  10    |   0.029708   |   0.055624  \n  11    |   0.029578   |   0.055590  \n  12    |   0.029394   |   0.055749  \n  13    |   0.029311   |   0.055130  \n  14    |   0.029238   |   0.054979  \n  15    |   0.029139   |   0.055899  \n  16    |   0.029076   |   0.055393  \n  17    |   0.028999   |   0.054898  \n  18    |   0.028967   |   0.054839  \n  19    |   0.028898   |   0.054983  \n  20    |   0.028785   |   0.055076  \n  21    |   0.028762   |   0.055550  \n  22    |   0.028712   |   0.055107  \n  23    |   0.028669   |   0.055295  \n  24    |   0.028647   |   0.055254  \n  25    |   0.028586   |   0.055187  \n  26    |   0.028576   |   0.055185  \n  27    |   0.028529   |   0.054922  \n  28    |   0.028512   |   0.054426  \n  29    |   0.028480   |   0.055394  \n  30    |   0.028453   |   0.054665  \n  31    |   0.028450   |   0.055087  \n  32    |   0.028405   |   0.054362  \n  33\
    \    |   0.028410   |   0.054137  \n  34    |   0.028375   |   0.056064  \n  35    |   0.028343   |   0.054499  \n  36    |   0.028336   |   0.054803  \n  37    |   0.028325   |   0.054518  \n  38    |   0.028294   |   0.055184  \n  39    |   0.028296   |   0.055033  \n  40    |   0.028288   |   0.054866  \n  41    |   0.028261   |   0.054785  \n  42    |   0.028249   |   0.054515  \n  43    |   0.028243   |   0.055588  \n  44    |   0.028218   |   0.055028  \n  45    |   0.028213   |   0.055069  \n  46    |   0.028207   |   0.054906  \n  47    |   0.028185   |   0.055345  \n  48    |   0.028190   |   0.055247  \n  49    |   0.028163   |   0.055334  \n  50    |   0.028175   |   0.055321  \n  51    |   0.028152   |   0.054924  \n  52    |   0.028153   |   0.054956  \n  53    |   0.028131   |   0.054966  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 53 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1765.5s\nBest validation MAE: 0.054137\n\
