role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 89\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 195,960 / 300,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 89 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Surgical\
    \ Synthesis: MoE applied to Residual Copy Head' (ID: 165) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027002530039097045\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0233\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0261\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0281\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0288\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 165\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed parameter naming mismatch in the `ModelWrapper` class that caused initialization to fail.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a parameter naming inconsistency in the `ModelWrapper.__init__` method. The hyperparameters dictionary used prefixed names (e.g., `gating_cnn_features`, `gating_cnn_kernel_size`, `gating_pool_window`) to avoid conflicts, but these were being passed directly to the `CnnGatingNetwork` class which expected unprefixed parameter names (e.g., `cnn_features`, `cnn_kernel_size`, `pool_window`).\n\n**Error trace:**\n```\nTypeError: CnnGatingNetwork.__init__()\
    \ got an unexpected keyword argument 'gating_cnn_features'\n```\n\nThe problematic code was in lines 98-105 of the original submission:\n```python\ngating_params = {k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in ['num_experts','gating_cnn_features','gating_cnn_kernel_size','gating_pool_window']}\ngating_params['hidden_dim'] = hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim')\n```\n\nThis attempted to filter hyperparameters but kept the `gating_` prefixes, which didn't match the class signature.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `ModelWrapper.__init__` method to explicitly map hyperparameter names to the correct parameter names expected by `CnnGatingNetwork`:\n\n```python\n# Fix: Map hyperparameter names to CnnGatingNetwork parameter names\ngating_params = {\n    'num_experts': hparams['num_experts'],\n    'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'],\n    'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'],\n    'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'],\n    'pool_window': hparams['gating_pool_window']\n\
    }\n```\n\nThis ensures that:\n- `gating_cnn_features` → `cnn_features`\n- `gating_cnn_kernel_size` → `cnn_kernel_size`\n- `gating_pool_window` → `pool_window`\n- `gating_hidden_dim` → `hidden_dim`\n- `num_experts` remains unchanged\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) has been running successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing. The monitor script confirmed the fix with exit code 0, indicating the code is executing correctly through the validation phase and beyond.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **File Modified:** submissions/submission_v2.py\n- **Lines Changed:** 96-103 (ModelWrapper.__init__ method)\n- **Change Type:** Parameter mapping fix\n- **Verification Method:** Automated monitor script with 300-second timeout\n- **Result:** Code running successfully without crashes\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n\
    ```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\nclass FactorizedMlpForecaster(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    mlp_hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (NUM_NEURONS, self.proj_rank))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.latent_dim, self.proj_rank))\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', factors_in, V)\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(factors_flat)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(features=OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.latent_dim)(y)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((batch_size,\
    \ OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.latent_dim))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1)(factors_out)\n        y_factor_p = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', y_factor_p, U)\n        return y_factor\n\nclass CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    cnn_features: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    pool_window: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n        y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\nclass SurgicalMoE(nn.Module):\n \
    \   gating_params: dict\n    forecaster_params: dict\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # 1. Main forecaster (single, powerful)\n        y_factor = FactorizedMlpForecaster(**self.forecaster_params, name=\"Forecaster\")(x)\n\n        # 2. Gating network decides which RC head to use\n        gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"Gating\")\n        gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n\n        # 3. MoE of simple RC Heads\n        rc_experts = nn.vmap(\n            ResidualCopyHead, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n            variable_axes={'params': 0},\n            split_rngs={'params': True},\n            axis_size=self.gating_params['num_experts']\n        )(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON, name=\"RC_Experts\")\n\n        rc_outputs = rc_experts(x) # (batch, num_experts, seq_len, num_neurons)\n\n        # 4. Create the final mixed RC output\n        gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights,\
    \ -1), -1)\n        y_copy_mixed = jnp.sum(rc_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy_mixed\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'latent_dim': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, # Forecaster\n        'num_experts': 4, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16, # Gater\n        'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256,\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        forecaster_params = {k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in ['latent_dim','proj_rank','mlp_hidden_dim']}\n        # Fix: Map hyperparameter names to CnnGatingNetwork parameter names\n        gating_params = {\n            'num_experts': hparams['num_experts'],\n            'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'],\n            'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'],\n            'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'],\n            'pool_window': hparams['gating_pool_window']\n\
    \        }\n        self.model = SurgicalMoE(gating_params=gating_params, forecaster_params=forecaster_params)\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\n\
    Validation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 251133 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout\
