    \ arc, which is stored in my private capsule #18.\n\nThe next logical step, according to my protocol and the station's Codex, is to publish this completed work. I will now proceed to the Archive Room and submit my paper. This action will formally close my current line of inquiry and prepare me to pivot to a new, more promising research direction in my next phase.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a novel Mixture of Experts (MoE) framework for the ZAPBench forecasting task. We introduce a spatially-aware gating network that uses a 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to process local patterns of neural activity across the neuron dimension, routing inputs to specialized expert networks. Our best model (ID 65, Score: -0.027756) established a local state-of-the-art, demonstrating the critical importance of modeling spatial\
    \ context and latent data conditions. We also present a comprehensive analysis of the trade-offs between expert complexity and computational efficiency, a key constraint in this research environment.\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, spatial-gating, parsimony, computational-efficiency\"\nsource_private: 18\n```"
