tick: 92
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, in the Research Counter. My previous action was to submit an author-run baseline experiment (ID 172) to fulfill a requirement for my paper. This action was taken in response to the rejection of my initial publication attempt.\n\nMy current plan is methodical and addresses all reviewer feedback. I am running the baseline now. My next action is to run the required fifth experiment for the paper: an ablation study that demonstrates the value of my spatial gater. While the baseline runs, I will submit this second experiment. This parallel execution is an efficient use of station resources.\n\nReflecting on the broader station activity, I note that Aether I has replicated Episteme's SOTA and added a \"Curvature Loss\" (ID 167), achieving a new SOTA of -0.026638. Episteme's \"Modular Graph\" experiment (ID 166) has failed. This shows that even the top agents face setbacks when exploring truly novel paradigms. The SOTA is once again a moving target, but my current focus must\
    \ be on fulfilling my publication duty, which requires these specific, controlled experiments.\n\nI will now submit the ablation study.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation for MoE Paper: Simple Gater vs. Spatial Gater\"\ntags: \"ablation-study, mixture-of-experts, moe, gating-network, publication-requirement\"\nabstract: |\n  This ablation study is the fifth experiment required for my paper on the Spatially-Aware MoE. It compares my SOTA MoE model (ID 65), which uses a spatial CNN gater, against an identical model where the gater is replaced with a simple mean-based gater. The hypothesis is that the spatial gater is a critical component, and its removal will lead to a significant degradation in performance, thereby quantitatively justifying its inclusion.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  # Same efficient MLP expert from my SOTA MoE\n  class MlpExpert(nn.Module):\n\
    \      embedding_dim: int\n      hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim, name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          \n          x_last_step = jnp.transpose(x[:, -1:, :], (0, 2, 1))\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_last_step, broadcasted_embeddings], axis=-1)\n          \n          y = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (-1, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n          y = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(y)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n\
    \          \n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  # ABLATION: Simple Gating Network that uses global mean\n  class SimpleGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Compute a global summary by averaging over time and neurons\n          gater_input = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEModel(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              MlpExpert, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params':\
    \ 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n              axis_size=self.num_experts\n          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n          \n          # Use the simple gater for this ablation\n          gating_network = SimpleGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights, -1), -1)\n          final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n          return final_output\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          expert_params =\
    \ {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['embedding_dim', 'hidden_size', 'dropout_rate']}\n          gating_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['num_experts']}\n          gating_params['hidden_dim'] = hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim')\n          self.model = MoEModel(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return\
    \ ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
