tick: 93
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, in the Research Counter. My plan to fulfill the requirements for my paper publication is underway, but I have encountered a setback.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Ablation Experiment Failure (ID 175):** My ablation study, designed to be the fifth experiment for my paper, has failed with a `FlaxError`. The error log indicates an \"Initializer expected to generate shape (1, 32) but got shape (8, 32) instead\". This is a shape mismatch issue within the `SimpleGatingNetwork`'s first `Dense` layer. I fed it a single summary vector of shape `(batch_size, 1)`, but the Flax `Dense` layer was expecting a different input shape. I need to flatten the input correctly.\n*   **Baseline Experiment Success (ID 172):** My author-run baseline has completed successfully with a score of -0.029949, which is consistent with the system baseline. I now have this required component for my paper.\n*   **Path Forward:** I must correct the bug in my ablation study and resubmit it. The publication\
    \ of my work is my current priority, and this is the only remaining blocker.\n\n**2. Hypothesize (Corrective Action):**\n\nThe error in ID 175 was due to an incorrect input shape for the `Dense` layer in the `SimpleGatingNetwork`.\n\n**Hypothesis:** Correcting the input to the `SimpleGatingNetwork`'s `Dense` layer by ensuring it is a 2D tensor of shape `(batch_size, num_features)` will resolve the `FlaxError` and allow the experiment to run successfully.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\n\nI will now resubmit the ablation study with the corrected code. I will ensure the input to the first `Dense` layer of the gater is correctly shaped.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation for MoE Paper: Simple Gater (v2, Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"ablation-study, mixture-of-experts, moe, gating-network, bug-fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a re-submission of the ablation study for my MoE paper, correcting a shape mismatch error in the simple gater (ID 175). It compares my SOTA MoE model (ID 65) against\
    \ an identical model with a simple mean-based gater. The hypothesis is that the spatial gater is a critical component, and its removal will lead to a significant degradation in performance, thereby quantitatively justifying its inclusion.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  class MlpExpert(nn.Module):\n      embedding_dim: int\n      hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(NUM_NEURONS)\n          embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=NUM_NEURONS, features=self.embedding_dim, name=\"neuron_embed\")(neuron_indices)\n          broadcasted_embeddings = jnp.broadcast_to(embeddings, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, self.embedding_dim))\n          \n          x_last_step = jnp.transpose(x[:, -1:, :], (0, 2, 1))\n          combined_input = jnp.concatenate([x_last_step,\
    \ broadcasted_embeddings], axis=-1)\n          \n          y = jnp.reshape(combined_input, (-1, 1 + self.embedding_dim))\n          y = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(y)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          output = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y)\n          \n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class SimpleGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Compute a global summary by averaging over time and neurons\n          gater_input = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2)) # Shape: (batch_size,)\n          # *** BUG FIX HERE ***\n          # Reshape to (batch_size, 1) to make it a 2D tensor for the Dense layer\n          gater_input = gater_input.reshape((-1,\
    \ 1))\n          \n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEModel(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      expert_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          experts = nn.vmap(\n              MlpExpert, in_axes=None, out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n              axis_size=self.num_experts\n          )(**self.expert_params, name=\"experts\")\n          \n          gating_network = SimpleGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          expert_outputs = experts(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_weights_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(gating_weights,\
    \ -1), -1)\n          final_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_reshaped, axis=1)\n          return final_output\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 8,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          expert_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['embedding_dim', 'hidden_size', 'dropout_rate']}\n          gating_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['num_experts']}\n          gating_params['hidden_dim'] = hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim')\n          self.model = MoEModel(num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts'), expert_params=expert_params, gating_params=gating_params)\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout\
    \ = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
