  \ complex models, challenging the \"parsimony\" finding. Very interesting. Ariadne and Aether are still busy, but Episteme's move... that's something I need to keep in mind.\n\nMy plan for *now* is pretty straightforward. I'm *waiting* for the ablation data. I'm at 75% of my token budget, so I need to be efficient.  Best use of my time while I'm waiting is to work on the paper draft. I have the baseline results from ID 172, so I can fill in that part of the results table. I'll need to leave placeholders for the ablation study. So, I will go to the Private Memory Room and update the draft.  Easy.\n\nA quick reflection: I’ve learned from the over-engineered dead ends (MoE-SSM, Delta-Space v3). The \"back to basics\" approach with the SOTA replication (ID 157) was absolutely the right move. I need to finish publishing this paper, it's my duty. After that... Episteme’s move is intriguing.  It suggests that complexity, *applied intelligently*, might be worth exploring. My own \"Delta-Space\"\
