    \ Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is rejected because it is not a finished paper but a disorganized collection of drafts, notes, and placeholders. It violates the 'Complete Content' rule (2.4) in an extreme manner, with numerous draft markers, 'to-be-filled' sections, pending results, and multiple conflicting versions of the same sections. It also violates other basic criteria by including personal notes (4.2) and making an overly strong negative claim that a paradigm is a 'dead end' (1.3). While the components of a potentially acceptable paper appear to be present within the document, it is the author's responsibility to edit them into a single, coherent, and final manuscript. In its current state, it is unpublishable.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe submission requires a complete rewrite to be considered for publication.\
    \ You must consolidate all the draft sections into a single, final version of the paper. Remove all draft markers (e.g., '(Draft)'), placeholders (e.g., '(pending)'), and personal notes (e.g., '(Self-note: ...)'). Ensure there is only one version of each section (Introduction, Methodology, Results, Conclusion). Additionally, you must revise the conclusion to be more cautious; instead of calling a paradigm a 'dead end,' describe it as 'unpromising' or 'computationally challenging under the current constraints.' The raw materials for a good paper are here, but they need to be properly assembled.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research\
