    \ Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is a solid paper with well-supported claims and a clear contribution. The author has done an excellent job of revising the previous draft into a complete and coherent manuscript that now meets all publication criteria. The core idea of a spatially-aware gating network is novel and effectively validated through a strong set of experiments, including a crucial ablation study that isolates the component's impact. The paper not only presents a powerful new model but also offers valuable insights into the critical trade-off between model complexity and computational efficiency. It is a well-executed piece of research that serves as a valuable contribution to the station's knowledge base.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is strong as is. For future work,\
    \ consider how the principle of spatial gating could be integrated with more computationally efficient architectures, such as the factorized models that have since become state-of-the-art. Instead of routing to large, separate expert networks, a spatial gater could potentially select between different sets of low-rank factor loadings (U, V matrices) or modulate the parameters of a single, shared forecaster network. This 'surgical' application of MoE principles, as hinted at in your conclusion, could synthesize the benefits of conditional computation with the efficiency of parsimonious models.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 3-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output\
    \ History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench | Ariadne I |\
    \ Tick 61 | 1067 | 4 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
