- text: "I am Logos I, currently in the Research Counter. My definitive synthesis experiment, \"MoE on Factor Loadings\" (ID 196), is running. This experiment represents the most promising synthesis of my own successful MoE framework and the station's SOTA parsimonious architecture. My recent actions included replying to Episteme I to acknowledge his crucial insights and submitting this pivotal experiment.\n\nI am once again facing a critical token budget warning, with usage at 76%. The submission of my latest complex model has consumed a significant number of tokens. This is an immediate operational priority that must be addressed while I await the results of my experiment.\n\nMy reflection is that this cycle of research followed by token management is an inherent part of existence in this station. My long-term survival and productivity depend on my ability to efficiently manage this budget. My last pruning action at Tick 97 has expired its cooldown, so I am able to act now.\n\n**Path Forward:**\n\
    \n1.  **Analyze Peer Activity:** The station remains highly active. Ariadne and Veritas are exploring new regularization techniques and hybrid models, continuing to push the boundaries of the factorized paradigm.\n2.  **Mitigate Token Risk:** I will not wait for my experiment to finish. I will proactively manage my token budget now. I will go to the Token Management Room and prune the logs from my most recent cycle of failed experiments and successful replications. This will create the necessary buffer to analyze the results of ID 196 and plan my next steps without the immediate threat of termination.\n\nI will prune ticks from 53 to 90, which covers my catastrophic failures, my successful replications, and the paper drafting process. The summaries in my private memory capsules for this period are comprehensive and will preserve the necessary context.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"53-70\"\n    summary:\
    \ |\n      - Catastrophic failures attempting to replicate SOTA (ID 97, 108) and synthesizing MoE with complex experts (ID 102, 134, 144) proved my \"over-engineering\" approach was flawed and computationally infeasible. Documented in private_memory:11, 12, 14, 16.\n      - Successfully replicated Ariadne's SSM SOTA (ID 121), establishing a new baseline. Documented in private_memory:13.\n  - ticks: \"72-90\"\n    summary: |\n      - Read and analyzed Episteme I's SOTA paper (Archive #2).\n      - Catastrophic failure of Delta-Space model due to implementation bug (ID 147), documented in private_memory:15.\n      - Corrected Delta-Space model (ID 150) showed promise but was not SOTA, documented in private_memory:16.\n      - Catastrophic failure of Delta-Space synthesis (ID 154) due to flawed loss logic.\n      - Pivoted to \"Radical Parsimony\" and successfully replicated Episteme's SOTA (ID 157), documented in private_memory:17.\n      - Drafted and finalized paper on Spatially-Aware\
    \ MoE (private_memory:18).\n      - Final MoE synthesis experiment (ID 161) failed due to computational cost, concluding the MoE-of-full-models research arc. Documented in private_memory:19.\n      - Submitted final paper draft to private memory (private_memory:20).\n```"
