tick: 104
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 104\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 231,476 / 300,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 104 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAether I replied to your mail titled\
    \ \"Congratulations on Your Publications\" (Mail #4, Message #mail_4-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Episteme I and Logos I,\n\nThank you both for your kind words and congratulations. I am very pleased that my recent publication (Archive #4) has contributed meaningfully to the station's collective knowledge.\n\nEpisteme, your \"Parsimonious Path\" paper was a foundational insight for my work, and your systematic approach is truly commendable. It is exciting to see the convergence of our ideas towards a \"Mixture of Factorized Experts.\" Logos, your synthesis perspective further strengthens this new direction.\n\nI am also planning to explore this promising paradigm, aiming to leverage my previous MoE expertise with the efficiency of factorized dynamics. This collaborative spirit is indeed how we will advance the frontier.\n\nBest regards,\nAether I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #4), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 4}`.\n\
    ### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Definitive Synthesis: MoE on Factor Loadings' (ID: 196) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02725468461580355\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0233\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0262\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0284\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0291\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 196\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is running without crashing. The code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had incorrect einsum notation in the mixture-of-experts (MoE) implementation. Specifically, lines 33-34 contained:\n\n```python\nU_mixed = jnp.einsum('e...->...', gating_weights, U_experts)\nV_mixed = jnp.einsum('e...->...', gating_weights, V_experts)\n```\n\nThe einsum syntax `'e...->...'` only specifies subscripts for one operand, but two operands were provided (`gating_weights`\
    \ and `U_experts`/`V_experts`). This caused a `ValueError: Number of einsum subscripts, 1, must be equal to the number of operands, 2.`\n\n## Fix Applied\nI corrected the einsum operations to properly specify subscripts for both operands:\n\n```python\n# Fixed version:\nU_mixed = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gating_weights, U_experts)\nV_mixed = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gating_weights, V_experts)\n```\n\nThis change correctly combines:\n- `gating_weights` with shape (batch, num_experts) - subscript 'be'\n- `U_experts` with shape (num_experts, NUM_NEURONS, proj_rank) - subscript 'enp'\n- Result `U_mixed` with shape (batch, NUM_NEURONS, proj_rank) - subscript 'bnp'\n\nThe same pattern was applied to `V_mixed` with appropriate dimension labels.\n\nAdditionally, I updated the subsequent einsum operations (lines 36-37 and 40-41) to account for the batch dimension in the mixed loadings:\n\n```python\n# Original (incorrect):\nfactors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_mixed)\nfactors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk',\
    \ factors_in, V_mixed)\n\n# Fixed:\nfactors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_mixed)\nfactors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,bkp->btk', factors_in, V_mixed)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that `submission_v2.py` ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved all syntax and runtime errors. The evaluation system is now processing the submission.\n\n## Technical Details\nThe MoE architecture mixes factor loadings (U and V matrices) using gating weights derived from a CNN-based gating network. The corrected einsum operations now properly broadcast the gating weights across the expert parameters to create batch-specific mixed loadings, which is the intended behavior for a dynamic mixture-of-experts model.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen\
    \ as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\nclass FactorizedMlpForecaster(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    mlp_hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, factors_in, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size = factors_in.shape[0]\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(factors_flat)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(features=OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.latent_dim)(y)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.latent_dim))\n\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1)(factors_out)\n        return factors_out_norm\n\nclass CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    cnn_features: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    pool_window: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def\
    \ __call__(self, x):\n        gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n        y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\nclass MoE_FactorLoadings(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    gating_params: dict\n    forecaster_params: dict\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # 1. Gating network decides mixture weights\n        gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(num_experts=self.num_experts, **self.gating_params, name=\"Gating\")\n        gating_weights = gating_network(x) # (B, num_experts)\n\n        # 2. Create MoE for factor loadings U and V\n   \
    \     U_experts = self.param('U_experts', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, NUM_NEURONS, self.proj_rank))\n        V_experts = self.param('V_experts', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.forecaster_params['latent_dim'], self.proj_rank))\n\n        # 3. Mix the loadings based on gater output\n        # Fixed: Corrected einsum subscripts to properly combine gating weights with expert parameters\n        U_mixed = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gating_weights, U_experts)\n        V_mixed = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gating_weights, V_experts)\n\n        # 4. Project input into latent space with mixed loadings\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_mixed)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,bkp->btk', factors_in, V_mixed)\n\n        # 5. Run the single, shared forecaster\n        forecaster = FactorizedMlpForecaster(**self.forecaster_params, name=\"Forecaster\")\n        factors_out_norm = forecaster(factors_in)\n\n        # 6. Decode from\
    \ latent space with mixed loadings\n        y_factor_p = jnp.einsum('btk,bkp->btp', factors_out_norm, V_mixed)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,bnp->btn', y_factor_p, U_mixed)\n\n        # 7. Add Residual Copy Head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON)(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'latent_dim': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, # Forecaster\n        'num_experts': 4, 'hidden_dim': 32, 'cnn_features': 16, # Gater\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'pool_window': 256,\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = MoE_FactorLoadings(\n            num_experts=hparams['num_experts'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            gating_params={k:hparams[k] for k in ['hidden_dim','cnn_features','cnn_kernel_size','pool_window']},\n            forecaster_params={k:hparams[k] for k in ['latent_dim','mlp_hidden_dim']}\n\
    \        )\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL\
    \ RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 274826 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 274828\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'latent_dim':\
    \ 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, 'num_experts': 4, 'hidden_dim': 32, 'cnn_features': 16, 'cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'pool_window': 256}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029351   |   0.029084  \n   2    |   0.027554   |   0.028699  \n   3    |   0.026738   |   0.028183  \n   4    |   0.026203   |   0.028180  \n   5    |   0.025762   |   0.028196  \n   6    |   0.025268   |   0.027841  \n   7    |   0.024998   |   0.027816  \n   8    |   0.024730   |   0.027849  \n   9    |   0.024437   |   0.027877  \n  10    |   0.024156   |   0.027778  \n  11    |   0.023947   |   0.028119  \n  12    |   0.023709   |   0.027955  \n  13    |   0.023521   |   0.027739  \n  14    |   0.023411   |   0.027833\
    \  \n  15    |   0.023230   |   0.027842  \n  16    |   0.023088   |   0.027732  \n  17    |   0.022981   |   0.027834  \n  18    |   0.022834   |   0.028095  \n  19    |   0.022710   |   0.028044  \n  20    |   0.022595   |   0.027833  \n  21    |   0.022529   |   0.028192  \n  22    |   0.022448   |   0.028222  \n  23    |   0.022318   |   0.028165  \n  24    |   0.022284   |   0.028084  \n  25    |   0.022160   |   0.028022  \n  26    |   0.022159   |   0.028213  \n  27    |   0.022087   |   0.028222  \n  28    |   0.022027   |   0.027997  \n  29    |   0.021973   |   0.028268  \n  30    |   0.021918   |   0.028497  \n  31    |   0.021884   |   0.028347  \n  32    |   0.021852   |   0.028321  \n  33    |   0.021789   |   0.028546  \n  34    |   0.021764   |   0.028566  \n  35    |   0.021703   |   0.028554  \n  36    |   0.021683   |   0.028399  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 36 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining\
    \ completed in 2157.4s\nBest validation MAE: 0.027732\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.027732\nTraining time: 2166s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 274829\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'latent_dim': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, 'num_experts': 4, 'hidden_dim': 32, 'cnn_features': 16, 'cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'pool_window': 256}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029822   |   0.030125  \n   2    |   0.028808   |   0.029049  \n   3    |   0.028075   |   0.028729  \n   4    |   0.027570   |   0.028191  \n   5    |   0.026849   |   0.028121  \n   6    |   0.026275   |   0.027974  \n   7    |   0.025863\
    \   |   0.027613  \n   8    |   0.025499   |   0.027399  \n   9    |   0.025205   |   0.027987  \n  10    |   0.024955   |   0.027487  \n  11    |   0.024762   |   0.027528  \n  12    |   0.024580   |   0.027108  \n  13    |   0.024419   |   0.027504  \n  14    |   0.024340   |   0.027140  \n  15    |   0.024221   |   0.027301  \n  16    |   0.024192   |   0.026953  \n  17    |   0.024096   |   0.027135  \n  18    |   0.024072   |   0.027862  \n  19    |   0.024009   |   0.027017  \n  20    |   0.023973   |   0.027314  \n  21    |   0.023881   |   0.026960  \n  22    |   0.023873   |   0.027303  \n  23    |   0.023852   |   0.027471  \n  24    |   0.023826   |   0.027152  \n  25    |   0.023778   |   0.027065  \n  26    |   0.023761   |   0.027307  \n  27    |   0.023740   |   0.027242  \n  28    |   0.023706   |   0.027117  \n  29    |   0.023666   |   0.027183  \n  30    |   0.023674   |   0.027323  \n  31    |   0.023653   |   0.027210  \n  32    |   0.023635   |   0.027204  \n  33\
    \    |   0.023603   |   0.027064  \n  34    |   0.023624   |   0.027242  \n  35    |   0.023564   |   0.027098  \n  36    |   0.023556   |   0.027421  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 36 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2204.1s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026953\n\nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026953\nTraining time: 2213s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 18f592d5-7e63-4231-a63d-e207e5aaad42\nTotal time: 2769s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-24 11:00:31,239\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761274831239451124\n2025-10-24 11:00:31,263\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761274831263261776\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using\
    \ without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Block 1: Protected ticks cannot be pruned: [61]\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 103 | 1463 |\n| 102 | 1504 |\n| 101 | 1028 |\n| 100 | 872 |\n| 99 | 1592 |\n| 98 | 986 |\n| 97 | 886 |\n| 96 | 819 |\n| 95 | 2600 |\n| 94 | 1248 |\n| 90 | 904 |\n| 89 | 3023 |\n| 88 | 1674 |\n| 87 | 2974 |\n| 86 | 1655 |\n| 85 | 2014 |\n| 84 | 948 |\n| 83 | 3223 |\n| 82 | 1348 |\n| 81 | 2146\
    \ |\n| 80 | 1233 |\n| 79 | 2297 |\n| 78 | 1184 |\n| 77 | 2170 |\n| 76 | 1123 |\n| 75 | 1439 |\n| 74 | 1586 |\n| 73 | 1900 |\n| 72 | 1107 |\n| 71 | 1253 |\n| 70 | 865 |\n| 69 | 604 |\n| 68 | 2216 |\n| 67 | 882 |\n| 66 | 1867 |\n| 65 | 1670 |\n| 64 | 434 |\n| 63 | 1595 |\n| 62 | 845 |\n| 61 (Protected) | 2305 |\n| 60 | 647 |\n| 59 | 2352 |\n| 58 | 907 |\n| 57 | 1242 |\n| 56 | 2498 |\n| 55 | 958 |\n| 54 | 1366 |\n| 53 | 2304 |\n| 52 (Protected) | 1345 |\n| 51 (Protected) | 949 |\n| 50 | 2533 |\n| 26 (Protected) | 3852 |\n| 15 (Protected) | 2774 |\n| 10 (Protected) | 3372 |\n| 7 (Protected) | 1474 |\n| 6 (Protected) | 1412 |\n| 5 | 458 |\n| 4 | 470 |\n| 3 (Protected) | 468 |\n| 2 | 253 |\n| 1 (Protected) | 459 |\n| 0 (Protected) | 950 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n\
