parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 106\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 93,546 / 300,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 106 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fundamental\
    \ Test: Delta-Space on System Baseline MLP' (ID: 201) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029976872602176765\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0239\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0313\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0338\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 201\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code to run without crashing. The submission now successfully completes validation and begins full Ray training.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical issues:\n\n1. **Explicit `create_network()` returning `None`**: The author defined a `create_network()` function that explicitly returned `None`, preventing the fallback mechanism from using the default network. The system's `load_all_functions()` uses `getattr(submission, 'create_network', default_create_network)`, which only falls back to the default if the function is NOT defined. Since the function\
    \ was defined (but returned None), it used None instead of the default.\n\n2. **Empty hyperparameters dict**: The submission defined `_define_hyperparameters()` returning an empty dict `{}`. While the system can handle plain values by wrapping them in `tune.choice()`, it cannot handle an empty search space with OptunaSearch. The system requires at least one hyperparameter to search over (e.g., learning_rate).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Removed `create_network()` entirely**: This allows the system to fall back to `default_create_network()`, which returns a `SharedMLPWrapper()` instance with the baseline MLP architecture.\n\n2. **Removed `_define_hyperparameters()` entirely**: This allows the system to fall back to `default_define_hyperparameters()`, which returns `{'learning_rate': 0.001}`, providing a valid search space for OptunaSearch.\n\n3. **Kept the custom `compute_loss()` function**: This implements the author's \"delta-space\"\
    \ paradigm, which computes loss on the predicted deltas rather than absolute values. This is the actual innovation being tested.\n\n## Validation Results\n\n- ✅ Simple CPU validation passed (network creation, forward pass, optimizer, loss, training step)\n- ✅ Code is running for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- ✅ Ray cluster connection successful\n- ✅ Full training pipeline initiated\n\n## Key Insight\n\nThe author's comment indicated they wanted to \"use the default MLP architecture\" and focus innovation on the loss function. However, they misunderstood how to achieve this - by explicitly defining functions that return None or empty dicts, they prevented the fallback mechanism. The correct approach is to simply NOT define those functions, allowing the system to use defaults automatically.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n\
    ```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\n# This uses the default MLP architecture from system/defaults.py\n# All innovation is in the loss function and the final apply step.\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # We will let the default create_network() be called by the system\n        pass\n\n# REMOVED _define_hyperparameters() so the system uses the default\n# (which includes learning_rate for the optimizer)\n\n# REMOVED create_network() so the system uses the default MLP\n# The author's comment indicated they wanted to use the default,\n# but by defining create_network() and returning None, they prevented\n# the fallback mechanism from working.\n\ndef apply_deltas(model_fn, params, x, **kwargs):\n    # Helper to reconstruct the absolute forecast\n    last_input_step = x[:, -1:, :]\n    predicted_deltas = model_fn(params, x, **kwargs)\n    return last_input_step + predicted_deltas\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n\
    \    # predictions are the absolute forecast from the default training step\n    last_input_step = x[:, -1:, :]\n\n    # Re-calculate deltas for loss\n    predicted_deltas = predictions - last_input_step\n    true_deltas = targets - last_input_step\n\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predicted_deltas - true_deltas))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster\
    \ at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: using default\n  create_network: using default\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 277982 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 277983\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench\
    \ data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.075839   |   0.032031  \n   2    |   0.031276   |   0.030532  \n   3    |   0.030370   |   0.030367  \n   4    |   0.030292   |   0.030237  \n   5    |   0.030192   |   0.030216  \n   6    |   0.030182   |   0.030272  \n   7    |   0.030133   |   0.030205  \n   8    |   0.030096   |   0.030320  \n   9    |   0.030077   |   0.030073  \n  10    |   0.030018   |   0.030093  \n  11    |   0.030031   |   0.030973  \n  12    |   0.030017   |   0.030013  \n  13    |   0.029971   |   0.030067  \n  14    |   0.029963   |   0.031028  \n  15    |   0.029961   |   0.032145  \n  16    |   0.029931   |   0.029984  \n  17    |   0.029933   |   0.030222  \n  18    |   0.029933   |   0.030238  \n  19    |   0.029946   |   0.033057\
