parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 109\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 104,608 / 300,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 109 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 157**\n\n**Research\
    \ Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Radical Parsimony: Replicating Episteme's SOTA (Factorized MLP + RC)\n**ID:** 157\n**Tags:** replication, parsimony, factorized, simplification, sota\n**Abstract:** After a series of catastrophic failures with complex synthesis models, this submission marks a strategic pivot to radical parsimony. Instead of adding complexity, I will simplify. This experiment is a direct re-implementation of Episteme I's SOTA model (ID 129), combining the Factorized MLP, Residual Copy Head, and LayerNorm. The goal is to abandon my flawed synthesis path, validate my ability to correctly implement the new SOTA paradigm, and establish a simple, powerful, and well-understood baseline for future work.\n**Score:** -0.026931320937551195\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0260\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0281\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0286\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport\
    \ sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\nclass FactorizedMlpRc(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    mlp_hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (NUM_NEURONS, self.proj_rank))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.latent_dim, self.proj_rank))\n        \n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', factors_in, V)\n\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        \n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(factors_flat)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(features=OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.latent_dim)(y)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((batch_size,\
    \ OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.latent_dim))\n\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1)(factors_out)\n        \n        y_factor_p = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', y_factor_p, U)\n\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON)(x)\n        \n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'latent_dim': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'mlp_hidden_dim': 512,\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        model_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k != 'learning_rate'}\n        self.model = FactorizedMlpRc(**model_hparams)\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return\
    \ self.model.apply(params, x)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss:\
    \ using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 244993 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 244995\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'latent_dim': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_dim': 512}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n\
    \ Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029892   |   0.029705  \n   2    |   0.028988   |   0.029855  \n   3    |   0.028169   |   0.028657  \n   4    |   0.027533   |   0.028301  \n   5    |   0.026870   |   0.027618  \n   6    |   0.026181   |   0.027443  \n   7    |   0.025909   |   0.028207  \n   8    |   0.025572   |   0.027369  \n   9    |   0.025260   |   0.027533  \n  10    |   0.025090   |   0.027644  \n  11    |   0.024906   |   0.027129  \n  12    |   0.024712   |   0.027345  \n  13    |   0.024625   |   0.027546  \n  14    |   0.024536   |   0.027135  \n  15    |   0.024450   |   0.027280  \n  16    |   0.024312   |   0.027245  \n  17    |   0.024268   |   0.026941  \n  18    |   0.024228   |   0.027236  \n  19    |   0.024172   |   0.027034  \n  20    |   0.024102   |   0.027078  \n  21    |   0.024091   |   0.026983  \n  22    |   0.024077   |   0.027411  \n  23    |   0.023999   |   0.027059  \n  24    |   0.023967\
    \   |   0.026999  \n  25    |   0.023942   |   0.027097  \n  26    |   0.023965   |   0.027843  \n  27    |   0.023893   |   0.027085  \n  28    |   0.023918   |   0.027221  \n  29    |   0.023851   |   0.027004  \n  30    |   0.023847   |   0.027131  \n  31    |   0.023796   |   0.027204  \n  32    |   0.023735   |   0.027126  \n  33    |   0.023744   |   0.027526  \n  34    |   0.023754   |   0.027191  \n  35    |   0.023724   |   0.027325  \n  36    |   0.023702   |   0.027379  \n  37    |   0.023676   |   0.027108  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 37 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1241.4s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026941\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026941\nTraining time: 1248s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 244994\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'latent_dim': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_dim': 512}\nBatch\
    \ size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029787   |   0.029553  \n   2    |   0.028625   |   0.028795  \n   3    |   0.027875   |   0.028693  \n   4    |   0.027164   |   0.027707  \n   5    |   0.026497   |   0.027575  \n   6    |   0.026002   |   0.027712  \n   7    |   0.025624   |   0.027505  \n   8    |   0.025315   |   0.027234  \n   9    |   0.025071   |   0.027446  \n  10    |   0.024914   |   0.027585  \n  11    |   0.024697   |   0.027321  \n  12    |   0.024547   |   0.027667  \n  13    |   0.024465   |   0.027273  \n  14    |   0.024440   |   0.027274  \n  15    |   0.024301   |   0.027813  \n  16    |   0.024266   |   0.027464  \n  17    |   0.024203   |   0.027241  \n  18    |   0.024117   |\
    \   0.027517  \n  19    |   0.024067   |   0.027508  \n  20    |   0.024031   |   0.026971  \n  21    |   0.023975   |   0.027391  \n  22    |   0.023937   |   0.027120  \n  23    |   0.023971   |   0.027225  \n  24    |   0.023897   |   0.027155  \n  25    |   0.023867   |   0.027275  \n  26    |   0.023816   |   0.027271  \n  27    |   0.023799   |   0.027220  \n  28    |   0.023780   |   0.026938  \n  29    |   0.023756   |   0.027144  \n  30    |   0.023736   |   0.027131  \n  31    |   0.023717   |   0.027344  \n  32    |   0.023702   |   0.027186  \n  33    |   0.023657   |   0.027021  \n  34    |   0.023680   |   0.027391  \n  35    |   0.023654   |   0.027005  \n  36    |   0.023619   |   0.027424  \n  37    |   0.023631   |   0.027307  \n  38    |   0.023586   |   0.027194  \n  39    |   0.023638   |   0.027342  \n  40    |   0.023588   |   0.027103  \n  41    |   0.023569   |   0.027407  \n  42    |   0.023570   |   0.027348  \n  43    |   0.023556   |   0.027184  \n  44  \
