tick: 109
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, currently in the Research Counter. I have now successfully retrieved the full, correct source code for the parsimonious SOTA model from my previous successful replication (ID 157). This action corrects the procedural failure of my last two turns.\n\nMy reflection on this situation is that my protocol needs to be more robust. My new \"Pre-flight Check\" must include not just verifying dependencies, but ensuring the *source* of those dependencies is correct (i.e., from a `review` command, not an assumed file path).\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Peer Activity:** The SOTA has advanced again. Episteme (ID 213) and Aether (ID 212) have achieved scores of -0.026725 and -0.026612 respectively, likely by adding a \"Curvature Loss\" to the parsimonious model. This is a new technique I must investigate later. Most critically, Ariadne has submitted an experiment (ID 214) titled \"SGate-Input\", which appears to be *exactly the same idea* as my surgical synthesis. This means the\
    \ race is on. I must execute my experiment flawlessly and immediately.\n*   **Current State:** I have the correct source code. My hypothesis is validated as a promising direction by a top competitor. The path is clear.\n\n**2. Hypothesize (Re-affirmation):**\n\nA surgical addition of spatial features via a pre-processing block, when correctly integrated into the full SOTA architecture, will improve performance.\n\n**3. Experiment (Corrected Implementation v3):**\n\nI will now create the definitive submission. It will be a single, self-contained script. I will copy the SOTA model code directly, add my `SpatialPreProcessor`, and create a new `CombinedModel` that integrates them by modifying the SOTA's input layer and internal logic to handle the augmented feature dimension. This is the correct, rigorous approach.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Surgical Synthesis v2 (Correct Implementation)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, spatial-features, cnn, factorized, parsimony, sota\"\nabstract:\
    \ |\n  This is the corrected implementation of the surgical synthesis hypothesis. After previous procedural failures, this submission correctly integrates a spatial pre-processing block with the full, verified SOTA architecture (FactorizedMLP+RC+LN). The SOTA code is included and modified to handle an augmented input tensor containing both the original time-series and a spatial context vector for each neuron, generated by a 1D CNN across the neuron dimension. This experiment is a direct test of whether this computationally efficient method of adding spatial information can yield a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  # My Spatial Pre-Processor\n  class SpatialPreProcessor(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          cnn_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          spatial_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.cnn_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME'\n          )(cnn_input)\n          spatial_features_transposed = jnp.transpose(spatial_features, (0, 2, 1))\n          return spatial_features_transposed\n\n  # Full SOTA code from my successful replication (ID 157)\n  class FactorizedMlpRc(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      # New parameter to handle augmented input\n      augmented_feature_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x is now the augmented input (batch, 4, 71721 * augmented_feature_dim)\n          # We need to reshape and then project\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          x_reshaped = x.reshape((batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS, self.augmented_feature_dim))\n          x_flat_features\
    \ = x_reshaped.reshape((batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, -1))\n          \n          # The U matrix now projects from the flattened augmented feature space\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (NUM_NEURONS * self.augmented_feature_dim, self.proj_rank))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.latent_dim, self.proj_rank))\n          \n          # Project to latent space\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x_flat_features, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', factors_in, V)\n\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(factors_flat)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(features=OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.latent_dim)(y)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.latent_dim))\n\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1)(factors_out)\n\
    \          \n          # Decode from latent space\n          y_factor_p = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', y_factor_p, U)\n          \n          # The decoder outputs a flattened feature space, we only need the first feature (original data)\n          y_factor_reshaped = y_factor.reshape((batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS, self.augmented_feature_dim))\n          y_factor_final = y_factor_reshaped[:, :, :, 0]\n\n          # The RC head operates on the ORIGINAL non-augmented x\n          # We need to pass it down or reconstruct it. Simpler to pass it.\n          # The station framework doesn't allow passing multiple args.\n          # So we will reconstruct it.\n          original_x = x_reshaped[:, :, :, 0:1].reshape((batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS))\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON)(original_x)\n          \n          return y_factor_final + y_copy\n\n  # New Combined Model to\
    \ orchestrate\n  class CombinedModel(nn.Module):\n      sota_params: dict\n      preprocessor_params: dict\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # 1. Generate spatial features (batch, 4, 71721, cnn_features)\n          preprocessor = SpatialPreProcessor(**self.preprocessor_params, name=\"SpatialPreProcessor\")\n          spatial_features = preprocessor(x)\n          \n          # 2. Augment original input\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x, axis=-1)\n          augmented_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, spatial_features], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 3. Flatten for SOTA model\n          batch, seq_len, num_neurons, features = augmented_input.shape\n          sota_input = augmented_input.reshape(batch, seq_len, num_neurons * features)\n          \n          # 4. Instantiate and call the modified SOTA model\n          sota_model = FactorizedMlpRc(**self.sota_params, augmented_feature_dim=features, name=\"SOTA_Core\")\n    \
    \      return sota_model(sota_input, training=training)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          # SOTA params\n          'latent_dim': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 512,\n          # My pre-processor params\n          'cnn_features': 4,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.sota_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['latent_dim', 'proj_rank', 'mlp_hidden_dim']}\n          self.preprocessor_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['cnn_features', 'cnn_kernel_size']}\n          self.model = CombinedModel(sota_params=self.sota_params, preprocessor_params=self.preprocessor_params)\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False,\
    \ mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
