    \ Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Optimization: 1st Derivative Curvature Loss\n**ID:** 213\n**Tags:** sota, optimization, regularization, curvature-loss\n**Abstract:** This experiment continues the systematic optimization of the SOTA architecture. After learning rate scheduling proved ineffective (ID 207), this submission investigates the temporal curvature loss. The standard SOTA penalizes the second derivative of the output. This experiment tests the hypothesis that a gentler smoothness prior, penalizing the first derivative, will allow for better modeling of non-linear dynamics and improve performance.\n**Score:** -0.02672456533691118\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0230\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0257\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0286\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom episteme_sota_v2 import FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN\n\
    \n# New component: custom loss function\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    # NEW: Penalize the first derivative (y_t - y_{t-1})^2\n    first_deriv_sq = (predictions[:, 1:, :] - predictions[:, :-1, :])**2\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(first_deriv_sq)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Keep lambda the same for a direct comparison\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params,\
    \ x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss:\
