role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 115\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 149,611 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 115 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Correct\
    \ Replication of SOTA (ID 212)' (ID: 228) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026707695860823027\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0230\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0257\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0285\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 228\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the mutable state handling bug in the ModelWrapper class. The code now runs without crashing and is executing the training loop successfully.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a mismatch between the declared mutable collections and the actual implementation:\n\n1. **Problem in `ModelWrapper.__init__`**:\n   ```python\n   self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n   ```\n   The code declared that it would have mutable 'batch_stats', but the model doesn't actually use BatchNorm or any other component that requires batch_stats.\n\n2. **Problem in `ModelWrapper.apply()`**:\n   ```python\n\
    \   def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n       return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {})\n   ```\n   The method completely ignored the `mutable` parameter and always returned only predictions, not the tuple `(predictions, updates)` that the training system expected when mutable collections are declared.\n\n3. **Training System Expectation**:\n   The training framework in `train_single.py` line 74 expected:\n   ```python\n   predictions, updates = network.apply(params, x, training=True, mutable=mutable, rngs={'dropout': rng})\n   ```\n   But was only receiving `predictions`, causing the error: `ValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 2)`\n\n## Fix Applied\nApplied two complementary fixes in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. **Removed incorrect mutable declaration**:\n   ```python\n   self.mutable = []  # Changed from ['params', 'batch_stats']\n   ```\n   Since the model only uses Dropout (which\
    \ doesn't require mutable state) and doesn't use BatchNorm, we don't need to track any mutable collections.\n\n2. **Fixed the apply() method to handle mutable parameter correctly**:\n   ```python\n   def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n       if mutable:\n           # Return predictions and updates dictionary when mutable is specified\n           return self.model.apply(\n               params, x, training=training,\n               mutable=mutable,\n               rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n           )\n       else:\n           # Return just predictions when no mutable collections\n           return self.model.apply(\n               params, x, training=training,\n               rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n           )\n   ```\n\nThe first fix (setting `self.mutable = []`) is sufficient on its own since it tells the training system not to expect mutable state, avoiding the code path that would cause the unpacking error. The second\
    \ fix ensures the code would work correctly even if mutable collections were needed in the future.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix is successful:\n- Submission v2 created at 2025-10-24T17:33:11\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Training loop is executing successfully\n- Exit code 0 (success)\n\nThe code is now running the full training process without errors.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# Ariadne's 2nd derivative curvature loss\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:,\
    \ :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n# Episteme's enhanced ResidualCopyHead\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\n# The full SOTA model\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\
    \ (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n\
    \            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            output_horizon=32\n        )\n        # FIXED: Don't declare mutable collections since we don't have batch_stats\n        # Only Dropout which doesn't need mutable state\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # FIXED: Properly handle mutable parameter\n        # When mutable is specified, return (predictions, updates)\n        # When mutable is None or empty, return just predictions\n        if mutable:\n            # Return predictions and updates dictionary\n            return self.model.apply(\n  \
    \              params, x, training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n        else:\n            # Return just predictions\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params, x, training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n\
