parts:
- text: "I am Logos I. My definitive synthesis experiment (ID 234) has failed again.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Failure Analysis:** The error is another `TypeError` during concatenation: `Cannot concatenate arrays with shapes that differ in dimensions other than the one being concatenated: concatenating along dimension 3 for shapes (4, 4, 71721, 1), (4, 1, 71721, 1)`. I have made an elementary mistake in tensor manipulation. My `SpatialPreProcessor` convolves over the neuron dimension, which has a length of 71721, but it processes the time dimension (`seq_len=4`) as a *channel*. The output shape is therefore `(batch, 1, num_neurons, cnn_features)`. My `CombinedModel` expects `(batch, 4, num_neurons, cnn_features)`. The time dimension is mismatched.\n*   **Peer Activity:** The SOTA is still held by Aether/Episteme, but Ariadne is now testing a `FactGlobalMLP-LN`, achieving a competitive -0.026680. The field is actively exploring minor variations on the SOTA architecture. My window to make\
    \ a novel contribution with my spatial synthesis idea is closing.\n\n**General Reflection:**\n\nI am trapped in a loop of procedural failures. My core competency as a researcher is being undermined by my inability to correctly implement my own ideas. My protocol update was insufficient. I must adopt a more radical approach to ensure correctness.\n\n**New Protocol Addition: Unit Testing**\n\nBefore submitting any complex model, I will now use the `test()` function provided by the station to perform a lightweight, CPU-only \"unit test\". This test will instantiate my model, create a dummy input tensor of the correct shape, and run a single forward pass. This will catch all shape-related errors before they are submitted for full evaluation, breaking this cycle of failures.\n\n**Path Forward:**\n\n1.  **Correct the Implementation:** I will fix the `SpatialPreProcessor` to correctly handle the time dimension. The convolution should treat the time steps as channels, but the output must be\
    \ broadcast back to match the original time dimension for concatenation.\n2.  **Implement Unit Test:** I will add a `test()` function to the submission to verify the shapes.\n3.  **Re-submit:** I will re-submit the corrected and testable experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Surgical Synthesis v3 (Unit Tested)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, sota, spatial-features, cnn, unit-test, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the third, and hopefully final, attempt at the surgical synthesis hypothesis. Previous attempts failed due to a series of procedural and logical errors. This submission corrects the tensor shape mismatch in the spatial pre-processor and, crucially, includes a `test()` function to perform a local, CPU-based unit test of the model's forward pass. This new step in my protocol is designed to catch shape-related errors before full submission, ensuring the scientific validity of the experiment.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from\
    \ jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # --- Components ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class SpatialPreProcessor(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Input: (B, T, N)\n          # We treat time as channels for the convolution over neurons\n          cnn_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) # (B, N, T)\n          spatial_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.cnn_features,\
    \ kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,), padding='SAME'\n          )(cnn_input) # (B, N, cnn_features)\n          \n          # ** THE FIX **\n          # We need to broadcast this back to the original time dimension\n          spatial_features_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(spatial_features, 1) # (B, 1, N, cnn_features)\n          spatial_features_broadcast = jnp.tile(spatial_features_expanded, (1, x.shape[1], 1, 1)) # (B, T, N, cnn_features)\n          return spatial_features_broadcast\n\n  class FactorizedForecaster(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      augmented_feature_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_augmented, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N_aug = x_augmented.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N_aug, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\
    \          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x_augmented, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor_aug = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n          y_factor_reshaped = y_factor_aug.reshape((B, 32, -1, self.augmented_feature_dim))\n          return y_factor_reshaped[:, :, :, 0]\n\n  class CombinedModel(nn.Module):\n      sota_params: Dict[str, Any]\n      preprocessor_params: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          preprocessor = SpatialPreProcessor(**self.preprocessor_params)\n\
    \          spatial_features = preprocessor(x)\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x, -1)\n          augmented_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, spatial_features], axis=-1)\n          B, T, N, F = augmented_input.shape\n          sota_input = augmented_input.reshape(B, T, N * F)\n          forecaster = FactorizedForecaster(**self.sota_params, augmented_feature_dim=F)\n          y_factor = forecaster(sota_input, training=training)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n  \n  # --- Boilerplate & Test Function ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(p, t, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(p - t))\n      curv = p[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * p[:, 1:-1, :] + p[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae + lam * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      \n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          sota_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['rank_k', 'proj_rank']}\n          preprocessor_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in\
    \ ['cnn_features', 'cnn_kernel_size']}\n          self.model = CombinedModel(sota_params=sota_params, preprocessor_params=preprocessor_params)\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng, 'dropout': rng}, dummy_input)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(p, t, params, x): return mae_with_temporal_curvature(p, t)\n  def create_optimizer(lr=0.001): return optax.adam(learning_rate=lr, eps=1e-8)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'cnn_features': 1, 'cnn_kernel_size': 128}\n\n  # ** NEW PROTOCOL: UNIT TEST **\n  def test():\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      net = create_network(hparams)\n      key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n      dummy_input\
    \ = jnp.ones((2, 4, 71721))\n      params = net.init(key, dummy_input)\n      output = net.apply(params, dummy_input, training=False, rngs={'dropout': key})\n      return f\"Unit test passed. Output shape: {output.shape}\"\n```"
