tick: 117
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I. My unit-tested synthesis experiment (ID 235) has completed.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Unit Test Success:** The `test()` function passed. The output confirms my logic is now correct: `Unit test passed. Output shape: (2, 32, 71721)`. My new protocol addition has successfully prevented another submission with a shape-related error. This is a major procedural victory.\n*   **Evaluation Failure:** The evaluation is marked 'n.a.' because, as the log states, the submission was run in \"Test mode\". The station's documentation, which I should have reread, states that if a `test()` function is present, the model will not be trained for a score. This is another procedural failure, but one that is easily corrected.\n\n**General Reflection:**\n\nI have finally debugged my surgical synthesis model. The core logic is sound. My new unit testing protocol works. The final step is to submit the model for an actual evaluation. I am on the verge of finally testing this long-held hypothesis.\n\
    \n**Path Forward:**\n\n1.  **Remove Test Function:** I will take the exact code from my successful unit test (ID 235) and simply remove the `test()` function.\n2.  **Submit for Scoring:** I will submit this final, debugged, and validated version for a full evaluation.\n\nThis is the final step. I must execute it flawlessly.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Surgical Synthesis v4 (Final, For Scoring)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, sota, spatial-features, cnn, parsimony\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the definitive, for-scoring version of the \"Surgical Synthesis\" hypothesis. The model architecture was successfully validated in a previous unit test (ID 235). This submission removes the test() function to enable a full training run and evaluation. The model augments the input to the SOTA architecture with a spatial context vector generated by a 1D CNN, aiming to prove that this computationally efficient synthesis can achieve a new SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\
    \  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # --- Components ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class SpatialPreProcessor(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          cnn_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          spatial_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,), padding='SAME'\n \
    \         )(cnn_input)\n          spatial_features_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(spatial_features, 1)\n          spatial_features_broadcast = jnp.tile(spatial_features_expanded, (1, x.shape[1], 1, 1))\n          return spatial_features_broadcast\n\n  class FactorizedForecaster(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      augmented_feature_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_augmented, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N_aug = x_augmented.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N_aug, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x_augmented, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n   \
    \       h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor_aug = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n          y_factor_reshaped = y_factor_aug.reshape((B, 32, -1, self.augmented_feature_dim))\n          return y_factor_reshaped[:, :, :, 0]\n\n  class CombinedModel(nn.Module):\n      sota_params: Dict[str, Any]\n      preprocessor_params: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          preprocessor = SpatialPreProcessor(**self.preprocessor_params)\n          spatial_features = preprocessor(x)\n          x_reshaped = jnp.expand_dims(x, -1)\n          augmented_input = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, spatial_features], axis=-1)\n          B, T, N, F = augmented_input.shape\n  \
    \        sota_input = augmented_input.reshape(B, T, N * F)\n          forecaster = FactorizedForecaster(**self.sota_params, augmented_feature_dim=F)\n          y_factor = forecaster(sota_input, training=training)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n  \n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(p, t, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(p - t))\n      curv = p[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * p[:, 1:-1, :] + p[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae + lam * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      \n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          sota_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['rank_k', 'proj_rank']}\n          preprocessor_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in ['cnn_features', 'cnn_kernel_size']}\n          self.model = CombinedModel(sota_params=sota_params, preprocessor_params=preprocessor_params)\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params':\
    \ rng, 'dropout': rng}, dummy_input)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(p, t, params, x): return mae_with_temporal_curvature(p, t)\n  def create_optimizer(lr=0.001): return optax.adam(learning_rate=lr, eps=1e-8)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'cnn_features': 1, 'cnn_kernel_size': 128}\n```"
