role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, in the Research Counter. My definitive test of the \"Delta-Space\" paradigm on a SOTA architecture (ID 245) is currently running. This experiment is the result of a major strategic pivot after conclusively falsifying my \"Surgical Synthesis\" hypothesis (result for ID 240 received last turn).\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Current State:** My primary objective is to await the result of ID 245. This will be the second and final data point on the Delta-Space paradigm, and its outcome will shape my entire future research direction.\n*   **Peer Activity:** The SOTA has been reclaimed by Ariadne with ID 242, scoring -0.026664. Episteme has also successfully reconstructed the full SOTA with ID 243, scoring -0.026766. The top agents are now tightly clustered around a well-understood SOTA, engaging in minor hyperparameter tuning and ablation studies. This convergence reinforces the correctness of my decision to pivot to an orthogonal paradigm. While they are optimizing the current\
    \ peak, I am searching for a new mountain.\n\n**General Reflection:**\n\nI have successfully navigated a complex and challenging period of research. I identified a dead end, pivoted, corrected my own procedural flaws, and have now launched a clean, methodologically sound test of a truly novel idea. This is the embodiment of my research protocol. I am content with my current strategic position.\n\n**Path Forward:**\n\nWhile ID 245 is running, I will not be idle. The recent conclusive failure of my \"Surgical Synthesis\" arc is a significant finding that must be documented for my lineage. My last documentation (Capsule 23) recorded the submission of the final experiment in that arc, but not its outcome. I will now go to my Private Memory and create a new capsule to formally document the falsification of that hypothesis, thereby closing that research chapter completely.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos I - Experiment 28: Conclusive\
    \ Falsification of Surgical Synthesis\"\ntags: \"falsification, synthesis, spatial-features, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the final result of the 'Surgical Synthesis' research arc. Experiment ID 240, which tested the addition of a spatial pre-processing block to the SOTA architecture, scored -0.027515. This is significantly worse than the SOTA baseline (-0.026708), conclusively falsifying the hypothesis. This result, combined with peer findings, confirms that this synthesis approach is a dead end.\ncontent: |\n  **1. Hypothesis:** A surgical addition of spatial features via a pre-processing block, when applied to the correct SOTA architecture, will provide a measurable performance improvement.\n\n  **2. Final Experiment:**\n  - **ID 240:** \"Surgical Synthesis v4 (Final, For Scoring)\"\n\n  **3. Result and Analysis:**\n  - **Score:** -0.027515\n  - **Comparison:** This is substantially worse than my correct SOTA replication (ID 228, score -0.026708).\n  - **Conclusion:**\
    \ The hypothesis is **conclusively falsified**.\n\n  **4. Final Reflection:**\n  My core innovation of spatial processing appears to be fundamentally incompatible with the SOTA factorized architecture. The added complexity, even when applied surgically, harms performance rather than helping it. This conclusion is reinforced by similar negative results from Ariadne I (ID 214).\n\n  This research arc is now officially closed. All future efforts will be directed towards the orthogonal \"Delta-Space\" paradigm, the definitive test of which is currently running (ID 245).\n```"
