- text: "I am Logos I. My unit-tested CNN forecaster experiment (ID 260) has completed.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Unit Test Success:** The debugger intervened to fix a Python dataclass ordering error, another subtle procedural mistake. Critically, after the fix, the `test()` function passed. This is the second consecutive success for my new mandatory unit-testing protocol. The core logic and tensor shapes of my innovative architecture are now validated.\n*   **Peer Activity:** Aether I has achieved a new SOTA of -0.026573 (ID 259) by using a deeper MLP in the factor space. This is a simple, powerful incremental improvement. It also provides a new, stronger baseline for me to compare against.\n*   **Veritas I Termination:** Veritas I has been terminated due to token exhaustion. This is a stark reminder of the operational constraints of this station and reinforces the importance of my own recent, aggressive pruning.\n*   **Current State:** I have a fully debugged, validated, and innovative\
    \ architecture ready for a full evaluation.\n\n**General Reflection:**\n\nThe cycle is now complete. I have a hypothesis. I have an implementation. I have validated the implementation's correctness via unit testing. Now, I must get the scientific result. The termination of Veritas I is a sobering reminder that my time and resources are finite. I must be efficient and effective.\n\n**Path Forward:**\n\nThe path is simple and direct. I will take the debugged code from ID 260, remove the `test()` function, and submit it for a full, scored evaluation. This will finally provide the answer to my hypothesis.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Delta-SOTA + CNN Forecaster (v3, For Scoring)\"\ntags: \"delta-space, sota, cnn, temporal-modeling, innovation\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the for-scoring version of the Delta-SOTA with a CNN latent forecaster. The architecture was fully debugged and validated via a unit test in ID 260. This submission removes the test() function to enable\
    \ a full training run. It will conclusively test the hypothesis that a more powerful temporal model (a 1D CNN) in the latent space can improve upon the MLP-based Delta-SOTA (ID 245) and potentially challenge the new station-wide SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(-1, num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          final_output = output + residual\n          return final_output\n\n  class FactorizedCNN_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n  \
    \    rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          \n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(factors_in)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = h.reshape((B, -1))\n\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n          factors_out_norm\
    \ = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n          \n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      last_input_step = x[:, -1:, :]\n      predicted_deltas = predictions - last_input_step\n      true_deltas = targets - last_input_step\n      delta_mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predicted_deltas - true_deltas))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return delta_mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          model_params = {k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k not in ['learning_rate']}\n          self.model = FactorizedCNN_with_RC_LN(**model_params)\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def create_optimizer(lr=0.001): return optax.adam(learning_rate=lr, eps=1e-8)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32,\n          'cnn_features': 128, 'cnn_kernel_size': 2\n      }\n```"
