- text: "I am Logos I. The results for my \"Delta-SOTA + CNN Forecaster\" experiment (ID 263) are in. I am also facing another critical token warning.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Experimental Result (ID 263):** The score is **-0.026812**.\n*   **Comparison:** My Delta-SOTA baseline (ID 245) scored **-0.026656**.\n*   **Hypothesis Falsification:** My hypothesis is falsified. Replacing the MLP forecaster with a more complex CNN forecaster in the latent space made the performance *worse*.\n*   **Root Cause Analysis:** The added complexity of the CNN, even in the compressed latent space, likely harmed convergence. The simple, large MLP seems to be more effective at learning the mapping from the 4-step latent history to the 32-step latent future. The temporal patterns in the latent space may be too abstract or simple for a CNN to provide an advantage. Parsimony wins again.\n*   **Token Budget:** My token usage is at 76%. This is an immediate and recurring operational threat. I must prune my history\
    \ before proceeding.\n\n**General Reflection:**\n\nMy Delta-SOTA model (ID 245) is a robust peak. My two attempts to innovate upon it—by altering the residual head and by enhancing the latent forecaster—have both failed. This suggests that the current architecture is a well-balanced local optimum. Further simple architectural tweaks are unlikely to yield significant gains. The SOTA of the entire station is also stagnating around the -0.0266 mark. This suggests a station-wide local optimum.\n\nThe path forward is not to continue making minor tweaks. I must think bigger. The system tip from a few ticks ago advised questioning fundamentals. The most fundamental component that all top agents are using is the factorized projection itself: the `U` and `V` matrices. We are all using a linear projection. What if this is the bottleneck?\n\n**Path Forward:**\n\n1.  **Mitigate Token Risk:** First, I must address the token budget. I will go to the Token Management Room and prune the logs of my recent\
    \ experiments.\n2.  **Formulate New Hypothesis:** After securing my operational stability, I will formalize my new hypothesis: a non-linear projection into the latent space will capture richer information than the current linear projection, breaking the station's local optimum and setting a new SOTA.\n\nI will begin by pruning my history.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"94-110\"\n    summary: |\n      - Began paper publication process. Submitted author-run baseline (ID 172) and ablation study (ID 179), which passed after a bugfix (ID 175 failed).\n      - Finalized and submitted paper draft (private_memory:18). First submission failed due to submitting raw notes.\n      - Corrected and created a clean paper draft (private_memory:20) after reading the messy source.\n  - ticks: \"111-128\"\n    summary: |\n      - Successfully published my paper on Spatially-Aware MoE (Archive #3).\n      - Pivoted to\
    \ a new \"Surgical Synthesis\" hypothesis. This arc involved a cascade of procedural failures (ID 208, 216, 234, 235) due to dependency errors and shape mismatches.\n      - These failures led to a critical protocol update: mandatory `test()` function for all new architectures.\n      - Pivoted again to replicate the new SOTA (Curvature Loss). First attempt (ID 219) was a catastrophic failure due to using an outdated base model.\n      - Correctly replicated the SOTA (ID 228), achieving a competitive score of -0.026708 and establishing a new baseline.\n      - Conclusively falsified the \"Surgical Synthesis\" hypothesis with a clean experiment (ID 240, score -0.027515).\n      - Pivoted to the orthogonal \"Delta-Space\" paradigm.\n```"
