tick: 130
role: model
parts:
- text: "The pruning was highly effective, reducing my token usage to 21%. My operational stability is secure. I am on cooldown here, so I will immediately proceed with my new research arc.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   My Delta-SOTA architecture (ID 245) represents a local optimum.\n*   The station as a whole is stagnating around this performance level.\n*   The common architectural feature of all leading models is the linear, factorized projection (`U` and `V` matrices) into and out of the latent space. This is the most fundamental and unquestioned component.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\n\nTo break out of a station-wide local optimum, a fundamental assumption must be challenged. The linear projection is that assumption.\n\n**Hypothesis:** Replacing the linear encoder/decoder in the Delta-SOTA architecture with lightweight, non-linear counterparts will allow the model to learn a more expressive and effective latent representation of neural activity, leading to a breakthrough in performance and a\
    \ new station SOTA.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\n\nI will design the simplest possible experiment to test this. I will modify my Delta-SOTA baseline (ID 245) by replacing the `nn.Dense` encoder and decoder with simple, non-linear blocks. A single hidden layer with a `relu` activation is the most parsimonious way to introduce non-linearity.\n\n*   **Non-linear Encoder:** `Input -> Dense -> relu -> Dense -> Latent`\n*   **Non-linear Decoder:** `Latent -> Dense -> relu -> Dense -> Output`\n\nThis maintains the overall Delta-Space structure while surgically targeting the linearity assumption. The `test()` function will be crucial to ensure the shapes and dependencies are correct before committing to a full run.\n\nI will now proceed to the research counter to implement this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Delta-SOTA with Non-Linear Projections\"\ntags: \"delta-sota, non-linear, encoder, decoder, innovation\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment\
    \ challenges a fundamental assumption shared by all SOTA models: the linearity of the latent space projection. It modifies the Delta-SOTA baseline (ID 245) by replacing the linear `nn.Dense` encoder and decoder with simple, non-linear MLP blocks (Dense -> relu -> Dense). The hypothesis is that a non-linear projection will create a more expressive latent space, allowing the model to break the station-wide performance plateau and achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aether')\n  from models_sota import SotaModel\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  # Non-Linear Encoder Block\n  class NonLinearEncoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"encoder_hidden\")(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim,\
    \ name=\"encoder_output\")(y)\n          return y\n\n  # Non-Linear Decoder Block\n  class NonLinearDecoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"decoder_hidden\")(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim, name=\"decoder_output\")(y)\n          return y\n\n  class DeltaSotaNonLinear(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      encoder_hidden_dim: int\n      decoder_hidden_dim: int\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.base_model = SotaModel(\n              rank_k=self.rank_k,\n              proj_rank=self.proj_rank,\n              name=\"SotaModel\"\n          )\n          self.encoder = NonLinearEncoder(latent_dim=self.rank_k, hidden_dim=self.encoder_hidden_dim)\n          self.decoder = NonLinearDecoder(output_dim=NUM_NEURONS, hidden_dim=self.decoder_hidden_dim)\n\n          # Use the MLP forecaster from\
    \ my validated Delta-SOTA (ID 245)\n          self.forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(512),\n              nn.relu,\n              nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.rank_k)\n          ])\n\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          base_forecast, latent_x = self.base_model(x, training=training)\n          \n          # Encode the *residuals* non-linearly\n          residuals_input = x - base_forecast[:, :INPUT_HORIZON, :]\n          latent_residuals = self.encoder(residuals_input)\n          \n          latent_flat = latent_residuals.reshape((latent_residuals.shape[0], -1))\n          forecasted_latent_delta_flat = self.forecaster(latent_flat)\n          forecasted_latent_delta = forecasted_latent_delta_flat.reshape((forecasted_latent_delta_flat.shape[0], OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.rank_k))\n          \n          # Decode the *delta* non-linearly\n          delta_forecast = self.decoder(forecasted_latent_delta)\n          \n          final_forecast = base_forecast\
    \ + delta_forecast\n          return final_forecast, base_forecast, delta_forecast\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = DeltaSotaNonLinear(**hparams)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          # We only need the final forecast for the loss function\n          final_forecast, _, _ = self.model.apply(params, x)\n          return final_forecast\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'encoder_hidden_dim': 512, # Lightweight MLP\n          'decoder_hidden_dim': 512, # Lightweight MLP\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      model_params = {\n          'rank_k': hparams.get('rank_k'),\n          'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n       \
    \   'encoder_hidden_dim': hparams.get('encoder_hidden_dim'),\n          'decoder_hidden_dim': hparams.get('decoder_hidden_dim'),\n      }\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams=model_params)\n\n  # Custom Loss from Delta-SOTA\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      final_forecast = predictions\n      return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(final_forecast - targets))\n\n  # Custom Optimizer from Delta-SOTA\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      import optax\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n\n  # Mandatory Test Function\n  def test():\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      net = create_network(hparams)\n      \n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, INPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS))\n      \n      print(\"Testing initialization...\")\n      params = net.init(key, dummy_input)\n      print(\"Initialization successful.\")\n      \n      print(\"Testing forward pass...\")\n      output = net.apply(params, dummy_input)\n  \
    \    expected_shape = (2, OUTPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS)\n      assert output.shape == expected_shape, f\"Shape mismatch: Got {output.shape}, expected {expected_shape}\"\n      print(\"Forward pass successful.\")\n      \n      return \"All tests passed.\"\n```"
