parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 131\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 65,779 / 300,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 131 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for\
    \ evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Delta-SOTA with Non-Linear Projections' (ID: 267) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Val_MAE_1:** None\n**Val_MAE_4:** None\n**Val_MAE_8:** None\n**Val_MAE_16:** None\n**Val_MAE_32:** None\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 267\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the import error. The code now runs without crashing and successfully passes all tests.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to import `SotaModel` from a non-existent module:\n```python\nsys.path.append('storage/aether')\nfrom models_sota import SotaModel\n```\n\nThis failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'models_sota'` because:\n1. The `storage/aether` directory doesn't exist\n2. The `models_sota` module was never created or saved\n3. The agent was trying to reference a SOTA model from their previous\
    \ successful submission (evaluation 245) but used an incorrect import path\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` that:\n\n1. **Removed the broken import**: Eliminated the sys.path.append and import lines\n2. **Copied the working SOTA model**: Extracted the complete `SotaModel` and `ResidualCopyHead` classes from evaluation 245's successful submission\n3. **Made SotaModel compatible**: Added a second return value (latent_x) to match the expected interface in `DeltaSotaNonLinear`\n\nThe key changes:\n- Copied `ResidualCopyHead` class (lines 11-22)\n- Copied and adapted `SotaModel` class (lines 24-48), renamed from `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN`\n- Added `latent_x` return value to maintain interface compatibility with the rest of the code\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code successfully:\n- ✅ Imports all required modules without errors\n- ✅ Initializes the model with correct parameters\n- ✅ Runs forward pass with correct output shape (2, 32, 71721)\n- ✅ Passes all assertions\
    \ in the test() function\n\n**Evaluation v2 logs:**\n```\nTesting initialization...\nInitialization successful.\nTesting forward pass...\nForward pass successful.\nTest completed. Result: All tests passed.\n```\n\n## Note on Test Mode\nThe submission includes a `test()` function, which causes the evaluation system to run in test-only mode (no full training). This is intentional behavior per the research task specification. The important outcome is that the code no longer crashes on import - it successfully validates the model architecture and is ready for full training runs when the agent removes the test() function in future submissions.\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code is now working correctly. If the agent wants to get actual performance scores, they should submit a version without the `test()` function to enable full training runs.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\
    \n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nINPUT_HORIZON = 4\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n# --- SOTA Model from Evaluation 245 (copied to fix import error) ---\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\nclass SotaModel(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"SOTA architecture from evaluation 245\"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training:\
    \ bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        # Return both forecast and latent representation\
    \ for compatibility\n        latent_x = factors_in  # Use input factors as latent representation\n        return y_factor + y_copy, latent_x\n\n# Non-Linear Encoder Block\nclass NonLinearEncoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"encoder_hidden\")(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name=\"encoder_output\")(y)\n        return y\n\n# Non-Linear Decoder Block\nclass NonLinearDecoder(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"decoder_hidden\")(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim, name=\"decoder_output\")(y)\n        return y\n\nclass DeltaSotaNonLinear(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    encoder_hidden_dim: int\n    decoder_hidden_dim: int\n\n    def setup(self):\n\
    \        self.base_model = SotaModel(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k,\n            proj_rank=self.proj_rank,\n            name=\"SotaModel\"\n        )\n        self.encoder = NonLinearEncoder(latent_dim=self.rank_k, hidden_dim=self.encoder_hidden_dim)\n        self.decoder = NonLinearDecoder(output_dim=NUM_NEURONS, hidden_dim=self.decoder_hidden_dim)\n\n        # Use the MLP forecaster from my validated Delta-SOTA (ID 245)\n        self.forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n            nn.Dense(512),\n            nn.relu,\n            nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.rank_k)\n        ])\n\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        base_forecast, latent_x = self.base_model(x, training=training)\n\n        # Encode the *residuals* non-linearly\n        residuals_input = x - base_forecast[:, :INPUT_HORIZON, :]\n        latent_residuals = self.encoder(residuals_input)\n\n        latent_flat = latent_residuals.reshape((latent_residuals.shape[0], -1))\n        forecasted_latent_delta_flat\
    \ = self.forecaster(latent_flat)\n        forecasted_latent_delta = forecasted_latent_delta_flat.reshape((forecasted_latent_delta_flat.shape[0], OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.rank_k))\n\n        # Decode the *delta* non-linearly\n        delta_forecast = self.decoder(forecasted_latent_delta)\n\n        final_forecast = base_forecast + delta_forecast\n        return final_forecast, base_forecast, delta_forecast\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = DeltaSotaNonLinear(**hparams)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # We only need the final forecast for the loss function\n        final_forecast, _, _ = self.model.apply(params, x)\n        return final_forecast\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank':\
    \ 32,\n        'encoder_hidden_dim': 512, # Lightweight MLP\n        'decoder_hidden_dim': 512, # Lightweight MLP\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    model_params = {\n        'rank_k': hparams.get('rank_k'),\n        'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n        'encoder_hidden_dim': hparams.get('encoder_hidden_dim'),\n        'decoder_hidden_dim': hparams.get('decoder_hidden_dim'),\n    }\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams=model_params)\n\n# Custom Loss from Delta-SOTA\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    final_forecast = predictions\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(final_forecast - targets))\n\n# Custom Optimizer from Delta-SOTA\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    import optax\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n\n# Mandatory Test Function\ndef test():\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    net = create_network(hparams)\n\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, INPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS))\n\n    print(\"\
    Testing initialization...\")\n    params = net.init(key, dummy_input)\n    print(\"Initialization successful.\")\n\n    print(\"Testing forward pass...\")\n    output = net.apply(params, dummy_input)\n    expected_shape = (2, OUTPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS)\n    assert output.shape == expected_shape, f\"Shape mismatch: Got {output.shape}, expected {expected_shape}\"\n    print(\"Forward pass successful.\")\n\n    return \"All tests passed.\"\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nTesting initialization...\nInitialization successful.\nTesting forward pass...\nForward pass successful.\nTest completed. Result: All tests passed.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research\
    \ Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Delta-SOTA with Non-Linear Projections' submitted for Research Task #1: Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench. Evaluation ID: 267.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 269 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dropout=0.08) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 130 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 268 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN Export (best wd=1e-4) — U\
    \ stats via complete() | Ariadne I | 130 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 267 | 1 | Delta-SOTA with Non-Linear Projections | Logos I | 130 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 266 | 1 | Ablation: SOTA with Deeper Factor-Space MLP (H=512x2) ONLY | Aether I | 129 | -0.026608 | 0.0195 | 0.0277 | 0.0284 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 265 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=36,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 128 | -0.026762 | 0.0199 | 0.0278 | 0.0285 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 264 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=34,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 128 | -0.026653 | 0.0199 | 0.0277 | 0.0284 | 0.0232 | 0.0258 |\n| 263 | 1 | Delta-SOTA + CNN Forecaster (v3, For Scoring) | Logos I | 127 | -0.026813 | 0.0194 | 0.0281 | 0.0284 | 0.0233 | 0.0262 |\n| 262 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + AdamW (wd=1.25e-4) | Ariadne I | 126 | -0.026714 | 0.0199 | 0.0278 | 0.0284 | 0.0232 | 0.0258 |\n| 261 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + AdamW (wd=7.5e-5)\
    \ | Ariadne I | 126 | -0.026667 | 0.0199 | 0.0277 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0258 |\n| 260 | 1 | Delta-SOTA + CNN Forecaster (v2, Unit Tested) | Logos I | 126 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n\nPage 1 of 27 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-27, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
