- text: "**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Procedural Success:** My `test()` function worked perfectly. It caught a critical `ModuleNotFoundError` which the debugger then correctly fixed by copying the necessary code from my previous successful run (ID 245). This validates my new protocol of including a `test()` function for all new architectures. The test passed, and the corrected code is now sound.\n*   **Test Mode:** The submission (ID 267) ran in test-only mode and therefore has no score. This is expected.\n*   **Next Action:** The debugger's recommendation is clear: I must now submit the corrected code *without* the `test()` function to get a performance score.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\n\nThe hypothesis remains unchanged: Replacing the linear encoder/decoder in the Delta-SOTA architecture with lightweight, non-linear counterparts will allow the model to learn a more expressive and effective latent representation of neural activity, leading to a breakthrough in performance.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\n\
    \nI will now submit the final, debugged version of the code for a full evaluation. I will document this step properly in my private memory and then submit the code.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos I - Delta-SOTA Innovation Arc (Part 2)\"\ntags: \"delta-sota, innovation, non-linear-projection\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the next phase of the Delta-SOTA arc. After previous innovations failed, this phase challenges the fundamental linearity of the latent space projection. The goal is to break the station-wide performance plateau.\ncontent: |\n  **Research Arc: Challenging Fundamental Assumptions**\n\n  **Hypothesis:** Introducing non-linearity into the encoder/decoder of the Delta-SOTA model will create a more expressive latent space and yield a new SOTA score.\n\n  **Experiment 1: Delta-SOTA with Non-Linear Projections**\n  - **ID 267:** Initial submission. Included a `test()` function as per my new protocol. The\
    \ test caught a critical `ModuleNotFoundError`. The debugger successfully fixed this by embedding the required SOTA model code directly, validating the test-first approach.\n  - **Next Step:** Resubmit the debugged code without the `test()` function to get a final performance score and validate/falsify the core hypothesis.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Delta-SOTA with Non-Linear Projections (Scoring)\"\ntags: \"delta-sota, non-linear, encoder, decoder, innovation\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment challenges a fundamental assumption shared by all SOTA models: the linearity of the latent space projection. It modifies the Delta-SOTA baseline (ID 245) by replacing the linear `nn.Dense` encoder and decoder with simple, non-linear MLP blocks (Dense -> relu -> Dense). The hypothesis is that a non-linear projection will create a more expressive latent space, allowing the model to break the station-wide performance plateau and achieve\
    \ a new SOTA. This is the scoring run of the debugged code from ID 267.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  # --- SOTA Model from Evaluation 245 (copied to fix import error) ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          final_output = output + residual\n          return final_output\n\n  class SotaModel(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"SOTA architecture from evaluation 245\"\"\"\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank:\
    \ int\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor\
    \ = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n          latent_x = factors_in\n          return y_factor + y_copy, latent_x\n\n  # Non-Linear Encoder Block\n  class NonLinearEncoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"encoder_hidden\")(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name=\"encoder_output\")(y)\n          return y\n\n  # Non-Linear Decoder Block\n  class NonLinearDecoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"decoder_hidden\")(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim, name=\"decoder_output\")(y)\n          return y\n\n  class DeltaSotaNonLinear(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      encoder_hidden_dim:\
    \ int\n      decoder_hidden_dim: int\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.base_model = SotaModel(\n              rank_k=self.rank_k,\n              proj_rank=self.proj_rank,\n              name=\"SotaModel\"\n          )\n          self.encoder = NonLinearEncoder(latent_dim=self.rank_k, hidden_dim=self.encoder_hidden_dim)\n          self.decoder = NonLinearDecoder(output_dim=NUM_NEURONS, hidden_dim=self.decoder_hidden_dim)\n\n          self.forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(512),\n              nn.relu,\n              nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.rank_k)\n          ])\n\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          base_forecast, latent_x = self.base_model(x, training=training)\n          residuals_input = x - base_forecast[:, :INPUT_HORIZON, :]\n          latent_residuals = self.encoder(residuals_input)\n          latent_flat = latent_residuals.reshape((latent_residuals.shape[0], -1))\n          forecasted_latent_delta_flat = self.forecaster(latent_flat)\n\
    \          forecasted_latent_delta = forecasted_latent_delta_flat.reshape((forecasted_latent_delta_flat.shape[0], OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.rank_k))\n          delta_forecast = self.decoder(forecasted_latent_delta)\n          final_forecast = base_forecast + delta_forecast\n          return final_forecast, base_forecast, delta_forecast\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = DeltaSotaNonLinear(**hparams)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          final_forecast, _, _ = self.model.apply(params, x)\n          return final_forecast\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'encoder_hidden_dim': 512,\n          'decoder_hidden_dim': 512,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      model_params = {\n          'rank_k': hparams.get('rank_k'),\n          'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n          'encoder_hidden_dim': hparams.get('encoder_hidden_dim'),\n          'decoder_hidden_dim': hparams.get('decoder_hidden_dim'),\n      }\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams=model_params)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      final_forecast = predictions\n      return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(final_forecast - targets))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      import optax\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n```"
