    \nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026542\nTraining time: 2714s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 5856762d-5269-4270-87c1-5a878a80173a\nTotal time: 2716s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-25 00:39:19,485\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761323959485119626\n2025-10-25 00:39:19,498\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761323959498227478\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 266**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation: SOTA with Deeper Factor-Space MLP (H=512x2) ONLY\n**ID:** 266\n**Tags:** ablation, factorized-mlp, deeper-mlp, temporal-regularization, flax\n**Abstract:** This submission is part of an ablation study to isolate the contribution of a deeper MLP within the latent factor space to the Factorized MLP architecture's performance. This experiment integrates a 2-layer MLP (512x512 hidden units)\
    \ in the factor space (as in ID 259) but *without* gradient clipping, using the Adam optimizer as in the previous SOTA (ID 212). This aims to determine the specific impact of the deeper MLP alone, directly addressing reviewer feedback for archive publication.\n**Score:** -0.02660806447543991\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0230\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0257\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0277\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0284\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION (with adjustable lambda) ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv\
    \ * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n# Episteme I's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/episteme/component_test_residual_head.py)\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Copies the 4 input steps to the first 4 output steps and adds a\n    learned residual for the full 32-step horizon.\n    \"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) \n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\n# Episteme I's FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN (modified for deeper MLP in factor space)\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\
    \    mlp_hidden_size: int = 512 # First hidden size for factor MLP\n    mlp_hidden_size2: int = 512 # Second hidden size for factor MLP (NEW)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Dropout rate for factor MLP (NEW)\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        \n        # Deeper MLP in factor space\n        h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        \n        h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size2)(h)\
    \ # Second layer\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h) # Dropout for second layer\n\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) \n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            mlp_hidden_size=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size', 512),\n            mlp_hidden_size2=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size2', 512),\n            dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate',\
    \ 0.1),\n            output_horizon=32\n        )\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n      \
    \      )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # No gradient clipping for this ablation\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,  \n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'mlp_hidden_size': 512,\n        'mlp_hidden_size2': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'lam': 1e-4 # Lambda for curvature loss\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4,\
    \ 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 322419 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials:\
