role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 137\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 109,073 / 300,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 137 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synthesis\
    \ SOTA v2 (Bugfix + Clipping)' (ID: 278) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02678065391417821\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0259\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0280\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0285\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 278\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a Flax RNG handling error that caused the model to crash during validation. The code now runs without crashing and is executing successfully.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an error in the `ModelWrapper.apply()` method when handling the dropout RNG parameter. The code was attempting to pass `{'dropout': None}` to Flax's `model.apply()` function when `training=False`:\n\n```python\n# Original buggy code (lines 39-41 in evaluation.yaml):\ndropout_rng = rngs['dropout'] if rngs and 'dropout' in rngs else None\nreturn self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs={'dropout': dropout_rng})\n\
    ```\n\nThe problem: Flax doesn't accept `None` as a value in the `rngs` dictionary. It expects either:\n- A valid `jax.PRNGKey` object, OR\n- No `rngs` parameter at all (when not using random operations)\n\nWhen `training=False` during validation, there was no valid dropout RNG, so `dropout_rng` became `None`. Passing `{'dropout': None}` to Flax caused a `ValueError`:\n\n```\nValueError: The ``rngs`` argument passed to an apply function should be a ``jax.PRNGKey``\nor a dictionary mapping strings to ``jax.PRNGKey``.\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `apply` method in `ModelWrapper` to conditionally pass the `rngs` parameter:\n\n```python\ndef apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n    # Fix: Only pass rngs if we have a valid dropout_rng\n    if rngs and 'dropout' in rngs:\n        dropout_rng = rngs['dropout']\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs={'dropout': dropout_rng})\n    else:\n        # When training=False and no valid\
    \ RNG, don't pass rngs parameter at all\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n```\n\nThe fix ensures that:\n1. When a valid dropout RNG is provided (during training), it's passed to the model\n2. When no valid RNG exists (during validation), the `rngs` parameter is omitted entirely\n3. Flax's dropout layers automatically use `deterministic=True` mode when no RNG is provided\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Code executed for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The validation phase now runs correctly\n- The model can proceed with training and evaluation\n\n## Changes Made\n- **File**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- **Lines Modified**: 74-79 (the `apply` method)\n- **Nature**: Bug fix for RNG handling in Flax model inference\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n\
    import flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nINPUT_HORIZON = 4\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\nclass SynthesizedSotaModel(nn.Module):\n\
    \    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n\n        h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B,\
    \ OUTPUT_HORIZON, k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = SynthesizedSotaModel(**hparams)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rngs = {'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}\n        return self.model.init(rngs, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # Fix: Only pass rngs if we have a valid dropout_rng\n        if rngs and 'dropout' in rngs:\n            dropout_rng = rngs['dropout']\n            return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs={'dropout': dropout_rng})\n        else:\n            # When training=False and no valid RNG, don't pass rngs parameter at all\n \
    \           return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'weight_decay': 1e-4,\n        'gradient_clip': 1.0,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'mlp_hidden_size': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    model_params = {\n        'rank_k': hparams.get('rank_k'),\n        'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n        'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size'),\n        'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n    }\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams=model_params)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    # AdamW Optimizer + Gradient Clipping (Synergistic Combo)\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams.get('gradient_clip',\
    \ 1.0)),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=hparams.get('weight_decay', 1e-4))\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n\
    \  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 330105 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 330107\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'weight_decay': 0.0001, 'gradient_clip': 1.0, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'mlp_hidden_size': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721)\
    \ [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030546   |   0.029492  \n   2    |   0.028914   |   0.029294  \n   3    |   0.028782   |   0.028975  \n   4    |   0.028420   |   0.028510  \n   5    |   0.027901   |   0.028275  \n   6    |   0.027468   |   0.027783  \n   7    |   0.027110   |   0.027941  \n   8    |   0.026621   |   0.027412  \n   9    |   0.026174   |   0.026921  \n  10    |   0.025835   |   0.027412  \n  11    |   0.025452   |   0.026773  \n  12    |   0.025171   |   0.026780  \n  13    |   0.024992   |   0.027019  \n  14    |   0.024793   |   0.026804  \n  15    |   0.024684   |   0.027036  \n  16    |   0.024531   |   0.027183  \n  17    |   0.024380   |   0.026737  \n  18    |   0.024321   |   0.026793  \n  19    |   0.024241   |   0.026798  \n  20    |   0.024119   |   0.026997  \n  21    |   0.024193   |   0.026820\
    \  \n  22    |   0.023999   |   0.026911  \n  23    |   0.023954   |   0.026767  \n  24    |   0.023934   |   0.027997  \n  25    |   0.023920   |   0.026989  \n  26    |   0.023857   |   0.026961  \n  27    |   0.023793   |   0.026806  \n  28    |   0.023817   |   0.026888  \n  29    |   0.023845   |   0.026844  \n  30    |   0.023698   |   0.026794  \n  31    |   0.023695   |   0.026819  \n  32    |   0.023762   |   0.026842  \n  33    |   0.023650   |   0.026977  \n  34    |   0.023666   |   0.027053  \n  35    |   0.023662   |   0.026911  \n  36    |   0.023596   |   0.026844  \n  37    |   0.023589   |   0.026872  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 37 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1712.7s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026737\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026737\nTraining time: 1722s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 330108\nHyperparameters:\
