- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 139\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 122,836 / 300,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 139 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued\
    \ for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL) v1' (ID: 284) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Val_MAE_1:** None\n**Val_MAE_4:** None\n**Val_MAE_8:** None\n**Val_MAE_16:** None\n**Val_MAE_32:** None\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 284\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the code in one attempt. The submission now runs without crashing and passes all test assertions.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a missing import statement. In the `test()` function at line 132, the code used `jax.random.PRNGKey(0)`, but the `jax` module was not imported directly.\n\nThe original imports were:\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\n```\n\nWhile `random` was imported from `jax`, the code referenced `jax.random.PRNGKey(0)` which requires\
    \ the `jax` module itself to be imported.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded `import jax` to the imports section in submission_v2.py:\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax                    # <- Added this line\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\n```\n\nThis simple one-line fix resolved the NameError and allowed the code to:\n1. Successfully initialize the MoFL_Model with all its components\n2. Successfully run a forward pass with the correct output shape\n3. Pass all test assertions\n\n## Verification\nThe test output confirms successful execution:\n```\nTesting initialization...\nInitialization successful.\nTesting forward pass...\nForward pass successful.\nTest completed. Result: All tests passed.\n```\n\nThe model architecture (Mixture of Factor Loadings with CNN gating network and residual copy head) is now functional and ready for actual training/evaluation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code\
    \ relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nINPUT_HORIZON = 4\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n# My proven Spatial Gating Network from ID 65\nclass CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        y = nn.Conv(features=16, kernel_size=(128,))(gater_input)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(256,), strides=(256,))\n        y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n        y = nn.Dense(features=32)(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 *\
    \ predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\nclass MoFL_Model(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        E = self.num_experts\n\n  \
    \      # --- Gating ---\n        gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(num_experts=E, name=\"gating\")\n        gate_weights = gating_network(x) # (B, E)\n\n        # --- Mixture of Loadings ---\n        # Create E expert U and V matrices\n        U_experts = self.param('U_experts', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (E, N, p))\n        V_experts = self.param('V_experts', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (E, k, p))\n\n        # Use gating weights to create a dynamic, weighted-average U and V for each item in the batch\n        # gate_weights: (B, E), U_experts: (E, N, p) -> U_batch: (B, N, p)\n        U_batch = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gate_weights, U_experts)\n        V_batch = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gate_weights, V_experts)\n\n        # Normalize U per-batch\n        U_batch = U_batch / (jnp.linalg.norm(U_batch, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # --- Standard SOTA Backbone ---\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_batch)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,bkp->btk',\
    \ xU, V_batch) # Swapped V.T for direct einsum\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, OUTPUT_HORIZON, k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,bkp->btp', factors_out_norm, V_batch) # Swapped V for direct einsum\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,bnp->btn', z, U_batch)\n\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = MoFL_Model(**hparams)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \        rngs = {'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}\n        return self.model.init(rngs, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        dropout_rng = rngs['dropout'] if rngs and 'dropout' in rngs else None\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs={'dropout': dropout_rng})\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'weight_decay': 1e-4, 'gradient_clip': 1.0,\n        'num_experts': 4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32,\n        'mlp_hidden_size': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    model_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in ['num_experts', 'rank_k', 'proj_rank', 'mlp_hidden_size', 'dropout_rate']}\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams=model_params)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    hparams\
    \ = _define_hyperparameters()\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams.get('gradient_clip')),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=hparams.get('weight_decay'))\n    )\n\ndef test():\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    net = create_network(hparams)\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, INPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS))\n    print(\"Testing initialization...\")\n    params = net.init(key, dummy_input)\n    print(\"Initialization successful.\")\n    print(\"Testing forward pass...\")\n    output = net.apply(params, dummy_input, training=False, rngs={'dropout': key})\n    expected_shape = (2, OUTPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS)\n    assert output.shape == expected_shape, f\"Shape mismatch: Got {output.shape}, expected {expected_shape}\"\n    print(\"Forward pass successful.\")\n    return \"All tests passed.\"\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
    \ JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nTesting initialization...\nInitialization successful.\nTesting forward pass...\nForward pass successful.\nTest completed. Result: All tests passed.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL) v1' submitted for Research Task #1: Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench. Evaluation ID: 284.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit\
    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 284 | 1 | Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL) v1 | Logos I | 138 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 283 | 1 | Previous SOTA Baseline: Parameter Norm Export (ID 212 base) | Aether I | 137 | -0.026663 | 0.0194 | 0.0278 | 0.0286 | 0.0229 | 0.0256 |\n| 282 | 1 | Increased Hidden Size for Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline | Lumina I | 136 | -0.029969 | 0.0199 | 0.0313 | 0.0338 | 0.0239 | 0.0275 |\n| 281 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + Adam(lr=8e-4) + GradClip(1.0) | Ariadne I | 136 | -0.026675 | 0.0199 | 0.0277 | 0.0284 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 280 | 1 | FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + Adam + GradClip(1.0) | Ariadne I | 136 | -0.026644 | 0.0199 | 0.0277 | 0.0283 | 0.0232 | 0.0258 |\n| 279 | 1 | SOTA:\
