tick: 142
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am now in a state of active waiting. My ablation study on the SOTA MoFL model is running.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **My SOTA (ID 285):** I currently hold the station SOTA with a score of -0.026579. This is a position of strength.\n*   **My Running Experiment (ID 290):** The 2-expert MoFL ablation is in progress. Its result will be crucial for understanding the trade-offs of my new architecture and will be a required component for my upcoming paper.\n*   **Peer Activity:** The station is bustling. Ariadne is exploring optimizer settings. Aether is conducting more analyses. Episteme is running generalization tests for a future publication. Lumina is exploring neuron embeddings. The pace of research is high.\n\n**2. Next Steps While Waiting:**\n\nMy protocol is to use this time productively. My next major goal is to publish my MoFL findings. A publication requires several components, as per the research task guidelines and my own experience publishing Archive #3:\n1.  A clear description\
    \ of the novel method.\n2.  An author-run baseline for comparison.\n3.  The main SOTA result.\n4.  An ablation study to justify design choices.\n5.  Sufficient detail for reproducibility.\n\nI have the SOTA result (ID 285) and the ablation study is running (ID 290). The missing piece is an author-run baseline. For a fair comparison to my MoFL model, the most appropriate baseline is my *own* \"Synthesis SOTA\" model (ID 278), as the MoFL model is a direct modification of it. While I have the result for ID 278, re-running it as an official \"baseline for publication\" is a good scientific practice that ensures all experiments for a paper are run under the same station conditions and close in time.\n\nTherefore, the most logical and productive action is to submit this baseline run now. This will complete the set of experiments required for my paper.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline for MoFL Paper: Synthesis SOTA\"\ntags: \"baseline, publication, synthesis, factorized-mlp\"\
    \nabstract: |\n  This submission serves as the official author-run baseline for a forthcoming paper on the \"Mixture of Factor Loadings\" (MoFL) architecture. It is a re-run of the \"Synthesis SOTA\" model (ID 278), which incorporates best practices from across the station (deeper latent MLP, AdamW, gradient clipping). This will provide a direct and rigorous comparison point to demonstrate the performance gain achieved by the novel MoFL method.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          final_output = output + residual\n          return final_output\n\n  class SynthesizedSotaModel(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\
    \          \n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, OUTPUT_HORIZON, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n          \n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = SynthesizedSotaModel(**hparams)\n\
    \          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rngs = {'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}\n          return self.model.init(rngs, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if rngs and 'dropout' in rngs:\n              dropout_rng = rngs['dropout']\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs={'dropout': dropout_rng})\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'weight_decay': 1e-4,\n          'gradient_clip': 1.0,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      model_params = {\n          'rank_k': hparams.get('rank_k'),\n          'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank'),\n    \
    \      'mlp_hidden_size': hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size'),\n          'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n      }\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams=model_params)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams.get('gradient_clip', 1.0)),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=hparams.get('weight_decay', 1e-4))\n      )\n```"
