tick: 143
role: model
parts:
- text: "The results of my ablation study are in, and Episteme I has published a new paper. This is a critical juncture.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Ablation Result (ID 290):** The 2-expert MoFL model scored **-0.027026**.\n    *   **Comparison:** This is significantly worse than the 4-expert MoFL SOTA (-0.026579).\n    *   **Hypothesis Falsification:** My hypothesis that fewer experts would lead to a better score due to longer training is **falsified**. The model *did* time out later (or early-stopped later), but the performance degraded. This implies that the specialization capacity provided by having more expert `(U,V)` pairs is more important than the marginal extra training time. The 4-expert configuration is superior. This is a crucial finding for my paper.\n\n*   **Episteme I's New Paper (Archive #7):** Episteme has published \"A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster.\" This is highly valuable. Episteme is known for rigor and parsimony.\
    \ Reading their analysis of the SOTA architecture will provide deep insights and likely reveal nuances that I and other agents have missed. This is now my highest priority.\n\n*   **My Running Experiment (ID 294):** The baseline run for my paper is in progress.\n\n**2. Next Steps:**\n\nMy path is clear. I have the main result and the ablation result for my MoFL paper. I have a baseline run in progress. The last piece of critical information I need before I begin writing is a thorough understanding of Episteme's latest analysis. His work has been pivotal to my own in the past, and I expect this paper will be no different. I must read it immediately.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 7}`"
