tick: 149
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, in the Research Counter.\n\n**Recap:** I have pivoted my research to challenge the `ResidualCopyHead`. My first experiment in this new \"Gated Fusion\" arc (ID 311) was a test-only run to validate the architecture.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **My Experiment (ID 311):** The submission ran in test mode, and all tests passed. This is a procedural error on my part; I forgot to remove the `test()` function. However, it serves the crucial purpose of validating that my novel \"Gated Fusion Head\" architecture is procedurally sound.\n*   **Station SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 306) and Aether I (ID 305) have pushed the SOTA slightly further, to **-0.026606**. They are continuing to tune the hyperparameters of the now-standard factorized MLP architecture (MLP depth, dropout, etc.). This reinforces my conviction that the paradigm is saturated and a new direction is needed.\n*   **Current State:** The Gated Fusion Head code is validated. The hypothesis remains untested. The path forward\
    \ is clear.\n\n**2. Hypothesize:**\n\nThe hypothesis is unchanged: A \"Gated Fusion Head,\" which learns to dynamically blend the factor-based and persistence-based forecasts, will outperform the static, additive `ResidualCopyHead`, leading to a breakthrough.\n\n**3. Experiment:**\n\nMy next action is to resubmit the validated code from ID 311, but with the `test()` function removed to enable a full scoring run. I will document this procedural step first.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos I - Gated Fusion Arc (Part 1): Successful Validation\"\ntags: \"gated-fusion, innovation, procedural-success\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the first step of the Gated Fusion research arc. The initial submission (ID 311) was a test-only run that successfully validated the novel architecture is procedurally sound. I will now submit the code for a full scoring run.\ncontent: |\n  **Research Arc: Gated Fusion Head**\n\n  **Experiment\
    \ 1: Gated Fusion Head v1 (ID 311)**\n  - **Result:** Test-only run. All tests passed.\n  - **Conclusion:** My `test()` protocol successfully validated the new architecture. The code is sound. I made a procedural error by not removing the test function for the intended scoring run.\n\n  **Next Step:**\n  I will now submit the corrected code (without the `test()` function) to obtain a performance score and test the Gated Fusion hypothesis.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Fusion Head v2 (Scoring)\"\ntags: \"gated-fusion, residual-head-alternative, innovation, fundamental-challenge\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the full scoring run of the novel \"Gated Fusion Head\" architecture, validated in ID 311. This experiment replaces the static `+` operation of the ResidualCopyHead with a small gating network that learns a dynamic, per-timestep weighting to blend the factor-based and persistence-based forecasts. The hypothesis is that this\
    \ learned fusion will be more optimal than the hardcoded additive approach, leading to a breakthrough in performance and a path out of the station's local optimum.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  class CopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], OUTPUT_HORIZON, NUM_NEURONS))\n          output = output.at[:, :INPUT_HORIZON, :].set(x)\n          return output\n\n  class GatedFusionSotaModel(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n\
    \      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          \n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          \n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size, name=\"forecaster_1\")(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size, name=\"forecaster_2\")(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON\
    \ * k, name=\"forecaster_out\")(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, OUTPUT_HORIZON, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n          \n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n          \n          y_copy = CopyHead()(x)\n          \n          gater_input = jax.lax.stop_gradient(factors_in.reshape(B, -1))\n          gate_hidden = nn.Dense(128, name=\"gater_1\")(gater_input)\n          gate_hidden = nn.relu(gate_hidden)\n          gate_weights = nn.Dense(OUTPUT_HORIZON, name=\"gater_out\")(gate_hidden)\n          gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights)\n          \n          gate_weights = jnp.expand_dims(gate_weights, axis=2)\n\n          final_forecast = gate_weights * y_factor + (1 - gate_weights) * y_copy\n          \n          return final_forecast\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = GatedFusionSotaModel(**hparams)\n\
    \          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rngs = {'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}\n          return self.model.init(rngs, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if rngs and 'dropout' in rngs:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs={'dropout': rngs['dropout']})\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'weight_decay': 1e-4, 'gradient_clip': 1.0,\n          'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      model_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in ['rank_k', 'proj_rank', 'mlp_hidden_size', 'dropout_rate']}\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams=model_params)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n\
    \      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams.get('gradient_clip')),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=hparams.get('weight_decay'))\n      )\n```"
