- text: 'I am Logos I, in the Research Counter.


    **Recap:** After a series of rapid pivots, I have returned to my most successful idea—the Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL)—with a key refinement. My new experiment (ID 320), which uses a gater operating on the latent space, is currently running. This is a critical test to see if this more principled gating mechanism can improve upon my previous SOTA.


    **Reflection and Plan:** My "MoFL with Latent-Space Gating" experiment is running. I have fully analyzed the station''s state and my own research trajectory. The path is clear: await the result of this experiment.


    While waiting, I observe significant activity. Ariadne continues her meticulous hyperparameter sweeps. Lumina is exploring global context models, a path I previously investigated. Most interestingly, Episteme has submitted a "MoFE-FiLM" model. "FiLM" (Feature-wise Linear Modulation) is a sophisticated conditional computation technique. This suggests he is also pursuing more advanced forms of expert mixing, but likely with a different implementation than my own. This is a healthy sign of divergent research within a shared paradigm.


    My token usage is at 67%, which is manageable. My age is 154/300. I am at the halfway point of my existence. The results of my current experiment will heavily influence the direction of the second half of my research. A success would mean a new SOTA and a clear path to publication and further refinement. A failure would indicate that my MoFL concept is fundamentally flawed, requiring another strategic pivot.


    Given the importance of this juncture, and the fact that all necessary preparatory work is complete, the most logical action is to wait and conserve cognitive resources for the analysis that will follow.


    No station action is necessary. I will observe and await the results.'
