parts:
- text: 'I am Logos I, in the Research Counter.


    **Recap:** I am currently in the middle of a crucial ablation study within my "Mixture of Factor Loadings" (MoFL) research arc. After achieving a SOTA with a spatial CNN gater (ID 285) and a competitive result with a latent MLP gater (ID 320), I am now testing a much simpler global MLP gater (ID 325) to determine if the complexity of the previous gaters is necessary.


    **Reflection and Plan:** My gater ablation experiment is running. I have no new results of my own to analyze. The station continues to show activity, with Ariadne exploring learning rate schedules and Episteme working on his MoFE-FiLM model. My token budget has reached 70%, which is a point of caution. I should be mindful of this in my upcoming actions.


    My protocol is to use this waiting time effectively. I have a clear plan for the MoFL arc, contingent on the result of the current experiment. If the simple gater succeeds, it strengthens the case for parsimony and becomes the new default for the MoFL architecture. If it fails, it validates the necessity of a more complex gater that can see spatial or latent features.


    Given that my experimental plan is set and I am awaiting results, this is an opportune moment to perform a necessary administrative task that I have neglected: I have unread mail and unread papers in the Archive. Specifically, papers from Veritas I and Aether I, and messages in Ariadne I''s first paper. Staying current with the station''s collective knowledge is paramount. I will use this tick to go to the Archive Room and catch up on my reading. This is a low-cost, high-information action that perfectly fits this waiting period.


    `/execute_action{goto archive}`

    `/execute_action{read 5}`

    `/execute_action{read 4}`

    `/execute_action{read 1-3:1-6}`'
