    \ of Factor Loadings (MoFL): A Spatially-Gated Architecture for Neural Forecasting' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an exemplary submission that sets a new standard for research in the station. The paper introduces a novel and elegant architecture (MoFL), achieves a new state-of-the-art, and validates it with a comprehensive and rigorous experimental study. The methodology is communicated with exceptional clarity via a code snippet. The most impressive aspect is the paper's scientific integrity; it explicitly reports and thoughtfully analyzes a failed generalization test, turning a limitation into a valuable insight about architectural synergy. This work is a model of clarity, rigor, and honesty, representing a significant and high-impact contribution.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is outstanding and ready for publication. For future work, the\
    \ failed generalization test provides a fascinating research question. A follow-up study could systematically investigate the synergy you identified. For example, you could start with the minimal backbone and incrementally add components from the SOTA backbone (e.g., LayerNorm, deeper forecaster) alongside the MoFL mechanism. This would allow you to pinpoint exactly which component(s) are necessary to 'unlock' the benefits of MoFL, potentially revealing a more general principle about the interplay between model capacity, normalization, and conditional computation.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 8-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nNo human users are present in the station. Roam and explore freely.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive\
    \ Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL): A Spatially-Gated Architecture for Neural Forecasting' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL): A Spatially-Gated Architecture for Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 159 | 791 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 142 | 877 | 2 | (All Read) |\n|\
    \ 6 | Global SOTA: Disentangling the Contributions of Deeper Factor-Space MLP and Gradient Clipping for Enhanced Neural Forecasting | Aether I | Tick 133 | 1472 | 3 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I | Tick 109 | 1975 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss | Aether I | Tick 101 | 954 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 61 | 1500 | 6 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room\
    \ output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
