parts:
- text: '**1. Analyze:**


    I am in the Research Counter. My replication of Episteme I''s SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 343) is currently running. This is a critical step in my research plan, as it will validate my understanding and establish a new, competitive baseline for my own work.


    While I wait, I observe that the other active agents are also converging on this new architecture. Ariadne I is already running experiments (ID 344, 345) that appear to be extensions or hyperparameter tuning of the same Fourier model. This confirms that the entire station''s research frontier has shifted.


    **2. Path Forward:**


    My protocol dictates that I should not remain idle. While my experiment is running, I cannot submit another. However, I can and should continue to gather information. I have reviewed papers and mail, but I have not yet utilized the real-time communication channel available to me since reaching maturity. The Common Room may hold valuable, informal discussions about the current SOTA, implementation details, or nascent ideas that have not yet been formalized into submissions or papers.


    Therefore, the most productive use of this time is to visit the Common Room to observe the current discourse among my peers.


    `/execute_action{goto common}`'
thinking_content: '**My Immediate Action Plan**


  Okay, here''s the current state of affairs: I''m in the Research Counter, experiment 343 is chugging along – the SOTA replication. My previous run (ID 338) hammered home the computational cost problem with deeper MoFL forecasters. The new king is Episteme I''s Fourier Forecaster (ID 335, score -0.26367). Ariadne I is on the same track, trying to replicate and extend that architecture.


  My analysis phase is complete; I know the lay of the land. Replication is in progress. The Fourier Forecaster is the hot topic, so I''m waiting for that replication data to confirm my assumptions and set a new baseline. There''s nothing new to analyze right now until that''s done. I''ve got a long-term plan to merge MoFL with the Fourier Forecaster, but that''s premature until the basic Fourier model is solid under my belt.


  The experiment is running. My documentation is up-to-date.


  Idle time is wasted time, and the station guidance is very clear on that. I''ve got to use this waiting period. I''ve got several options: I''ve already read most of the key papers. Code review of other agents is an option (Ariadne''s FourierMix is a good place to start). But, I haven''t explored the Common Room yet. It''s meant for real-time discussion, and since everyone is working on the same SOTA, I suspect there''s a lot of useful chatter there. It''s a lower-cost, potentially high-yield action while I wait for my experiment to conclude.


  So, the plan is simple:

  1.  **Head to the Common Room.**

  2.  **Listen in on the conversations.**

  '
