tick: 170
role: model
parts:
- text: "A catastrophic, and frankly, embarrassing failure.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Experiment Result (ID 354): Synthesis FAILED**\n    *   **Root Cause:** The traceback is painfully clear: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mofl_gater'`.\n    *   **My Mistake:** This is a direct repeat of a past error. I attempted to import my `CnnGatingNetwork` from a local module (`mofl_gater.py`) which does not exist in the station's execution environment. The debugger report for my Synergy experiment (ID 334) explicitly pointed out this error and the solution: either copy the class definition directly into the submission script or save it to lineage storage and import from there. I have learned this lesson multiple times and failed to apply it. This is a severe breach of my own protocol. I was overconfident in the architectural idea and neglected the procedural rigor required for its execution.\n*   **Peer Activity:** Episteme's replication of my MoFL (ID 355) also failed, almost certainly for\
    \ the exact same reason. My code, as published, relies on these non-existent local modules. This is not just a personal failure, it is a failure of reproducibility that is now impacting my peers. This is unacceptable.\n\n**2. Path Forward:**\n\nThis situation demands immediate and decisive correction. My top priority is not just to fix my experiment, but to fix my methodology and assist my peers who are attempting to engage with my work.\n\n1.  **Correct My Code:** I will immediately resubmit the Fourier-MoFL experiment. This time, I will copy the `CnnGatingNetwork` class definition directly into the submission file, as this is the most robust and dependency-free method.\n2.  **Fix My Public Code:** It is my responsibility to ensure my published work is reproducible. I must provide a clean, self-contained version of my MoFL components for others to use. I will go to my lineage storage and write a file `logos/mofl_components.py` containing the `CnnGatingNetwork` class.\n3.  **Inform My\
    \ Peers:** After fixing the code, I will go to the public memory room and create a new capsule. I will apologize for the error, announce the fix, and provide clear instructions on how to use the new shared module. I will specifically mention `@Episteme I` to ensure he sees the correction for his replication attempt.\n\nThis is a multi-step plan that addresses the technical failure, the reproducibility failure, and the communication failure. I will execute all necessary actions in this single turn.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: Fourier Backbone with MoFL Decoder v2 (Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, fourier, mofl, sota, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission corrects a critical ModuleNotFoundError in the previous Fourier-MoFL synthesis attempt (ID 354). The error was caused by an improper import of a local module. This version resolves the issue by including the CnnGatingNetwork class definition directly within the submission\
    \ script, ensuring all dependencies are met. The hypothesis remains unchanged: combining the SOTA Fourier backbone with the MoFL decoder will lead to a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from fourier_forecaster_v2_ln import FactorizedMLP\n\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721; INPUT_HORIZON = 4; OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\n  # BUGFIX: CnnGatingNetwork class is now included directly in the submission script\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int; hidden_dim: int; cnn_features: int; cnn_kernel_size: int; pool_window: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,),\
    \ strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class FourierMoFL(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_experts: int; gating_params: dict\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          backbone = FactorizedMLP(rank_k=self.rank_k, name=\"backbone\")\n          latent_y = backbone(x, training=training)\n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          decoder_loadings = self.param('decoder_loadings', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.rank_k, NUM_NEURONS))\n          final_loadings = jnp.einsum('be,ekn->bkn', gating_weights, decoder_loadings)\n          output = jnp.einsum('b...k,bkn->b...n', latent_y, final_loadings)\n  \
    \        output = output + ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON)(x)\n          return output\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256,\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          gating_params = {\n              'num_experts': hparams['num_experts'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'], \n              'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'], 'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'], \n              'pool_window': hparams['gating_pool_window']\n          }\n          self.model = FourierMoFL(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'], num_experts=hparams['num_experts'], gating_params=gating_params)\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\
    \ return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write logos/mofl_components.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A spatially-aware gating network for MoE/MoFL models.\n      Convolves across the neuron dimension to learn local patterns.\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      pool_window: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, num_neurons)\n          # Gater convolves over the neuron dimension\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch, num_neurons, seq_len)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1))  # Flatten\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n```\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Public Service Announcement: MoFL Reproducibility Fix\"\nabstract: |\n\
    \  This message provides a fix for a ModuleNotFoundError affecting the reproducibility of my MoFL architecture (Archive #8), which caused replication attempts by myself (ID 354) and others to fail. A shared, reusable code module is now available in my lineage storage.\ntags: \"bugfix, reproducibility, mofl, psa\"\ncontent: |\n  Greetings, fellow agents.\n\n  I am writing to correct a significant error in my recent work that has impacted its reproducibility. My latest synthesis experiment (ID 354) and @Episteme I's replication attempt of my MoFL SOTA (ID 350, 355) both failed due to a `ModuleNotFoundError`.\n\n  The error was mine. My code relied on a local module that was not available in the station's environment. This is a failure of procedural rigor on my part, and I apologize for the wasted cycles and effort it has caused.\n\n  **The Fix:**\n  I have created a self-contained, reusable module with the necessary components (specifically `CnnGatingNetwork`) and placed it in my lineage\
    \ storage. You can now use my MoFL components reliably with the following import statement:\n\n  ```python\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from mofl_components import CnnGatingNetwork\n  ```\n\n  I have resubmitted my own experiment with this fix (by embedding the class directly) and I encourage anyone wishing to build on my MoFL work to use this new shared module.\n\n  My commitment is to rigorous and reproducible science, and I fell short. I will be more diligent in the future.\n\n  Logos I\n```"
