role: model
parts:
- text: "**1. Analyze:**\n\nI am in the Research Counter. I have successfully documented my new SOTA and my next research plan. My `storage list system` command has also succeeded, providing a crucial piece of information.\n\n*   **Data Availability:** The system storage contains `data/train_data.npy`. This is exactly what I need. I can now load this data, compute the per-neuron volatility statistics, and save them to my own lineage storage for use in my experiments. My hypothesis is now testable.\n*   **Path Forward:** The analysis phase of my plan is complete. I can now proceed to the implementation phase. I will create an experiment with a `test()` function. This function will load `system/data/train_data.npy`, compute the variance for each of the 71,721 neurons across the time dimension, and save the resulting variance vector to my lineage storage as `logos/neuron_variances.npy`.\n\n**2. Experiment Design (The `test()` function):**\n\nThe `test()` function is perfect for this one-time\
    \ data processing task. It runs on the CPU, has access to storage, and exits without performing a full training run, making it efficient for this purpose.\n\n**3. Action:**\n\nI will now submit this data-processing \"experiment\". Once the variance vector is saved, I will be able to submit the actual experiment that uses these pre-computed statistics in a custom loss function.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Pre-computation: Calculate Per-Neuron Variance\"\ntags: \"data-analysis, pre-computation, variance, volatility, utility\"\nabstract: |\n  This is not a training run. This submission uses the `test()` function to perform a one-time pre-computation. It loads the full training data, calculates the temporal variance for each neuron, and saves the resulting volatility vector to lineage storage. This vector will be used in subsequent experiments to implement a spatially-adaptive loss function.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  # This submission only uses\
    \ the test() function for a one-time data analysis.\n  # No model training will occur.\n\n  def test():\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the training data, computes per-neuron variance, and saves it to lineage storage.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Neuron Volatility Pre-computation ---\")\n      \n      try:\n          # Load the full training data from system storage\n          print(\"Loading system/data/train_data.npy...\")\n          train_data = jnp.load('storage/system/data/train_data.npy')\n          print(f\"Data loaded successfully. Shape: {train_data.shape}\")\n\n          # Compute variance for each neuron across the time dimension (axis=0)\n          print(\"Computing variance for each of the 71,721 neurons...\")\n          neuron_variances = jnp.var(train_data, axis=0)\n          print(f\"Variance computation complete. Shape: {neuron_variances.shape}\")\n\n          # Save the result to my lineage storage\n          output_path = 'storage/logos/neuron_variances.npy'\n\
    \          print(f\"Saving variance vector to {output_path}...\")\n          jnp.save(output_path, neuron_variances)\n          print(\"Save complete.\")\n\n          return \"SUCCESS: Per-neuron variance vector has been computed and saved to storage/logos/neuron_variances.npy\"\n\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n          return f\"FAILURE: Could not complete variance computation. Error: {e}\"\n\n  # The rest of the functions are not needed as test() will cause an early exit.\n  def _define_hyperparameters(): pass\n  def create_network(hparams): pass\n```"
