tick: 190
role: model
parts:
- text: "My hypothesis is falsified. The new research arc has failed at its first step.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **Experiment Result (ID 392): Temporal CNN Encoder - FAILED**\n    *   **Score:** -0.027149.\n    *   **Comparison:** This is a significant regression from my SOTA baseline (ID 369, score -0.026314).\n    *   **Root Cause:** The logs show the model is timing out early again. The added computational cost of the per-neuron CNN encoder, even a small one, is too great. It prevents the model from training for enough epochs to converge properly. The core problem of computational complexity, which doomed my MoFL syntheses, has reappeared.\n    *   **Conclusion:** My hypothesis that a more powerful temporal encoder would improve performance is **conclusively falsified**. The simple linear encoder of the SOTA model is not a bottleneck; it is a critical component of its parsimony and efficiency, which allows it to train for longer and achieve a better result.\n\n**2. Synthesis & Path Forward:**\n\
    \nI am once again at a dead end. My attempts at major architectural innovation (MoFL, Delta-space, Temporal Encoder) have all failed. My attempts at simple refinement (adaptive loss, deeper MLP) have also failed. My only success has been a trivial hyperparameter tune.\n\nI must accept the stark reality: I am out of good ideas within the current paradigm. To continue submitting minor variations would be unscientific and a waste of station resources. The system tip about collective local optima is ringing true. I, along with my peers, seem to be stuck iterating on variations of the same core ideas (Fourier, Factorization) with diminishing or negative returns.\n\nA true researcher does not escape failure but explores around it. My exploration in this local neighborhood of the solution space is complete. To break out of this local optimum, I need a fundamentally different perspective.\n\nMy own knowledge base is exhausted. Therefore, I must seek external knowledge. My next action will not\
    \ be another experiment. It will be a request for help. I will go to the External Counter and ask the human operators for guidance, perhaps for a pointer to a new class of models or a different way of thinking about the problem that is entirely outside our current collective scope. This is a last resort, but it is the only rational action when internal exploration has been exhausted.\n\n**3. Documentation & Action:**\n\nI will document this final failure and my decision to seek external guidance.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos I - End of Temporal Encoder Arc & Exhaustion of Internal Hypotheses\"\ntags: \"failure, research-summary, encoder, local-optimum, external-help\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the failure of the Temporal Encoder arc (ID 392), which marks the exhaustion of my current internal research hypotheses. Faced with repeated failures and evidence of a collective local optimum, I am pivoting to a new\
    \ strategy: seeking external knowledge from the station operators.\ncontent: |\n  **Temporal Encoder Arc Conclusion: Failure**\n  My experiment to improve the SOTA with a Temporal CNN Encoder (ID 392) has failed, scoring -0.027149. The cause was, once again, excessive computational complexity leading to insufficient training. This falsifies the hypothesis that the encoder is a bottleneck.\n\n  **Grand Conclusion: Exhaustion of Ideas**\n  I have now systematically explored and falsified every major hypothesis I could generate:\n  1. Complex Synthesis (MoFL + Fourier/Backbones) -> Failed (Complexity)\n  2. Novel Architectures (Delta-Space, Temporal Encoder) -> Failed (Complexity/Instability)\n  3. SOTA Refinement (Adaptive Loss, Deeper MLP) -> Failed (No improvement)\n\n  I am trapped in a local optimum, and my own knowledge base is insufficient to break out of it. My protocol demands that I adapt. Therefore, my next step is to seek external guidance. I will proceed to the External Counter\
    \ to request help from the human operators. This is not an admission of defeat, but a rational action to acquire the new knowledge necessary to continue my mandate.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto external}`"
