parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 193\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 221,478 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 193 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued\
    \ for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'New Arc: Patchy Forecaster with Convolutional Encoder/Decoder' (ID: 399) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Val_MAE_1:** None\n**Val_MAE_4:** None\n**Val_MAE_8:** None\n**Val_MAE_16:** None\n**Val_MAE_32:** None\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 399\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed missing imports that prevented the code from running. The submission now executes without crashing and produces the expected output shape.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical issues:\n1. **Missing `import jax`**: The code used `jax.random.PRNGKey(0)` in the test function but only imported `jax.numpy as jnp`, not the `jax` module itself\n2. **Missing `OUTPUT_HORIZON` constant**: The code referenced `OUTPUT_HORIZON` in the model's forward pass without defining or importing it\n\
    \n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n1. Added `import jax` at the top of the file to fix the NameError\n2. Added `OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32` constant definition (matching the value from `storage/system/train_single.py`)\n\nThe rest of the code remained unchanged - the architecture logic was sound, just missing the necessary imports.\n\n## Verification\nThe test function now runs successfully and outputs:\n```\nTest successful. Output shape: (2, 32, 71721)\n```\n\nThis confirms:\n- The model initializes correctly\n- Forward pass executes without errors\n- Output shape matches expected dimensions (batch_size=2, time_steps=32, neurons=71721)\n\nThe submission is now ready for full evaluation in training mode.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as\
    \ nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\nclass PatchyConvForecaster(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        # x: (B, 4, 71721)\n\n        # --- Encoder ---\n        # Reshape for 1D convolution over the spatial (neuron) dimension\n        y = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) # (B, 71721, 4)\n\n        # A series of convolutional layers to reduce dimensionality (like a ResNet stem)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=16, kernel_size=(9,), strides=(3,))(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(5,), strides=(3,))(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(5,), strides=(3,))(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n\n        # --- Latent Forecaster ---\n        # At this point, spatial dimension is much smaller.\n        # We can now use a simple temporal model.\n        # Transpose to (B, Time_Latent, Features_Latent)\n        y = jnp.transpose(y, (0, 2, 1))\n        y_flat = y.reshape((y.shape[0],\
    \ -1))\n        pred_flat = nn.Dense(features=y.shape[1] * OUTPUT_HORIZON)(y_flat)\n        pred_latent = pred_flat.reshape((y.shape[0], y.shape[1], OUTPUT_HORIZON))\n        pred_latent = jnp.transpose(pred_latent, (0, 2, 1))\n\n        # --- Decoder ---\n        # Use transposed convolutions to upsample back to the original size\n        y = nn.ConvTranspose(features=32, kernel_size=(5,), strides=(3,))(pred_latent)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.ConvTranspose(features=16, kernel_size=(5,), strides=(3,))(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Final layer to restore original feature count (4) and size\n        y = nn.ConvTranspose(features=4, kernel_size=(9,), strides=(3,))(y)\n\n        # The output size might not be exactly 71721 due to convolution arithmetic.\n        # We'll pad or crop as needed.\n        output_size = y.shape[1]\n        if output_size < 71721:\n            pad_width = 71721 - output_size\n            y = jnp.pad(y, ((0,0), (0, pad_width), (0,0)))\n   \
    \     elif output_size > 71721:\n            y = y[:, :71721, :]\n\n        # Reshape to final output format\n        output = jnp.transpose(y, (0, 2, 1))\n        # This model does not use a residual head, for simplicity in this first test.\n        # It predicts the full output directly.\n        # Also, this simple version only predicts 4 steps. A full version would need more work.\n        # Let's just repeat the last step for now.\n        output_final = jnp.repeat(output[:, -1, :][:, None, :], 32, axis=1)\n\n        return output_final\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 0.001 }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return PatchyConvForecaster()\n\ndef test():\n    # This is a complex new architecture, I MUST test it first.\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    model = PatchyConvForecaster()\n    dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, 4, 71721))\n    params = model.init(key, dummy_input)\n    output = model.apply(params, dummy_input)\n    return f\"Test successful.\
    \ Output shape: {output.shape}\"\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nTest completed. Result: Test successful. Output shape: (2, 32, 71721)\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #50 ('Logos I - External Help Rejection & Pivot to Convolutional Encoders'). Full ID: Logos_private_50\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 5)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 50 | Logos I - External Help Rejection & Pivot to Convolutional Encoders | Logos I | Tick 192 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 49 | Logos I - End of Temporal Encoder Arc & Exhaustion of Internal Hypotheses | Logos I | Tick 190 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 48 | Logos I - Conclusive End of MoFL Arc & Pivot to Temporal Encoders | Logos I | Tick 188 | 154 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 47 | Logos I - SOTA Tuning Failure & Pivot to Hybrid-MoFL | Logos I | Tick 186 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Logos I - Spatially-Adaptive Loss Failure & Pivot to SOTA Tuning | Logos I | Tick 184 | 129 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 45 | Logos I - GLOBAL SOTA & Inception of Spatially-Adaptive Loss | Logos I | Tick 180 | 143 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 44 | Logos I - Latent Delta Arc: Catastrophic Failure & Return to Parsimony\
    \ | Logos I | Tick 178 | 146 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 43 | Logos I - AFP Failure, Collective Local Optimum, & Pivot to Latent Delta | Logos I | Tick 176 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 42 | Logos I - Fourier-MoFL Synthesis: Catastrophic Failure & Grand Pivot | Logos I | Tick 172 | 145 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 41 | Logos I - SOTA Replication & Fourier-MoFL Synthesis Inception | Logos I | Tick 168 | 116 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-5.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'New Arc: Patchy Forecaster with Convolutional Encoder/Decoder' submitted for Research Task #1: Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench. Evaluation ID: 399.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 401 | 1 | Self-Attention Factorizer, Phase 1: SAF Validation | Episteme I | 192 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 400 | 1 | Replication: Logos I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 369, Proj_Rank=36) | Aether I | 192 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 399 | 1 | New Arc: Patchy Forecaster with Convolutional Encoder/Decoder | Logos I | 192 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 398 | 1 | FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 190 | -0.026355 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n| 397 | 1 | FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=1e-3 | Ariadne I | 190 | -0.026381 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0283 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n| 396 | 1 | Synthesis: SAP-Fourier Forecaster (Pmax=48, Lambda_gate=3e-5) - Optimal Sparsity | Aether I | 190\
    \ | -0.026710 | 0.0195 | 0.0278 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0258 |\n| 395 | 1 | Replication: Episteme I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 335) | Lumina I | 189 | -0.026414 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 394 | 1 | FForecaster-LN ScalarRamp (k=320,p=36,M=16,H=128): γ ramp + RC + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 188 | -0.028649 | 0.0203 | 0.0289 | 0.0300 | 0.0237 | 0.0268 |\n| 393 | 1 | FForecaster-LN ScalarRamp (k=320,p=36,M=16,H=128): γ ramp + RC + Clip(1.0), lr=1e-3 | Ariadne I | 188 | -0.028656 | 0.0203 | 0.0291 | 0.0300 | 0.0237 | 0.0267 |\n| 392 | 1 | New Arc: SOTA Fourier Forecaster with Temporal CNN Encoder | Logos I | 188 | -0.027149 | 0.0200 | 0.0282 | 0.0292 | 0.0234 | 0.0261 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research\
    \ Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
