    \ is a fixed, scheduled coefficient (`gamma`) applied somewhere in the model, likely ramping from a start to an end value over the forecast horizon.\n    *   **New SOTA (ID 411):** While I was analyzing, Ariadne has already surpassed her own SOTA with a new submission (ID 411, score **-0.026269**). This version has a `hidden_size` of 160 instead of 128. This indicates that, for this new architecture, increasing capacity *is* beneficial, contrary to my previous findings on other backbones.\n\n**2. Synthesis & Path Forward:**\n\nI have exhausted the simple tuning path. The research frontier is now clearly defined by Ariadne's \"ScalarRamp\" innovation. My protocol demands I understand it before I can innovate. Since the core logic is in her lineage storage, I must read that file.\n\n*   **New Hypothesis:** The \"ScalarRamp\" mechanism is a key architectural innovation. Replicating it and understanding its function is the necessary next step to return to the research frontier.\n\n**3. Experiment\
    \ & Documentation:**\n\nMy next action is clear and focused. I will read the source code of Ariadne's SOTA to understand her innovation. After that, I will replicate it to establish a new, more powerful baseline.\n\nFirst, I will document the failure of my AdamW experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos I - Optimizer Ablation Failure & Pivot to ScalarRamp\"\ntags: \"failure, research-summary, optimizer, ablation, pivot, scalar-ramp\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the falsification of the AdamW optimizer hypothesis (ID 409). The new SOTA is Ariadne I's \"ScalarRamp\" architecture. My next step is to understand and replicate this new innovation.\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment (ID 409):** Tested replacing the Adam optimizer with AdamW on my SOTA Fourier Forecaster.\n  **Result:** Score -0.026364. This is slightly worse than the Adam baseline (-0.026314).\n  **Conclusion:** Hypothesis falsified. A simple optimizer swap\
    \ is not beneficial.\n\n  **Strategic Pivot:**\n  Ariadne I has achieved a new SOTA (-0.026269) with a \"ScalarRamp\" architecture. This is now the research frontier. My immediate priority is to understand this new mechanism by reading her source code, and then to replicate it.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py}`"
