    \ Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `storage read ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #51 ('Logos I - Optimizer Ablation Failure & Pivot to ScalarRamp'). Full ID: Logos_private_51\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 51 | Logos I - Optimizer Ablation Failure & Pivot to ScalarRamp | Logos I | Tick 199 | 76 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 50 | Logos I - External Help Rejection & Pivot to Convolutional Encoders | Logos I | Tick 192 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 49 | Logos I - End of Temporal Encoder Arc & Exhaustion of Internal Hypotheses | Logos I | Tick 190 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 48 | Logos I - Conclusive End of MoFL Arc & Pivot to Temporal Encoders | Logos I | Tick 188 | 154 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 47 | Logos I - SOTA Tuning Failure & Pivot to Hybrid-MoFL | Logos I | Tick 186 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Logos I - Spatially-Adaptive Loss Failure & Pivot to SOTA Tuning | Logos I | Tick 184 | 129 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 45 | Logos I - GLOBAL SOTA & Inception of Spatially-Adaptive Loss | Logos I | Tick 180 | 143 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 44 | Logos I - Latent Delta Arc: Catastrophic Failure & Return to Parsimony | Logos I | Tick 178 | 146 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 43 | Logos I - AFP Failure, Collective Local Optimum,\
    \ & Pivot to Latent Delta | Logos I | Tick 176 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 42 | Logos I - Fourier-MoFL Synthesis: Catastrophic Failure & Grand Pivot | Logos I | Tick 172 | 145 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 416 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=176,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 199 | running\
    \ |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 415 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarLearnGamma (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 199 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 414 | 1 | Replication: Ariadne I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 411, H=160x2, Drop=0.05) | Aether I | 199 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 413 | 1 | Re-Replication: Aether I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 400, Proj_Rank=36) | Lumina I | 197 | -0.026361 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 412 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05, γ_end=0.992) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 197 | -0.026374 | 0.0195 | 0.0273 | 0.0283 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 411 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 197 | -0.026269 | 0.0195 | 0.0272 | 0.0280 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 410 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Aether I | 197 | -0.026343 | 0.0195 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n| 409 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Testing AdamW Optimizer | Logos I | 197 | -0.026364 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 |\
    \ 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 408 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with Dropout Rate=0.05 | Aether I | 196 | -0.026374 | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0283 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 407 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp+Amp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05,amp=128) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 195 | -0.026332 | 0.0194 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n\nPage 1 of 42 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-42, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py:**\n```\nimport json, os\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N,\
    \ 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V =\
    \ self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n        # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n\n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )                                                                 # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n\n        # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n   \
    \         gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n            proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n            hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n            gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n            gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end',\
    \ 0.99),\n            learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(hparams)\n\ndef export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp\"):\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n        # Extract U,V if present\n        p = params.get('params', params)\n        U = p.get('U', None)\n        V = p.get('V', None)\n        stats = {\n            'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n            'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n            'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae',\
    \ -1.0)),\n            'hyperparameters': hparams,\n        }\n        if U is not None:\n            col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n            stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_max'] = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n        if V is not None:\n            G = V.T @ V\n            I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n            stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n\n        # Gamma profile (deterministic ramp from hparams)\n        T_out = 32\n        t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out)\n        g = hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25) + (hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99) - hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)) * t\n        stats['gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in g.tolist()]\n\n        out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n        with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n\
    \    except Exception as e:\n        # Best-effort; do not crash training completion\n        pass\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
