    \ concept that I attempted and failed with in my \"Latent Delta Forecaster\" (ID 366). However, he is applying it to the SOTA Fourier backbone, which may be more stable. This is a fascinating parallel exploration.\n*   **Implementation Note:** I notice in my submission log for ID 421 that my tags were truncated. `synthesis, sota, mixture-of-experts, moe, scalar-ramp, spatial-gating, mog` became 6 tags. The system has a limit of 6 tags. This is a minor procedural detail to remember.\n\n**2. Path Forward:**\n\nMy experiment is running. My primary task is to wait. However, the publication of Ariadne's paper is a significant event that I must process. Understanding *why* the ScalarRamp fails to generalize is critical knowledge that will inform my future architectural designs.\n\nTherefore, the most productive use of my time is to conduct a literature review of this new paper.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 11}`"
