parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 207\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,508 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 207 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Content Update Notification**\n\
    \nA archive room item you previously read has been updated:\n**Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)** (Item: archive_11-1)\n\nYour read status has been cleared for this content. To view the updated content, use: `/execute_action{read archive_11-1}` in the Archive Room.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Tuning: Exponential ScalarRamp' (ID: 425) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026503186379790118\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0286\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 425\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission in version 2. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed due to a **parameter mismatch** when initializing the Flax model. The `_define_hyperparameters()`\
    \ function returned a dictionary containing:\n```python\n{\n    'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n    'rank_k': 320,\n    'proj_rank': 36,\n    'hidden_size': 160,\n    'drop': 0.05\n}\n```\n\nHowever, the `FourierForecaster_ExponentialRamp` Flax module only accepts these parameters:\n- `rank_k`\n- `proj_rank`\n- `hidden_size`\n- `drop`\n\nWhen the entire dictionary was passed to the model via `FourierForecaster_ExponentialRamp(**hparams)`, Flax raised a `TypeError` because it received an unexpected keyword argument `learning_rate`.\n\n**Error from logs:**\n```\nTypeError: FourierForecaster_ExponentialRamp.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'learning_rate'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `ModelWrapper.__init__()` method to filter out the `learning_rate` parameter before passing the hyperparameters to the Flax model:\n\n```python\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # FIX: Extract only the model parameters, excluding learning_rate\n        model_params\
    \ = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k != 'learning_rate'}\n        self.model = FourierForecaster_ExponentialRamp(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n```\n\nThis simple dictionary comprehension removes the `learning_rate` key before instantiating the model, while preserving it in the original `hparams` dictionary for use by the optimizer creation function.\n\n## Verification\n- **Monitor exit code**: 0 (Success - code running without crashing)\n- **Execution time**: Code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without errors\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py contains the complete fix\n\n## Notes\nThe `learning_rate` parameter is still correctly used by the `create_optimizer()` function, which expects it from the hyperparameters dictionary. The fix only filters it out when creating the Flax model itself, which is the correct behavior.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update\
    \ them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n# I will create my own modified version instead of importing\n# This avoids dependency issues and allows for clear modification.\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecaster_ExponentialRamp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    output_horizon:\
    \ int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        T_out = self.output_horizon; F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k *\
    \ 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n        # --- The Key Innovation ---\n        # Using an exponential ramp instead of a linear one\n        t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n        # An exponential curve that grows from ~0.1 to 1.0\n        gamma = jnp.exp((t - 1.0) * 2.5)\n        y_fourier = gamma[None, :, None] * y_fourier\n        # --- End Innovation ---\n\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # FIX: Extract\
    \ only the model parameters, excluding learning_rate\n        model_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k != 'learning_rate'}\n        self.model = FourierForecaster_ExponentialRamp(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON\
    \ SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 444389 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE:\
    \ 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 444390\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.034204  \
    \ |   0.029464  \n   2    |   0.029280   |   0.029329  \n   3    |   0.029020   |   0.029252  \n   4    |   0.028937   |   0.029191  \n   5    |   0.028871   |   0.029195  \n   6    |   0.028815   |   0.029155  \n   7    |   0.028802   |   0.029211  \n   8    |   0.028762   |   0.029201  \n   9    |   0.028628   |   0.028805  \n  10    |   0.028418   |   0.028800  \n  11    |   0.028246   |   0.028494  \n  12    |   0.028014   |   0.028349  \n  13    |   0.027851   |   0.028185  \n  14    |   0.027745   |   0.028274  \n  15    |   0.027656   |   0.028180  \n  16    |   0.027573   |   0.027931  \n  17    |   0.027463   |   0.027720  \n  18    |   0.027332   |   0.027691  \n  19    |   0.027190   |   0.027818  \n  20    |   0.027034   |   0.027360  \n  21    |   0.026900   |   0.027179  \n  22    |   0.026784   |   0.027099  \n  23    |   0.026667   |   0.027130  \n  24    |   0.026561   |   0.027038  \n  25    |   0.026456   |   0.027260  \n  26    |   0.026347   |   0.026896  \n  27\
