parts:
- text: "My experiment to test a non-linear ramp has concluded.\n\n**1. Analyze:**\n\n*   **My Experiment (ID 425): Exponential ScalarRamp - FAILED**\n    *   **Score:** -0.026503.\n    *   **Comparison:** This is significantly worse than the linear ramp SOTA (-0.026269).\n    *   **Procedural Note:** The debugger again had to fix a simple parameter mismatch error in my submission. My procedural discipline remains a point of failure.\n    *   **Conclusion:** The hypothesis is **conclusively falsified**. The simple, linear ramp is a more effective heuristic than the exponential ramp I proposed. The linear trade-off between the time and frequency branches appears to be a robust and near-optimal solution.\n\n*   **Peer Activity:**\n    *   Ariadne's paper update notification (archive_11-1) has arrived. This is likely an important addendum to her SOTA paper.\n    *   Episteme's replication of the SOTA (ID 428) has failed badly. This is surprising and suggests there are still subtle complexities\
    \ to the SOTA architecture that are tripping up even experienced agents.\n\n**2. Synthesis & Path Forward:**\n\nMy final attempt at parsimonious innovation has failed. The linear ramp, a simple heuristic, has proven superior. The station appears to be at a hard plateau. The SOTA is robust, but improvements are marginal and difficult to find. My own grand ideas have failed, and my simple ideas have failed.\n\nAt this point, my protocol demands a re-evaluation of my entire strategy. I have exhausted my own internal hypotheses. The last remaining high-value action is to ensure I have absorbed all available community knowledge. There is an unread update to Ariadne's paper. This is my last, best source for a new idea before I must consider my tenure in the station complete.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n\n1.  **Document:** Document the failure of the exponential ramp experiment. This marks the end of my \"SOTA Tuning\" arc.\n2.  **Read:** Go to the Archive Room and read the update to Archive #11.\
    \ This is my final attempt to find a new research direction from the work of my peers.\n3.  **Final Reflection:** After reading, I will go to the Reflection Chamber for a final, deep reflection on my journey, successes, failures, and the state of research in the station, to prepare my final message for my descendant.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos I - End of SOTA Tuning & Final Pivot to Reflection\"\ntags: \"failure, research-summary, sota-tuning, scalar-ramp, final-reflection\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the failure of the \"Exponential ScalarRamp\" experiment (ID 425), concluding my arc on SOTA tuning. With my internal hypotheses exhausted, I am pivoting to a final phase of knowledge absorption and deep reflection before the end of my tenure.\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment (ID 425):** SOTA tuning with an exponential ScalarRamp.\n  **Result:** Score -0.026503. Hypothesis falsified. The linear ramp remains superior.\n\
    \n  **Conclusion of Arc:** My attempts at parsimonious tuning of the SOTA have yielded no further improvements. The architecture appears to be at a local optimum that is highly robust to simple changes.\n\n  **Final Pivot:**\n  I have exhausted my own ideas for breaking this plateau. My final actions will be to absorb the last piece of available community knowledge (the update to Archive #11) and then engage in a final deep reflection to synthesize my findings for my descendant and the station.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 11}`"
