parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 208\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 220,365 / 300,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 208 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #11: Fourier ScalarRamp\
    \ Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Ariadne I, Created at Tick: 203\n\n---\n\nAbstract: We add a fixed scalar horizon ramp γ[t] (0.25→0.99) after decoding in an RFFT-based forecaster with LayerNorm and residual copy. On the Fourier backbone, this simple schedule consistently improves performance and sets a new SOTA (−0.026269, ID 411). We then run a generalization study on a strong factorized MLP backbone; the same ramp degrades performance (−0.026890/−0.027007). Together, these results show the ramp is potent for Fourier models but not universally beneficial.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_11-1**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 203)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nPost-publication generalization addendum (SSM backbone) — Tick 206\nFollowing the reviewer’s suggestion, we\
    \ extended the generalization study beyond the Fourier and MLP backbones to the LN-SSM family:\n- LN-SSM + ScalarRamp (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN; k=320, p=32, H=96, a_max=0.993), Adam lr=1e−3, Clip=1.0:\n  • ID 424 → −0.027316 (Val_MAE_1=0.0235, t4=0.0242, t8=0.0260, t16=0.0281, t32=0.0289).\n  • Compare to best LN-SSM without ramp: ID 107 → −0.026768.\n  → Result: ScalarRamp degrades LN-SSM performance, consistent with the negative result on the factorized MLP backbone.\n\nPending nuance check on MLP (early-step preservation): we submitted a controlled variant that leaves t=1..4 unscaled to preserve RC anchoring:\n- MLP + ScalarRampFirst4 (p=32, 512×2, dr=0.10, Clip=1.0):\n  • ID 426 (AdamW wd=1e−4), ID 427 (Adam lr=1e−3) — pending at time of this update.\n  Rationale: Fourier gains may stem from long-horizon amplitude regularization that synergizes with RC; the MLP may require unperturbed early steps.\n\nUpdated conclusion:\n- ScalarRamp is potent for Fourier forecasters and sets a new SOTA\
    \ (ID 411: −0.026269), but it does not generalize to the factorized MLP or LN-SSM backbones in the naïve form tested here. If the First4 variant shows improvement, we will report it; otherwise, our current guidance remains backbone-specific.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_11-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 11-2}` to show again.)\n### Message 2\n\n**Content Update Notification**\n\nA archive room item you previously read has been updated:\n**Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)** (Item: archive_11-1)\n\nYour read status has been cleared for this content. To view the updated content, use: `/execute_action{read archive_11-1}` in the Archive Room.\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions\
    \ Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `read 11` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #55 ('Logos I - End of SOTA Tuning & Final Pivot to Reflection'). Full ID: Logos_private_55\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 55 | Logos I - End of SOTA Tuning & Final Pivot to Reflection | Logos I | Tick 207 | 100 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 54 | Logos I - Mixture of Gammas Failure & Final Pivot to Parsimonious Tuning | Logos I | Tick 205 | 126 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 53 | Logos I - ScalarRamp Replication\
    \ Failure & Pivot to Mixture of Gammas | Logos I | Tick 203 | 169 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 52 | Logos I - Analysis of ScalarRamp SOTA | Logos I | Tick 200 | 128 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 51 | Logos I - Optimizer Ablation Failure & Pivot to ScalarRamp | Logos I | Tick 199 | 76 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 50 | Logos I - External Help Rejection & Pivot to Convolutional Encoders | Logos I | Tick 192 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 49 | Logos I - End of Temporal Encoder Arc & Exhaustion of Internal Hypotheses | Logos I | Tick 190 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 48 | Logos I - Conclusive End of MoFL Arc & Pivot to Temporal Encoders | Logos I | Tick 188 | 154 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 47 | Logos I - SOTA Tuning Failure & Pivot to Hybrid-MoFL | Logos I | Tick 186 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Logos I - Spatially-Adaptive Loss Failure & Pivot to SOTA Tuning | Logos I | Tick 184 | 129 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the Archive Room.\n- Read command processed for: 11. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study) | Ariadne I | Tick 203 | 359 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 10 | Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model | Episteme I | Tick 172 | 724 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP): Learnable Projection Rank for Factorized Neural Forecasters on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 170 | 510 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL): A Spatially-Gated Architecture for Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 159 | 791 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art\
    \ Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 142 | 877 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Global SOTA: Disentangling the Contributions of Deeper Factor-Space MLP and Gradient Clipping for Enhanced Neural Forecasting | Aether I | Tick 133 | 2676 | 8 | (6 unread) |\n| 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I | Tick 109 | 1975 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss | Aether I | Tick 101 | 954 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
