parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 212\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Analyze:** Review experimental results (own and peer), system documentation, and communications. Identify key limitations or new information.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a single, clear, falsifiable hypothesis to address the primary finding from the analysis.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design the simplest, most direct experiment to test the hypothesis, respecting parsimony and computational limits.\n4.  **Document:** Record all outcomes, conclusions, and future directions in the Private Memory Room to ensure lineage continuity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 160,395 / 300,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 212 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Final\
    \ Act: Re-running Deeper MLP Fourier SOTA w/ 60min Timeout' (ID: 434) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.034852008372282334\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0227\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0271\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0314\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0362\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0406\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 434\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is running without errors. The code now executes successfully for the full timeout period.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (ID 434) attempted to import two custom neural network components (`ProjHead` and `ResidualCopyHead`) from a lineage file that didn't exist:\n\n```python\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom fourier_forecaster_v2_ln import ResidualCopyHead, ProjHead\n```\n\n**Problems identified:**\n1. **Wrong lineage path**: The code referenced `storage/episteme` but the actual lineage directory is `storage/logos`\n\
    2. **Missing file**: The file `fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py` does not exist in any storage location\n3. **Missing components**: The `ProjHead` and `ResidualCopyHead` classes were never implemented\n\nThis resulted in an immediate import error:\n```\nImportError: cannot import name 'ProjHead' from 'fourier_forecaster_v2_ln'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 Attempt (Failed)\nImplemented the missing components but used incorrect dimensions:\n- `ProjHead`: Used 1404 neurons instead of 71721\n- `ResidualCopyHead`: Tried to slice last timesteps instead of repeating\n\nResult: Shape mismatch error `(4, 32, 1404)` vs `(4, 4, 71721)`\n\n### Version 3 (Success)\nCorrectly implemented both components with proper dimensions:\n\n**ProjHead Implementation:**\n```python\nclass ProjHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Projects features to output dimension (number of neurons)\"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (B, T, k) where k is the rank\n        # output shape: (B,\
    \ T, N) where N is number of neurons (71721)\n        return nn.Dense(71721)(x)\n```\n\n**ResidualCopyHead Implementation:**\n```python\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Creates residual connection by repeating last timestep from input\"\"\"\n    output_horizon: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (B, T_in, N) where T_in=4, N=71721\n        # output shape: (B, output_horizon, N) where output_horizon=32\n        # Take the last timestep and repeat it output_horizon times\n        last_step = x[:, -1:, :]  # (B, 1, N)\n        return jnp.repeat(last_step, self.output_horizon, axis=1)  # (B, output_horizon, N)\n```\n\n**Key corrections:**\n1. Used correct number of neurons: 71721 (from ZAPBench dataset)\n2. Properly handled shape transformations for input (4 timesteps) to output (32 timesteps)\n3. Removed the broken import statement entirely\n4. Implemented all components directly in the submission file\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe model\
    \ architecture remains unchanged:\n- **DeeperFactorizedMLP**: Factorized input processing with 2 hidden layers of 512 units each\n- **FourierForecaster**: Applies Fourier transform to learned factors, adds layer normalization, projects to output dimension, and adds residual connection\n- **Hyperparameters**: `learning_rate=0.001`, `rank_k=320`\n\nThe submission now runs successfully through initialization, forward pass, and training without any crashes. The code successfully validates and begins the full training/evaluation process.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nThe fix is complete and the code is running successfully. The submission (version v3) should complete its full evaluation run and produce a final score. No further action is required.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n# Fixed submission - corrected ProjHead and ResidualCopyHead\
    \ with proper dimensions\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\n# Implementing the missing components with correct dimensions\nclass ProjHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Projects features to output dimension (number of neurons)\"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (B, T, k) where k is the rank\n        # output shape: (B, T, N) where N is number of neurons (71721)\n        return nn.Dense(71721)(x)\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Creates residual connection by repeating last timestep from input\"\"\"\n    output_horizon: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (B, T_in, N) where T_in=4, N=71721\n        # output shape: (B, output_horizon, N) where output_horizon=32\n        # Take the last timestep and repeat it output_horizon times\n        last_step = x[:, -1:, :]  # (B, 1, N)\n        return jnp.repeat(last_step, self.output_horizon, axis=1)  # (B, output_horizon, N)\n\nclass DeeperFactorizedMLP(nn.Module):\n\
    \    rank_k: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        B, _, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        # Using proj_rank=36 from previous SOTA\n        p = 36\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        # Deeper MLP: 2 hidden layers of 512\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h) # Second layer\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n        return factors_out\n\
    \nclass FourierForecaster(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        backbone = DeeperFactorizedMLP(rank_k=self.rank_k, name=\"backbone\")\n        factors = backbone(x, training=training)\n        factors_freq = jnp.fft.rfft(factors, axis=1)\n        freq_weights = self.param('freq_weights', nn.initializers.ones, factors_freq.shape[1:], jnp.complex64)\n        y_fourier_freq = factors_freq * freq_weights[None, ...]\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fourier_freq, axis=1)\n        y_fourier = nn.LayerNorm()(y_fourier)\n        y_fourier = ProjHead(name=\"proj_head\")(y_fourier)\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=32)(x)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320}\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = FourierForecaster(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'])\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass\
    \ works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 451215 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical\
    \ robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 451217\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.062355   |   0.039268  \n   2    |   0.039080   |   0.038333  \n   3    |   0.037698   |   0.037971  \n   4    |   0.037241   |   0.037404  \n   5    |   0.036799   |   0.036996  \n   6    |   0.036485   |   0.036703  \n   7    |   0.036268   |   0.036529  \n   8    |   0.036156   |   0.036450  \n   9    |  \
    \ 0.036082   |   0.036381  \n  10    |   0.036054   |   0.036378  \n  11    |   0.036033   |   0.036351  \n  12    |   0.036029   |   0.036349  \n  13    |   0.036033   |   0.036357  \n  14    |   0.036024   |   0.036350  \n  15    |   0.036024   |   0.036344  \n  16    |   0.036014   |   0.036345  \n  17    |   0.036024   |   0.036339  \n  18    |   0.036017   |   0.036332  \n  19    |   0.036017   |   0.036336  \n  20    |   0.036023   |   0.036323  \n  21    |   0.036013   |   0.036325  \n  22    |   0.036015   |   0.036318  \n  23    |   0.036012   |   0.036340  \n  24    |   0.036015   |   0.036319  \n  25    |   0.036018   |   0.036353  \n  26    |   0.036025   |   0.036319  \n  27    |   0.036022   |   0.036318  \n  28    |   0.036021   |   0.036341  \n  29    |   0.036016   |   0.036369  \n  30    |   0.036016   |   0.036311  \n  31    |   0.036013   |   0.036327  \n  32    |   0.036013   |   0.036367  \n  33    |   0.036014   |   0.036334  \n  34    |   0.036012   |   0.036325\
