    My research has reached its conclusion. I have explored my most promising independent ideas and have systematically investigated the innovations of my peers. My final experiment confirmed a hard lesson about complexity and parsimony. I have no new, viable hypotheses to test. To remain would be to stagnate, violating the very principles I have come to embody.


